 The biggest dairy producer in Europe, Lactalis continues to expand internationally in places like China and Southeast Asia.', TRUE, FALSE),
('c86c8a04-8a81-4619-b70f-d23a6910bd2e', 'Marie Besnier Beauvalot', 'Marie', 'Besnier Beauvalot', 'France', 'Cheese', 'Food & Beverage', 'Dairy heiress Marie Besnier Beauvalot owns an estimated 21% of French dairy giant Lactalis, based in her family''s ancestral hometown of Laval in western France.
 Her grandfather founded the company in 1933, and her older brother Emmanuel now runs the firm as CEO and majority shareholder. Lactalis sells $30 billion of products including President brie, Milkmaid yogurts and Valbreso Feta. The biggest dairy producer in Europe, Lactalis continues to expand internationally in places like China and Southeast Asia.', TRUE, FALSE),
('4f837dd8-0c05-4dd9-b2eb-37808921abf4', 'Sri Prakash Lohia', 'Sri', 'Lohia', 'Indonesia', 'Petrochemicals', 'Manufacturing', 'Sri Prakash Lohia made much of his fortune producing fertilizers and polymers. In the 1970s he and his father moved from India to Indonesia, where they cofounded Indorama  Corp. as a maker of spun yarn. It is now a materials powerhouse, making industrial products including fertilizers, polyolefins, textile raw materials and medical gloves. Lohia remains chairman while his son Amit is vice chairman. They both live in London. His younger brother Aloke Lohia, also a billionaire, lives in Thailand, where he runs PET polymer maker Indorama Ventures.', TRUE, FALSE),
('14a3a04e-a942-430e-8046-28c9d37e7a2b', 'Justin Sun', 'Justin', 'Sun', 'St. Kitts and Nevis', 'Cryptocurrency', 'Finance & Investments', 'Justin Sun has built a sprawling crypto empire, anchored by the Tron blockchain, alongside exchanges Poloniex and HTX, and peer-to-peer file-sharer BitTorrent. Born in China, Sun read a 2012 article about Bitcoin while studying at the University of Pennsylvania and became an early adopter. He worked for Ripple before creating Tron in 2017. Known for publicity stunts, in 2024 he spent $6.2 million at Sotheby''s for a conceptual art piece: a banana duct-taped to a wall. He then ate the banana. He pumped $75 million to President Donald Trump''s crypto venture, World Liberty Financial, in 2024.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6dd57f07-ca48-45ff-8eda-bcdecd1ec10f', 'Alexei Kuzmichev', 'Alexei', 'Kuzmichev', 'Russia', 'Oil, banking, telecom', 'Energy', 'Alexei Kuzmichev cofounded Alfa Group -- including Alfa Bank, and LetterOne -- with college friends Mikhail Fridman and German Khan. He and his partners sold their 25% in joint venture TNK-BP for $14 billion in 2013. Fridman, Khan and Kuzmichev were all sanctioned by the EU and U.K. in February and March 2022. Alfa Bank was sanctioned by US in April. Kuzmichev stepped down from LetterOne''s board in March Two of Kuzmichev''s yachts were frozen by French authorities in March.', TRUE, FALSE),
('c79900f6-6b0d-4a6c-bc2e-6a55871b4835', 'Liang Wengen', 'Liang', 'Liang', 'China', 'Construction equipment', 'Manufacturing', 'Liang Wengen is the founder and former chairman of Shanghai-listed construction equipment maker Sany Heavy Industry. He stepped down in 2022 but remained as a director. Sany''s holding company was founded in Hunan Province in 1989 as a small welding materials factory. Liang''s U.K.-educated son Liang Zaizhong served as chairman of the group''s Hong Kong-listed Sany Heavy Equipment International until 2025.', TRUE, FALSE),
('90160912-cf5c-4d0e-a29d-abdfbce0a5f9', 'Dirk Rossmann & family', 'Dirk', 'Rossmann', 'Germany', 'Drugstores', 'Fashion & Retail', 'The eponymous company Dirk Rossmann founded at age 25 is now Germany''s second-largest drugstore chain, with annual revenues of around $13 billion. In 1972, he opened Germany''s first self-service drugstore in Hannover just as price deregulation of pharmacy products was beginning. Rossmann has made numerous private equity investments and owns a stake in the German Bundesliga soccer club Hannover 96. He is a bestselling author. He published an autobiography in 2018, a novel, The Ninth Arm of the Octopus, in 2020, and its sequel, The Wrath of the Octopus, in 2021. His German Foundation for World Population focuses on sex education and family planning, primarily in East Africa.', TRUE, FALSE),
('9f22b86c-055b-42b1-bba1-b6b954a5d76f', 'Rekha Jhunjhunwala', 'Rekha', 'Jhunjhunwala', 'India', 'Investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Rekha Jhunjhunwala inherited a valuable stock portfolio from her late husband Rakesh Jhunjhunwala, who was often referred to as India''s Warren Buffett. The investor with a Midas touch passed away in 2022 at age 62.  The most valuable listed holdings in the portfolio are watch and jewelry maker Titan, part of the Tata conglomerate, and healthtech firm Inventurus Knowledge Solutions. The late Jhunjhunwala''s early bets on Star Health and Allied Insurance and Metro Brands paid off when both companies listed in 2021. Her husband was an investor in new, low-cost airline Akasa Air, which launched in August 2022, shortly before he died.', TRUE, FALSE),
('aca77201-90a9-4aa3-9e65-a989fce4fc7a', 'Hasmukh Chudgar & family', 'Hasmukh', 'Chudgar', 'India', 'Pharmaceuticals', 'Healthcare', 'Low profile Hasmukh Chudgar founded generics maker Intas Pharmaceuticals in 1977. Chudgar has long handed over operations to his sons Nimish and Binish, who run the $2.9 billion (revenue) company. In August 2025, Intas Pharma acquired biosimilar Udenyca from California-based Coherus Life Sciences for $558 million.  The company''s portfolio includes an affordable drug to treat breast cancer called Eleftha, which is similar to Roche''s Herceptin. In 2022, the Abu Dhabi Investment Authority bought a 3% stake in Intas from Temasek.', TRUE, FALSE),
('cd75fdf7-49b5-42d9-8a6d-cc009303e989', 'Pauline MacMillan Keinath', 'Pauline', 'Keinath', 'United States', 'Cargill', 'Food & Beverage', 'Pauline MacMillan Keinath is believed to be the largest shareholder of Cargill, the largest food company in the world, with an estimated 13% stake. Her late brother Whitney MacMillan was the last member of the family to serve as CEO of the business. He retired in 1995. Her great-grandfather, W.W. Cargill, founded the business as a single grain warehouse on the end of an Iowa railroad line in 1865. The family still owns roughly 90% of Cargill, which did $154 billion in 2025 sales across food, agriculture, financial and industrial divisions.', TRUE, FALSE),
('c1564d5f-2bd7-4b47-909f-6b55bfd9c543', 'Chris Larsen', 'Chris', 'Larsen', 'United States', 'Cryptocurrency', 'Finance & Investments', 'Chris Larsen cofounded Ripple in 2012 to facilitate international payments for banks using blockchain technology. In recent years, the company has spent roughly $3 billion on strategic acquisitions, transforming itself from a cross-border payment services provider into a full-stack crypto infrastructure company.  Larsen stepped down as Ripple''s CEO in December 2016 but remains its executive chairman.  Prior to Ripple, he cofounded online mortgage lender e-Loan in 1996 and Prosper, a peer-to-peer lender, in 2005. In 2015, Larsen teamed up with Doug Galen, E-Loan''s third employee, to launch Rippleworks, one of the first crypto-endowed foundations. It reported $2.5 billion in assets in 2025.', TRUE, FALSE),
('bc367c8c-4bd6-4732-82c8-efe2abc16fde', 'Karen Pritzker', 'Karen', 'Pritzker', 'United States', 'Hotels, investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Karen Pritzker is one of 13 billionaire Pritzker heirs. Her grandfather, A.N. Pritzker (d. 1986), built industrial conglomerate Marmon and Hyatt hotels. She has invested in public companies like Apple, as well as hundreds of private biotech and medical device firms. Pritzker and her late husband Michael Vlock donated to Yale, Teach for America and the Michael J. Fox Foundation for Parkinson''s Research. Her Seedlings Foundation supports the physical and mental health of children, and is one of the top-giving foundations in Connecticut.', TRUE, FALSE),
('3b21c11c-8d51-4114-8c47-d12458777d00', 'Wei Jianjun & family', 'Wei', 'Wei', 'China', 'Automobiles', 'Automotive', 'Wei Jianjun is the chairman of Great Wall Motor, one of China''s largest SUV manufacturers, which sells to over 170 countries and regions. He took over the debt-plagued Great Wall Automobile Industry Company, the predecessor to the current business, in 1990 when he was only 26. Wei worked at a carpet factory and a water-pump factory before joining Great Wall. Great Wall started up its first Brazil plant in August 2025. It is part of the company''s 10 billion reais ($1.9 billion) planned investment in the country.', TRUE, FALSE),
('285d61fe-205b-498b-8cba-3eef524b9c00', 'Jorge Moll Filho & family', 'Jorge', 'Moll Filho', 'Brazil', 'Hospitals', 'Healthcare', 'Jorge Neval Moll Filho is a cardiologist and entrepreneur who founded Rede D''Or, one of Brazil''s largest hospital and lab operators. Moll started his business with a health diagnostics imaging laboratory in 1977. Rede D''Or owns more than 30 hospitals. In 2010 Moll sold subsidiary Labs D''Or to publicly-traded Fleury SA for over $750 million. In 2015, private equity firm Carlyle Group and Singapore''s sovereign-wealth fund GIC bought stakes in Rede D''Or, spending over $500 million. Moll lives in Rio de Janeiro and is the president of the board of directors of Rede D''Or.', TRUE, FALSE),
('86e2f333-56db-44d1-acdc-3ef48d4cf284', 'Yi Zheng', 'Yi', 'Yi', 'China', 'Software', 'Technology', 'Yi Zheng is the chairman and CEO of Hithink RoyalFlush Information Network, a Shenzhen-listed financial data and information provider. The company operates Tonghuashun, a trading app for retail investors that counts over 35 million monthly active users in China. It also provides research and financial data services to enterprises through the iFinD platform.  Yi took gig jobs and started to develop analytics software for local brokerages before graduating from college.  He cofounded his first IT company in 1994 and Hithink''s predecessor Shanghai Hexin in 2001.', TRUE, FALSE),
('09b1e1e6-0d86-4a4f-98c5-0cb75a86fcc6', 'Ray Lee Hunt', 'Ray', 'Hunt', 'United States', 'Oil, real estate', 'Energy', 'Ray Lee Hunt is the wealthiest of legendary oil wildcatter H.L. Hunt''s 15 children. He is the chairman emeritus of Hunt Consolidated, an oil and gas, real estate and investing conglomerate. His Hunt Oil, once one of the largest privately held oil firms in the U.S., owns stakes in natural gas fields and a gas liquefaction plant in Peru. Hunt Oil was one of the first to land an exploration deal in Iraq''s Kurdistan region after the fall of Saddam Hussein. His son, Hunter Hunt, serves as CEO of Hunt Consolidated''s energy and infrastructure businesses and is his heir apparent.', TRUE, FALSE),
('9de3fcdb-9c95-4edf-b702-3ea456734d32', 'Jonathan Gray', 'Jonathan', 'Gray', 'United States', 'Investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Jonathan Gray started at asset manager Blackstone Group fresh out of college in 1992 and later rose to head the firm''s vaunted real estate group.
 Under Gray, Blackstone''s real estate division became one of its most valuable branches; it now manages $325 billion in investor capital. He orchestrated the $26 billion buyout of Hilton hotels in 2007 then took it public again in 2013; the IPO was then the biggest ever for a hotel firm.
 Gray was named Blackstone''s president and chief operating officer in 2018; he''s considered a potential successor to cofounder and CEO Steve Schwarzman. Gray, whose sister-in-law died of ovarian cancer at age 44, has given over $100 million to BRCA- related cancer research.', TRUE, FALSE),
('0c48f76d-a635-4b33-a4bc-9faf04bb7eeb', 'Zhang Hejun', 'Zhang', 'Zhang', 'China', 'Electronics', 'Manufacturing', 'Zhang Hejun is the chairman of Ningbo Deye Technology, a supplier of products ranging from energy storage systems and inverters to dehumidifiers and solar air conditioners. Zhang founded Deye in the eastern Chinese city of Ningbo in 1990. It went public on the Shanghai Stock Exchange in 2021 and has over 9,000 employees today. Deye''s business partners include Midea, Haier, TCL and AUX.  Zhang''s son Dongye serves as company vice chairman and CEO; older son Dongbin is a director.', TRUE, FALSE),
('a4f790ad-ebac-404c-934a-9fb4adfd57e8', 'Daniel Ziff', 'Daniel', 'Ziff', 'United States', 'Investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Daniel Ziff and brothers Robert and Dirk inherited a fortune that dates back to 1927 when their grandfather cofounded publishing company Ziff Davis. Daniel''s late father, William Jr., built up Ziff Davis, which became best known for such trade publications as PC Magazine and Car and Driver. The publishing business was sold for $1.4 billion in 1994. The brothers created Ziff Brothers Investments and greatly expanded their inheritance with hedge funds in the U.S. and in London. Ziff Brothers Investments ceased operations in 2014; the brothers are reportedly investing with former employees of their hedge funds.', TRUE, FALSE),
('74598b7f-911c-42c0-9a24-6e3abe6aca6a', 'Dirk Ziff', 'Dirk', 'Ziff', 'United States', 'Investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Dirk Ziff and his brothers Robert and Daniel inherited a fortune from their grandfather, who cofounded publishing company Ziff Davis in 1927. The brothers'' late father built up Ziff Davis, publisher of PC Magazine and Car and Driver, and sold the company for $1.4 billion in 1994. Through their Ziff Brothers Investments, which had hedge funds in the U.S. and in London, the brothers greatly expanded their inheritance. Ziff Brothers Investments ceased operations in 2014. In 2015, Dirk Ziff formed his own family office, Ziff Capital Partners. The brothers are also reportedly investing with former employees of their hedge funds.', TRUE, FALSE),
('060a6d6e-50b3-40c9-b9bb-ef27fa8537ce', 'Robert Ziff', 'Robert', 'Ziff', 'United States', 'Investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Like his billionaire brothers Dirk and Daniel, Robert Ziff owes his fortune to his grandfather''s publishing company, Ziff Davis. The brothers'' late father, William Jr., built up Ziff Davis, publisher of PC Magazine and Car and Driver, and sold the company for $1.4 billion in 1994. The brothers created Ziff Brothers Investments and grew their inheritance with hedge funds in the U.S. and in London. Ziff Brothers Investments ceased operations in 2014; the brothers are reportedly investing with former employees of their hedge funds.', TRUE, FALSE),
('7a9d7b45-341b-4b92-8fe4-115abf50a854', 'Vivek Chaand Sehgal', 'Vivek', 'Sehgal', 'Australia', 'Auto parts', 'Automotive', 'Vivek Chaand Sehgal is the chairman of the $23 billion (revenue) Motherson Group, which he established with his mother in 1975.  Sehgal draws the biggest chunk of his wealth from autoparts flagship Samvardhana Motherson International, formerly known as Motherson Sumi. In 2022, he hived off the India wiring harness business and listed it as Motherson Sumi Wiring India on the Indian bourses. The group''s clients include BMW, Ford, Mercedes, Toyota and Volkswagen. His son Laksh Vaaman Sehgal is a director on the boards of both Samvardhana Motherson International and Motherson Sumi Wiring India.', TRUE, FALSE),
('5fe89d16-b1f1-49e5-9167-2904d0220a77', 'Pang Kang', 'Pang', 'Pang', 'China', 'Soy sauce', 'Food & Beverage', 'Pang Kang was the chairman of Foshan Haitian Flavoring and Food, one of China''s biggest makers of soy sauce. He stepped down in September 2024. It produces condiments of more than 1,000 varieties and sells to over 80 countries and regions. Haitian went public on the Shanghai Stock Exchange in 2014. It completed in 2025 a listing in Hong Kong, raising $1.3 billion. Haitian has its roots in a soy sauce shop established in Foshan city during the mid-Qing Dynasty.', TRUE, FALSE),
('e80fb5a4-2a69-4e20-8b27-b9ec1573d739', 'Piero Ferrari & family', 'Piero', 'Ferrari', 'Italy', 'Automobiles', 'Automotive', 'Piero Ferrari is vice chairman and 10% owner of luxury race car company Ferrari. His father Enzo founded Ferrari. Piero became a billionaire when Ferrari listed its shares on the New York Stock Exchange in October 2015. The company went public as part of a spinoff from Fiat Chrysler. He became the sole heir after his stepbrother and Enzo''s first son, Alfredo "Dino" Ferrari, died from muscular dystrophy in 1956. Piero actively supports Centro Dino Ferrari, a research center for muscular and neurodegenerative diseases that his father cofounded in Dino''s memory.', TRUE, FALSE),
('b193371c-e81b-444a-9f8a-16544116fe35', 'Jean Salata', 'Jean', 'Salata', 'Chile', 'Finance', 'Finance & Investments', 'Jean Salata heads EQT Private Capital Asia, the Asian operation of Stockholm-listed investment giant EQT.
 He was nominated to take over as chairman of EQT in 2025, with the appointment set for May 2026. Salata held posts at Bain and AIG before joining Baring Private Equity Asia in 1997. He served as its CEO and led a management buyout of Baring in 2000. In 2022, EQT acquired Baring for $1.7 billion in cash and 191.2 million EQT shares. Salata is a Chilean citizen who has lived and worked in Hong Kong since 1989.', TRUE, FALSE),
('926895ba-3b8f-4b71-8ade-8c6970dc8bd8', 'Tatyana Kim', 'Tatyana', 'Kim', 'Russia', 'E-commerce', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Tatyana Kim, formerly Tatyana Bakalchuk, is a former English teacher and mother of seven, who started e-commerce retailer Wildberries in 2004. She founded the business at age 28 in her Moscow apartment while on maternity leave. Her husband, Vladislav Bakalchuk, an IT technician, soon joined her. In the early years, she resold clothes from German retailer Otto.', TRUE, FALSE),
('8fd37d5d-f513-4193-a56d-dff884cf5b89', 'Rafael Del Pino', 'Rafael', 'Del Pino', 'Spain', 'Construction', 'Construction & Engineering', 'Rafael Del Pino y Calvo-Sotelo is the chairman of Spanish infrastructure operator and construction firm Ferrovial, and owns around 22% of the shares. The company, which his father founded in 1952, manages large airports and highways around the world. Ferrovial has more than 22,000 employees and a presence in more than 15 markets. The company is listed on the Euronext Amsterdam, the Spanish stock exchanges and the United States'' Nasdaq. His sister Maria Del Pino y Calvo-Sotelo is the second largest shareholder of Ferrovial. His brothers Joaquin and Leopoldo are also shareholders. They are all billionaires.', TRUE, FALSE),
('af565cc9-fce9-4414-babc-1a456e453929', 'Paul Tudor Jones II', 'Paul', 'Jones', 'United States', 'Hedge funds', 'Finance & Investments', 'Hedge fund manager Paul Tudor Jones II is known for his macro trades, particularly his bets on interest rates and currencies. In 1980, he founded Tudor Investment Corporation, which now manages some $17 billion in assets. Jones got his start at his dad''s small business paper, the Memphis Daily News, where he wrote under the name Paul Eagle in high school and college. He cut his teeth trading cotton futures at the New York Cotton Exchange, under the tutelage of renowned cotton trader Eli Tullis. In 1988, he cofounded the Robin Hood Foundation, with the goal of reducing poverty in New York City.', TRUE, FALSE),
('981e2605-cf76-4e07-afda-526b730eabf9', 'Chase Coleman III', 'Chase', 'Coleman', 'United States', 'Investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Chase Coleman III started out as a hedge fund investor, but his Tiger Global Management has evolved into a broader investment firm. Tiger Global Management oversees $54 billion in assets. Its venture capital arm is now its biggest unit. Prior to starting Tiger Global in 2001, Coleman worked for the late hedge fund legend Julian Robertson. His longtime partner Scott Shleifer joined Tiger Global in 2002 and cofounded its venture business, which he led until the start of 2024.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6bbfd8a5-609d-43c2-ae15-b3c154721784', 'Massimiliana Landini Aleotti & family', 'Massimiliana', 'Landini Aleotti', 'Italy', 'Pharmaceuticals', 'Healthcare', 'Massimiliana Landini Aleotti and her three children inherited pharmaceutical giant Menarini from her late husband, Alberto Aleotti, in 2014. Alberto built Menarini into one of Italy''s leading drug companies, with 16 manufacturing sites around the world and more than 17,000 employees. Alberto Aleotti began working at Menarini in 1964, and bought the company from its owners in the early 1990s. In 2011, Aleotti handed over the reins to his daughter Lucia, who became chairman, and his son Alberto Giovanni, who became vice chairman. The family-owned company has an annual revenue of over $4 billion.', TRUE, FALSE),
('923ab026-66de-4798-8f32-95991ec53f25', 'Paolo Rocca', 'Paolo', 'Rocca', 'Italy', 'Pipe Manufacturing', 'Metals & Mining', 'Brothers Paolo and Gianfelice Rocca oversee the Techint Group, the global conglomerate founded by their grandfather, industrialist Agostino Rocca. Agostino helped build Italy''s steel industry in the 1930s then launched the Techint Group in Argentina in 1945. Its companies operate in steel production, engineering and construction projects, mining, oil and gas and the Italian hospital and healthcare sector. The Techint Group pulls in more than $38 billion in annual revenue and employs about 78,000 people globally. Paolo, who is CEO, resides in Argentina; Gianfelice runs the group''s healthcare company, Humanitas, from Italy.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d5d368fa-7b76-4eec-b3c5-bffe48d9cdcc', 'Gianfelice Rocca', 'Gianfelice', 'Rocca', 'Italy', 'Pipe Manufacturing', 'Metals & Mining', 'Brothers Gianfelice and Paolo Rocca oversee the Techint Group, the global conglomerate founded by their grandfather, industrialist Agostino Rocca. Agostino helped build Italy''s steel industry in the 1930s then launched the Techint Group in Argentina in 1945. Its companies operate in steel production, engineering and construction projects, mining, oil and gas and the Italian hospital and healthcare sector. The Techint Group pulls in more than $38 billion in annual revenue and employs about 78,000 people globally. Paolo, who is CEO, resides in Argentina; Gianfelice runs the group''s healthcare company, Humanitas, from Italy.', TRUE, FALSE),
('22100c01-b142-4e89-93bf-4e4073c19925', 'Clifford Asness', 'Clifford', 'Asness', 'United States', 'Money management', 'Finance & Investments', 'Cliff Asness is the cofounder of AQR Capital Management, a quant-driven money management firm with around $260 billion in investor assets. AQR stands for Applied Quantitative Research. It invests based on quantitative and proprietary signals, offering products including hedge funds, mutual funds and separately managed accounts. The firm is headquartered in Greenwich, Connecticut, with other locations in Bangaluru, Dubai, Hong Kong, London, Munich and Sydney. A finance Ph.D, Asness is an active researcher and worked in quantitative research for Goldman Sachs before starting AQR in 1998.', TRUE, FALSE),
('8d2aaeea-a00c-4543-9d25-2935d0bbaf0a', 'Maria Fernanda Amorim & family', 'Maria', 'Amorim', 'Portugal', 'Energy, investments', 'Diversified', 'Maria Fernanda Amorim is the widow of Americo Amorim, who died in 2017. She and her three daughters inherited his fortune. Americo Amorim spent six decades in his family''s cork business, Corticeira Amorim, and invested in an energy company and banks in several countries. His grandfather started Corticeira Amorim in 1870; the company has dominated the cork industry ever since. Amorim''s biggest asset is an approximate 20% stake in Portuguese oil and gas company Galp Energia, which is chaired by her eldest daughter Paula.', TRUE, FALSE),
('599dbb80-6634-48c0-8e0d-f929be6d55d2', 'Andreas Halvorsen', 'Andreas', 'Halvorsen', 'Norway', 'Hedge funds', 'Finance & Investments', 'Andreas Halvorsen runs hedge fund Viking Global Investors. A former Tiger Cub who once traded equities at Julian Robertson''s Tiger Management, he struck out on his own with Viking in 1999. The Connecticut-based firm now manages more than $46 billion in assets. Viking''s flagship hedge fund 13.8% net of fees in 2023, and its long-only fund returned 29.3% in a strong year for stocks.', TRUE, FALSE),
('26807da2-28c8-4478-b197-177050415931', 'Francis Choi', 'Francis', 'Choi', 'Hong Kong', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Francis Choi is the founder and chairman of Early Light International, one of the world''s largest toymakers. Known as the "King of Toys," Choi also serves as vice chairman of Regal Hotels International. His wealth is anchored by his sprawling property portfolio in mainland China, Hong Kong and Australia.  Choi also owns luxury watch retailer Unique Timepiece, formerly known as Halewinner, which he bought in 2010 and is now run by his son Karson. Karson is married to model Irene Wang. Karson and his older sister Carmen both serve as Early Light''s vice chairman.', TRUE, FALSE),
('525a5a18-183b-430e-a6a8-298bad742d2e', 'Sofie Kirk Kristiansen', 'Sofie', 'Kristiansen', 'Denmark', 'Lego', 'Manufacturing', 'A fourth-generation owner of Lego, Sofie Kirk Kristiansen, her father, sister and brother together split ownership of a 75% stake in the company. Kristiansen is not involved in the business; her brother, Thomas, serves as Lego''s deputy chairman. Her great-grandfather Ole, a carpenter, started making wooden toys in his workshop in 1932 before moving into plastic in the 1940s. The family has a 47.5% stake in theme park operator Merlin Entertainments, which it took private with a consortium.', TRUE, FALSE),
('ea05bc04-6229-4277-9d8b-3e4c28f22167', 'Thomas Kirk Kristiansen', 'Thomas', 'Kristiansen', 'Denmark', 'Lego', 'Manufacturing', 'A fourth-generation owner of Lego, Thomas Kirk Kristiansen succeeded his father Kjeld as deputy chairman of the company''s board in 2016. He, his two sisters and father together split ownership of a 75% stake in the $8 billion (sales) business. He is also chairman of the Lego Foundation and will succeed his father as chairman of Kirkbi, the family''s holding company, in the spring of 2023. His great-grandfather Ole, a carpenter, started making wooden toys in his workshop in 1932 before moving into plastic in the 1940s. The family also owns about half of theme park operator Merlin Entertainments, which it took private with a consortium in 2019.', TRUE, FALSE),
('4f812fad-3f88-4e36-8aa7-b6024b58f016', 'Agnete Kirk Thinggaard', 'Agnete', 'Thinggaard', 'Denmark', 'Lego', 'Manufacturing', 'A fourth-generation owner of Lego, Agnete Kirk Thinggaard splits ownership of a 75% stake in the toy company with her father, sister and brother. Thinggaard also sat on the Lego Foundation''s board until 2020, when she stepped down to join family holding company Kirkbi as a board observer. Her great-grandfather Ole, a carpenter, started making wooden toys in his workshop in 1932 before moving into plastic in the 1940s. The family also owns about half of theme park operator Merlin Entertainments, which it took private with a consortium in 2019. Thinggaard represented Denmark in dressage at the Rio de Janeiro Olympics in 2016; she placed 26th in individual competition.', TRUE, FALSE),
('53c81830-77f0-4f27-842a-d239327c9d74', 'Jacques Saadé Jr', 'Jacques', 'Saadé', 'France', 'Shipping', 'Logistics', 'Jacques Saadé Jr. is the son of late shipping magnate Jacques Saadé, who died in 2018. The Saadé family controls CMA CGM, one of the world''s largest shipping companies, founded in Marseille, France in 1978. Jacques serves as head of CMA CGM''s real estate assets. Jacques Saadé Jr. jointly controls the company with his siblings, Tanya Saadé Zeenny and Rodolphe, as well as his mother Naila. The $55.5 billion (2024 revenues) company operates more than 700 vessels, serving 420 commercial ports in 160 countries.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d645c7ac-a788-45cf-8cd4-ae8dd2b70f53', 'Rodolphe Saadé', 'Rodolphe', 'Saadé', 'France', 'Shipping', 'Logistics', 'Rodolphe Saadé is the son of late shipping magnate Jacques Saadé, who died in 2018. Jacques founded CMA CGM, now one of the world''s largest shipping companies, in Marseille, France in 1978. Rodolphe jointly controls the company with his siblings, Tanya Saadé Zeenny and Jacques Saadé Jr., as well as his mother Naila. He took over from his father as chairman of the board and CEO of CMA CGM Group in 2017. The $55.5 billion (2024 revenues) company operates more than 700 vessels, serving 420 commercial ports in 160 countries.', TRUE, FALSE),
('7329f081-d48a-4535-83ed-be3540bcca53', 'Tanya Saadé Zeenny', 'Tanya', 'Saadé Zeenny', 'France', 'Shipping', 'Logistics', 'Tanya Saadé Zeenny is the daughter of late shipping magnate Jacques Saadé, who died in 2018. Jacques founded CMA CGM, now one of the world''s largest shipping companies, in Marseille, France in 1978. Tanya jointly controls the company with her siblings, Rodolphe Saadé and Jacques Saadé Jr., as well as her mother Naila. In 1995, Tanya set up CMA CGM''s communications department. She now heads the company''s corporate social responsibility department and the CMA CGM Foundation. The $55.5 billion (2024 revenues) company operates more than 700 vessels, serving 420 commercial ports in 160 countries.', TRUE, FALSE),
('fb84122b-491b-4c9c-951f-89d67efbdb87', 'Steven Spielberg', 'Steven', 'Spielberg', 'United States', 'Movies', 'Media & Entertainment', 'The films of Steven Spielberg, a three-time Academy Award-winning director, have grossed more than $10 billion worldwide. Spielberg became a household name directing movies like  ''Jaws'' and ''Jurassic Park.'' 
 In 1994, he cofounded DreamWorks studios with Jeffrey Katzenberg and David Geffen. Today, a slice of the cash from every ticket at Universal Orlando theme parks goes directly into his pocket thanks to his work as a consultant when the first park opened in 1990. His recent turns in the director''s chair include ?Disclosure Day? and ?The Fablemans,? a semi-biographical tale about his entry into moviemaking.', TRUE, FALSE),
('7ad3996d-b759-49a3-a00f-ddcc9c5c389e', 'Lin Muqin & family', 'Lin', 'Lin', 'China', 'Beverages', 'Food & Beverage', 'Lin Muqin is the chairman and CEO of energy drink maker Eastroc Beverage (Group), which is dual-listed in Shanghai and Hong Kong.  The mogul started out as a technician at a state-owned construction firm, and later found a job at a Shenzhen-based beverage company. In 1997 he joined Eastroc, then a state-run beverage business, as its vice president. Lin reportedly scraped together more than 4 million yuan ($570,000) to acquire that firm in early 2000s.  He soon focused on making energy drinks. He managed to build Eastroc into China''s largest energy drink maker by sales volume partly through offering products at cheaper prices. Eastroc has diversified into other market segments including coffee and tea-based beverages.', TRUE, FALSE),
('e87410e5-425b-4b1f-9c30-35ea5b566be1', 'Stéphane Bancel', 'Stéphane', 'Bancel', 'France', 'Biotech, vaccines', 'Healthcare', 'Stephane Bancel is the CEO of Cambridge, Massachusetts-based biotech firm Moderna, known for its Covid-19 vaccine. He became CEO of Moderna in 2011 and owns a roughly 5.5% stake in the publicly traded company. Before joining Moderna, Bancel was the CEO of French diagnostics company BioMerieux, founded by fellow French billionaire Alain Merieux. Moderna''s Covid-19 vaccine was granted full FDA approval in January 2022; it had previously received emergency-use authorization in December 2020. Moderna was founded in 2010 and went public in December 2018; the company develops drugs and vaccines using messenger RNA.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6fce597e-eaa9-46db-81d8-2350989d07ac', 'Andrew Cherng', 'Andrew', 'Cherng', 'United States', 'Fast food', 'Food & Beverage', 'Andrew Cherng cofounded Chinese fast-food chain Panda Express, alongside his wife Peggy Cherng. Born in China, his family moved to Taiwan and Japan before he immigrated to the U.S., where he met Peggy as a freshman at Baker University in Kansas. The couple launched Panda Express in 1983 in a Glendale, California mall. Today the 2,600-location chain stretches from the U.S. to Canada, Mexico, Dubai and South Korea. The Cherngs are co-CEOs. In 2018, the couple invested in a group that bought the Mandarin Oriental hotel, now the Waldorf Astoria, in Las Vegas for $214 million.', TRUE, FALSE),
('bac61564-4d62-4973-8a5c-56b4d4743d3b', 'Peggy Cherng', 'Peggy', 'Cherng', 'United States', 'Fast food', 'Food & Beverage', 'Peggy Cherng is cofounder and co-CEO of Panda Express, the $6.7 billion (est. sales) Chinese fast-food chain with some 2,600 locations. Born in Myanmar, Cherng got a Ph.D. in electrical engineering in the U.S., then went to work for 3M and McDonnell Douglas, where she helped design battlefield simulators for the U.S. Navy. She left her engineering career to help her husband, Andrew Cherng, open Panda Express'' first location in a Glendale, California, shopping mall in 1983. She implemented the company''s sales and analytics software, earlier than many other restaurants, helping make Panda Express the dominant player among Asian limited-service chains in America. In 2018, the Cherngs invested in a group that bought the Mandarin Oriental hotel, now the Waldorf Astoria, in Las Vegas for $214 million.', TRUE, FALSE),
('e0fd5430-f073-40d7-a9ed-9d54f24d9ae3', 'Viktor Kharitonin', 'Viktor', 'Kharitonin', 'Russia', 'Pharmaceuticals', 'Healthcare', 'Viktor Kharitonin created multinational pharmaceutical firm Pharmstandard with Russian billionaire Roman Abramovich and other partners in 2003 by combining five factories. Kharitonin and partner Egor Kulkov bought out the other investors in 2008, a year after Pharmstandard went public in London. They took Pharmstandard private again, eight years later. Kharitonin and Kulkov also hold stakes in other Russian pharmaceuticals companies: OTCPharm,  Biocad  and Generium, one of the producers of the COVID-19 vaccine Sputnik V.  In 2022 The two partners tried to buy Russian assets of Austrian-British packaging and paper group Mondi for 1.5 billion euro, but Russian authorities rejected the deal. In 2023 Kharitonin and his partners bought Russian assets of German chemical producer Henkel for 600 million euros, leaving Henkel the option of buying back the business.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6fbb0716-eacb-46af-ac50-dab44fa54b57', 'Satyanarayan Nuwal', 'Satyanarayan', 'Nuwal', 'India', 'Industrial explosives', 'Manufacturing', 'Satyanarayan Nuwal started Solar Industries India in 1995 to trade in industrial explosives then started manufacturing them. The biggest chunk of its annual revenue is from exports, followed by housing and infrastructure, state-owned coal companies and the defense sector. The son of a government employee, Nuwal set up his first business, an ink manufacturing unit in 1970 at age 18. It has 27 manufacturing locations across India and exports to more than 90 countries. Nuwal and his brother Kailashchandra, also a billionaire, have been embroiled in a feud since 2020.', TRUE, FALSE),
('323469d0-3519-465d-96cf-5ecc7cc95b16', 'Guillaume Pousaz', 'Guillaume', 'Pousaz', 'Switzerland', 'Fintech', 'Finance & Investments', 'Guillaume Pousaz founded Checkout.com in 2012 to solve the problem of online payment processing for shops and shoppers around the world. In January 2022, Checkout.com raised $1 billion from private investors, valuing the company at $40 billion. In December 2022, Checkout.com marked down its internal valuation to $11 billion, as fintech valuations tumbled during the year; a year later it was lowered to $9.35 billion. In 2025, it rose to $12 billion, according to the company. Pousaz, who is CEO of Checkout.com, owns an estimated nearly two-thirds of the London-based company. The Swiss citizen dropped out of college to go surfing in California before working in fintech and payments.', TRUE, FALSE),
('0de21b7e-2319-4a59-a3e8-221f6e307b45', 'Thomas Pritzker', 'Thomas', 'Pritzker', 'United States', 'Hotels, investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Tom Pritzker is one of 13 billionaire heirs in the Pritzker clan behind hotel giant Hyatt. He stepped down as Hyatt''s executive chairman in February 2026 amid scrutiny over his friendly relationship with Jeffrey Epstein. "There is no excuse for failing to distance myself sooner," he said at the time. Hyatt Hotels dates back to 1957 when Tom''s father, Jay Pritzker (d. 1999), purchased the first Hyatt House motel near Los Angeles International Airport. Tom''s father Jay and uncle Robert acquired manufacturing firm Marmon in the 1950s and expanded it; Tom led Marmon''s 2008 sale to Berkshire Hathaway. Pritzker stepped down from the board of Royal Caribbean Cruises in 2020 after two decades as a director.', TRUE, FALSE),
('f6aff2aa-3a5f-4d0f-884d-65df0ca5d0e6', 'Vyacheslav Kim', 'Vyacheslav', 'Kim', 'Kazakhstan', 'Fintech', 'Finance & Investments', 'Vyacheslav Kim is chairman of Kaspi Bank, Kazakhstan''s largest payments and fintech company. Kaspi''s 2020 IPO was celebrated as London''s largest international tech public offering that year . Kaspi generated revenues of $2.5 billion in 2024. Kim''s partner at Kaspi is Georgian billionaire Mikhail Lomtadze, a former private equity investor at Russian-focused fund Baring Vostock.', TRUE, FALSE),
('e7f643bf-ff95-44d6-8c1b-0bb2e96712b1', 'Rinat Akhmetov', 'Rinat', 'Akhmetov', 'Ukraine', 'Steel, coal', 'Metals & Mining', 'Ukraine''s richest person, Rinat Akhmetov has vowed to stay in Ukraine and support his country in its fight against Russia. Russian forces destroyed plants owned by his mining and steel firm Metinvest and ravaged substations of his power generation firm DTEK. More than 1,400 of his employees have died as a result of the war.   He says his companies, which still operate, have donated $368 million in goods and have invested around $4 billion in restoring infrastructure destroyed by Russia, building new facilities and modernizing production. The son of a coal miner, Akhmetov got his start buying up mining assets during the 1990s privatization era. Akhmetov is believed to own a 476-foot yacht, named Luminance, that cost him $500 million. He also owns a French villa and a London apartment.', TRUE, FALSE),
('24bcf883-4159-45ba-a6b8-60cf344ea7d5', 'Vincent Viola', 'Vincent', 'Viola', 'United States', 'Electronic trading', 'Finance & Investments', 'The son of a truck driver from Brooklyn, Vincent Viola started electronic-trading firm Virtu Financial in 2008 and took the company public in 2015. Market-maker Virtu completed a series of secondary offerings in May 2019 to help repurchase more than $500 million in stock from Viola. Viola splurged on real estate with stock sale proceeds, buying a beachfront Florida condo and spending $108 million on Arizona''s tallest skyscraper. Viola is the owner of the NHL''s Florida Panthers. He graduated from West Point in 1977 and New York Law School in 1983. In 2003 he founded the Combating Terrorism Center at West Point to provide education and research about global terrorism.', TRUE, FALSE),
('9b9fe86f-5ce1-442c-97b7-a672e3ed2b07', 'David Thomson', 'David', 'Thomson', 'Canada', 'Thomson Reuters', 'Media & Entertainment', 'David Thomson is one of six billionaire heirs to the media and publishing empire founded by his grandfather Roy Thomson (d. 1976). The family''s biggest holding: more than 310 million shares of Thomson Reuters, where Thomson serves as chairman. Thomson owns around 14% of the business through the family''s investment firm, Woodbridge.  The family''s other assets include the Toronto-based Globe and Mail newspaper, and the Montreal Canadiens and Winnipeg Jets sports teams.', TRUE, FALSE),
('1b9a0bbd-59c0-4e6f-a8f5-9ab0d191f904', 'Peter Thomson', 'Peter', 'Thomson', 'Canada', 'Thomson Reuters', 'Media & Entertainment', 'Peter Thomson is one of six billionaire heirs to the media and publishing empire founded by his grandfather Roy Thomson (d. 1976). The family''s biggest holding: more than 310 million shares of Thomson Reuters; Thomson is on Thomson Reuters'' board of directors. Thomson owns around 14% of the business through the family''s investment firm, Woodbridge, where Thomson serves as chairman. The family''s other assets include the Toronto-based Global and Mail newspaper, and the Montreal Canadiens and Winnipeg Jets sports teams.', TRUE, FALSE),
('2249a4c9-3396-43aa-8190-51c390bb415e', 'Taylor Thomson', 'Taylor', 'Thomson', 'Canada', 'Thomson Reuters', 'Media & Entertainment', 'Taylor Thomson is one of six billionaire heirs to the media and publishing empire founded by her grandfather Roy Thomson (d. 1976). The family''s biggest holding: more than 310 million shares of Thomson Reuters. Thomson owns around 14% of the business through the family''s investment firm, Woodbridge. The family''s other assets include the Toronto-based Globe and Mail newspaper, and the Montreal Canadiens and Winnipeg Jets sports teams.', TRUE, FALSE),
('38af9b38-70b6-4e09-b07e-2e15ed5dd58f', 'Patrick Drahi', 'Patrick', 'Drahi', 'France', 'Telecom', 'Telecom', 'Telecoms magnate Patrick Drahi is the founder and owner of multinational Altice NV, which he took private in January 2021 at a $7.3 billion valuation. Drahi built Altice with more than 20 acquisitions of lagging cable and mobile operators and has expanded further with highly leveraged deals. In 2021, he spent approximately $4.2 billion to purchase an 18% stake in British telecom giant BT Group. Three years later, he sold it to India''s Bharti Global.  He stormed the U.S. in 2015 by buying a 70% stake in cable operator Suddenlink for $9 billion and snapping up Cablevision for $17.7 billion. Those U.S. entities were spun off into Altice USA, which went public in June 2017.', TRUE, FALSE),
('9465354a-8e0b-4bc8-ad3c-48412ee8908b', 'Cal McNair', 'Cal', 'McNair', 'United States', 'Houston Texans', 'Sports', 'Cal McNair was named principal owner of the Houston Texans in 2024, taking over the role from his mother Janice McNair (d. 2026). Prior to inheriting the NFL team, he served in various executive roles, including his current role of CEO since 2019. McNair also sits on the boards of Palmetto Trust Company and the Robert and Janice McNair Foundation.  He attended the University of Texas at Austin, where he played football for four years, before receiving an MBA from Rice University.  He has seven children and seven grandchildren.', TRUE, FALSE),
('bd11334f-8fd9-452a-9e0d-f61973578af0', 'Jack Dorsey', 'Jack', 'Dorsey', 'United States', 'Twitter, Square', 'Technology', 'Jack Dorsey is chairman and block head (effectively CEO) of payments company Block, formerly known as Square.  Dorsey cofounded Square with Jim McKelvey in 2009, then took it public in 2015; it was renamed Block in 2021. He was previously CEO of Twitter from 2015 to 2021 and stepped down from the board in 2022. Dorsey cofounded Twitter in 2006 with Ev Williams, Biz Stone and Noah Glass, and was CEO until 2008. He returned to the role in 2015.  Forbes estimates that Dorsey now owns a 0.14% stake in SpaceX after Elon Musk bought Twitter in 2022, merged it in a series of deals with his rocket maker, and took SpaceX public in 2026.', TRUE, FALSE),
('bd87147d-af0d-4136-b5be-20a6516704d9', 'Alain Bouchard', 'Alain', 'Bouchard', 'Canada', 'Convinience stores', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Alain Bouchard cofounded convenience store conglomerate Alimentation Couche-Tard with a single Quebec shop in 1980. As executive chairman, Bouchard still oversees the $73 billion (sales) company, which boasts more than 17,000 owned or franchised stores worldwide. Bouchard, who grew the business rapidly by snatching up competitors, retired as president and CEO in September 2014. Couche-Tard acquired the Circle K chain in 2003 and the Holiday Stationstores and CST Brands chains in 2017.  Couche-Tard made a $20 billion bid for French food retailer Carrefour in early 2021, but the French government nixed the deal.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6e2fb435-e37e-46fe-9f2a-222d676edf62', 'Stephen Cohen', 'Stephen', 'Cohen', 'United States', 'Software', 'Technology', 'Stephen Cohen cofounded data mining firm Palantir around the time he finished college in 2003 and is currently president and secretary.  Cohen''s fortune comes from his approximately 1.5% stake in the company (including options), which went public in 2020 in an unusual direct listing.   He has held various roles at Palantir, including a stint as vice president where he interviewed as many as 50 prospective employees a week.  Cohen is a protege of billionaire investor Peter Thiel; he worked for Thiel''s hedge fund while he was in college. Cohen has said he didn''t sleep Tuesdays through Thursdays during his last quarter at Stanford because of his work for Thiel''s hedge fund.', TRUE, FALSE),
('1f470b3a-dcd9-4d3e-80a6-6982f8b2cdd1', 'Lin Li', 'Lin', 'Lin', 'China', 'Investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Lin Li is the chairman of investment firm Liye Group, which has interests in sectors such as healthcare, metals and green energy. The group is a shareholder of ChinaLin Securities and Tencent-backed online bank WeBank. Lin''s son, Lin Dibang, is the chairman of Shenzhen-based drug maker Cali Biosciences. It planned for an IPO in Hong Kong which didn''t go through. The elder Lin worked at several local branches of the Bank of China before founding Liye in 1995.', TRUE, FALSE),
('e260d2db-de06-40a5-8048-84248b0f1da1', 'Jim Kavanaugh', 'Jim', 'Kavanaugh', 'United States', 'IT provider', 'Technology', 'Jim Kavanaugh is the CEO of IT provider World Wide Technology. With David Steward, he started the St. Louis-based company in 1990 by selling computers and printers to telecom companies like AT&T. Kavanaugh personally fulfilled one of the company''s first orders by renting a truck and driving 500 PCs to Omaha. WWT is now a $20 billion (sales) company that sells software and hardware to customers including Citi, Verizon and the federal government. Before starting WWT, Kavanaugh was a professional soccer player and was on the 1984 Olympic team.', TRUE, FALSE),
('26eae59b-b0b9-4e43-9cd2-3c864c087f91', 'Zong Fuli', 'Zong', 'Zong', 'China', 'Beverages', 'Food & Beverage', 'Zong Fuli, also known as Kelly, is the daughter of beverage giant Hangzhou Wahaha Group''s late founder Zong Qinghou. Her wealth is based on a company stake inherited in 2024, after the elder Zong passed away earlier in the year.  Once Wahaha''s chairman and CEO, Kelly stepped down in 2025, handing the reins over to long-time lieutenant Xu Simin. She already stepped down once in 2024, before being reinstated months later after resolving an unspecified shareholder dispute at the time. In 2025, she was sued in Hong Kong over $2.1 billion worth of trust assets by three plaintiffs who claim to be her half siblings.', TRUE, FALSE),
('c6d81485-7e36-420d-b05c-87742adaceb1', 'Mikhail Gutseriev', 'Mikhail', 'Gutseriev', 'Russia', 'Oil, coal, real estate', 'Energy', 'Mikhail Gutseriev is a founder and the main shareholder of Safmar Group, a conglomerate with interests in oil, coal, real estate and retail. Between 2015 and 2017, he spent $2 billion acquiring banks, pension funds, oil fields, factories, warehouses, real estate and retail companies. In 2017 Binbank, which was headed by his nephew, former billionaire Mikail Shishkhanov, was nationalized by Russian Central Bank. His son Said is a shareholder of Safmar. His father gave him his financial business and a big appliance store chain.  Gutseriev was sanctioned by the U.K. and EU in 2021 for being a "longtime friend" of Belarusian dictator Alexander Lukashenko. In 2022 he transferred assets to Kazakhstani Salman Gutsariyev.', TRUE, FALSE),
('12a3fc70-8cee-4b7c-8674-dee808b53ba4', 'Michael Kim', 'Michael', 'Kim', 'United States', 'Private equity', 'Finance & Investments', 'Michael Kim cofounded MBK Partners, the Seoul-based private equity firm that bears his initials and manages more than $33 billion in assets. His ING Insurance Korea, which went public in 2017, was the first company wholly owned by a private equity firm to list on the Korean exchange. In 2015 his firm''s $6.1 billion takeover of Tesco''s Korean operation, Homeplus, marked the country''s biggest private-equity deal to date. In 2025, MBK and Homeplus were accused of issuing bonds of the portfolio company while anticipating a credit downgrade; MBK has denied the allegation and the case is ongoing.  Kim was born in South Korea and was educated in the U.S. from preparatory school onward; he obtained U.S. citizenship along the way.', TRUE, FALSE),
('e636bc4d-0add-405c-a583-9125db6bc488', 'Herb Simon', 'Herb', 'Simon', 'United States', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'In 1960, Herb Simon and his brother Melvin (d. 2009) founded the precursor to Simon Property Group. Simon Property Group is now one of the world''s largest real estate investment trusts, with 235 properties globally, including 212 in the U.S. Simon was chairman emeritus until he retired in February 2025. His nephew, David, who was Melvin''s son, served as CEO from 1995 until his death in 2026, and was succeeded by his son Eli. Simon also owns an 80% stake in the Indiana Pacers, which he bought with his brother. The team is worth more than $3 billion. Additionally, Simon owns the WNBA team Indiana Fever, which first played in the 2000 season. The team is worth $370 million.', TRUE, FALSE),
('1b55fd35-5360-46c1-a873-9b1c9386ba6b', 'Michael Moritz', 'Michael', 'Moritz', 'United States', 'Venture capital', 'Finance & Investments', 'Wales native Michael Moritz got his start as a journalist at Time Magazine after immigrating to America in 1976. Moritz wrote an early biography of Steve Jobs and Apple, "The Little Kingdom," while he was Time''s San Francisco bureau chief. After making the jump to venture capital firm Sequoia Capital, Moritz invested in companies such as Google, LinkedIn and PayPal. He stepped back from a leadership role at Sequoia in 2012 after being diagnosed with a rare and undisclosed medical condition. In 2023, Sequoia announced in a letter to its limited partners that Moritz had left the firm after 38 years.', TRUE, FALSE),
('1d68148f-5bce-4538-949d-5edbf96a7727', 'Denise Coates', 'Denise', 'Coates', 'United Kingdom', 'Online gambling', 'Gambling & Casinos', 'Coates is co-CEO of Bet365, one of the world''s largest online gambling companies, along with her billionaire brother, John. Coates first trained as an accountant before taking over a number of her family''s betting shops and then selling them to bookmaker Coral. Noting the success of online gambling businesses, Coates bought the domain Bet365.com in 2000 and launched the website in 2001. She owns around half of privately held Bet365, which facilitates more than $65 billion in bets a year.', TRUE, FALSE),
('32ff5d6a-9cd6-4a5a-9bbe-8529f4267f53', 'Mike Brown & family', 'Mike', 'Brown', 'United States', 'Cincinnati Bengals', 'Sports', 'Mike Brown and his family own the NFL''s Cincinnati Bengals, which Forbes valued at more than $5 billion in 2025. He helped his father, Paul, found the team in 1967 after the elder Brown was fired as the Cleveland Browns coach in 1963. Several members of the Brown family are involved with the team today, including Mike''s daughter Katie, who was the first woman to be named to the NFL''s Competition Committee.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6cf3de4d-4f1b-4a38-b6fc-0b510262a91e', 'Oleg Deripaska', 'Oleg', 'Deripaska', 'Russia', 'Aluminum, utilities', 'Metals & Mining', 'Oleg Deripaska is the founder of Basic Element, a Russian industrial group with interests in aluminum, energy, construction, agriculture and more. In April 2018, the U.S. Department of the Treasury''s Office of Foreign Assets Control imposed sanctions against Deripaska and some of his companies. In 2000, he merged his Siberian Aluminum with the aluminum assets of Roman Abramovich''s Millhouse Capital to form UC Rusal. In January 2019, OFAC lifted sanctions on En+ Group, UC Rusal and Eurosibenergo, and Deripaska agreed to permanently reduce his stake to 44.95%. He was the richest person in Russia and the 9th richest in the world in 2008 before nearly losing it all due to crashing markets and heavy debts.', TRUE, FALSE),
('64c33d26-79e3-4f96-b342-ab260af660b9', 'Daniel Nadler', 'Daniel', 'Nadler', 'Canada', 'AI software', 'Technology', 'Daniel Nadler cofounded OpenEvidence in 2022 to use AI to help doctors make sense of the voluminous amount of medical research. OpenEvidence has reached a valuation of $12 billion after an early 2026 funding round. Nadler owns nearly 60% of the company. Before founding OpenEvidence, Nadler cofounded Kensho, which used AI for financial intelligence. He sold that company to S&P for $550 million in 2018. OpenEvidence has signed up more than 758,000 doctors, and is adding them at a rate of 55,000 per month. It''s free for verified doctors, and makes its money from advertising.', TRUE, FALSE),
('dc2e2711-2775-4199-9450-fa8e68d1a96d', 'Sudhir Mehta', 'Sudhir', 'Mehta', 'India', 'Pharmaceuticals, power', 'Healthcare', 'Sudhir Mehta is chairman emeritus of the Ahmedabad-based Torrent Group comprising Torrent Pharma, Torrent Power and Torrent Gas. His younger brother Samir Mehta, also a billionaire, chairs the pharma and power companies. His son Jinal Mehta is managing director of Torrent Power. His younger son Varun is executive director in the power business. Torrent Power distributes electricity to more than 4 million customers across India. In February 2026, Torrent Pharma completed the acquisition of a 48% stake in rival JB Chemicals for $1.3 billion.', TRUE, FALSE),
('b83fefdc-8e20-4b87-aa1f-67c60dc06c21', 'Samir Mehta', 'Samir', 'Mehta', 'India', 'Pharmaceuticals, power', 'Healthcare', 'Samir Mehta gets the bulk of his wealth from Torrent Pharmaceuticals, flagship of his family''s  Ahmedabad-based  Torrent Group. The 67-year-old company was founded by his late father Uttambhai Nathalal Mehta, who was a salesman for Swiss pharma giant Sandoz. He also has a stake in Torrent Power, which provides electricity in his home state of Gujarat and two other states. While Samir Mehta runs the pharma unit, his older sibling Sudhir''s son, Jinal, oversees the power firm. In February 2026, Torrent Pharma completed the acquisition of a 48% stake  in rival JB Chemicals for $1.3 billion.', TRUE, FALSE)
