 The trio founded Apollo in 1990, after Drexel filed for bankruptcy following a cash shortage caused by turmoil in the junk bond market. Rowan and his cofounders took Apollo Global public in 2011. Rowan replaced Black as Apollo''s CEO in 2021, after the latter stepped amid controversy surrounding his longtime relationship with convicted sex offender Jeffrey Epstein.', TRUE, FALSE),
('43a13001-3e4e-4389-bde2-88dbf404d955', 'Maria Angelicoussis', 'Maria', 'Angelicoussis', 'Greece', 'Shipping', 'Logistics', 'Maria Angelicoussis is the CEO and owner of Angelicoussis Group, a shipping company based in Athens, Greece. Founded in 1947 by her grandfather, Antonis, Maria took the reins of the group after the death of her father, John, in April 2021. The Angelicoussis Group owns 158 ships, including oil tankers, liquid natural gas carriers and dry bulk vessels. Angelicoussis obtained a medical degree from Cambridge University and worked as a junior doctor in the British National Health Service for two years. She first joined the family business in 2008, when she returned to Greece from the U.K. to work as the group''s vice president.', TRUE, FALSE),
('68a71b4c-bc66-4c0a-abd4-79101b0c3ef4', 'John Grayken', 'John', 'Grayken', 'Ireland', 'Private equity', 'Finance & Investments', 'John Grayken is the founder and owner of Lone Star Funds, a private equity firm based in Dallas, Texas, that focuses on corporate equity, real estate, credit, and other financial assets. Since 1995, Grayken has raised 25 funds with approximately $95 billion in committed capital.  The assets Lone Star buys are managed by Hudson Advisors, a firm based in Dallas that Grayken owns with over 800 employees and more than $260 billion in cumulative assets managed. Grayken is from a suburb south of Boston, but he renounced his U.S. citizenship for tax purposes in the 1990s and took Irish citizenship.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d78f77fd-9690-43af-aca4-43192521c01b', 'Otto Toto Sugiri', 'Otto', 'Sugiri', 'Indonesia', 'Data centers', 'Technology', 'Otto Toto Sugiri is cofounder and CEO of DCI Indonesia. He started the company in 2011 and built it into one of Indonesia''s largest operators of data centers. DCI Indonesia was listed in 2021. Prior to DCI, Sugiri founded Sigma Cipta Caraka in 1989, which was acquired by Telkom Indonesia and is now called Telkomsigma. In 1994, Sugiri cofounded Indonet, the first internet service provider in Indonesia, which went public in 2021. In 2023, he and other cofounders sold their stakes to Singapore''s Digital Edge.', TRUE, FALSE),
('53070592-87a6-4076-b8c7-d322ccab4c6c', 'Jeffrey Koo Jr', 'Jeffrey', 'Koo', 'Taiwan', 'Finance', 'Finance & Investments', 'Jeffrey Koo Jr. owns a significant stake in CTBC Financial Holding, one of Taiwan''s largest financial institutions. It was set up in 2002 by his late father, Jeffrey Sr., and today has 27,000 employees around the world with interests in banking, insurance, brokerage and other services. Jeffrey Jr. is the seventh-generation of the Koo Family that trace their roots to Koh Lay Huan, the first Kapitan Cina of Penang. The family first made their fortune in camphor, salt, sugar and land and founded the Koos Group. His eldest son Jeffrey III became a director at subsidiaries CTBC Venture Capital and Taiwan Lottery in 2022. Jeffrey Jr.''s brothers, Andre and Angelo, are also billionaires and own stakes in Taiwan''s financial giants Chailease Holding and China Development Financial Holding, respectively.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d0f17bb7-94f4-4722-866f-30c85c5e6692', 'H. Ross Perot Jr', 'H.', 'Perot', 'United States', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Ross Perot Jr. founded real estate development company Hillwood, whose diversified portfolio spans 13,007 acres owned or optioned. His father, late billionaire presidential candidate Ross Perot Sr., let his son borrow against his fortune to start his real estate empire. Perot Jr.''s Hillwood has developed and acquired over 300 million square feet of industrial space and 90 residential communities. Hillwood also built AllianceTexas, an inland port on 27,000 acres of pasture outside Fort Worth, which is home to 590 companies. Perot Jr. was elected chairman of the board of the U.S. Chamber of Commerce in 2025. He was previously elected vice chairman in 2024 and has served on the board since 2020.', TRUE, FALSE),
('3a31b496-dca2-4e50-89f6-8dff5df7993f', 'Xu Hang', 'Xu', 'Xu', 'Hong Kong', 'Medical devices', 'Healthcare', 'Xu Hang is cofounder and director of Shenzhen Mindray Bio-Medical Electronics, a supplier of medical devices. Mindray, founded in 1991, is headquartered in Shenzhen. He also owns China''s real estate developer Parkland Group, best known for its mixed-use skyscraper complex One Shenzhen Bay.', TRUE, FALSE),
('02b2632e-ca9d-443d-9574-6a42aa64a1eb', 'Dona Bertarelli', 'Dona', 'Bertarelli', 'Switzerland', 'Biotech and investments', 'Healthcare', 'The bulk of Dona Bertarelli''s wealth comes from the 2007 sale of her family''s biotech business Serono for over $13 billion. In the 1990s Dona was Serono''s executive director of public and professional affairs. Her brother Ernesto is the richest man in Switzerland. They split ownership of most family assets. She now focuses her time on marine conservation efforts and is a special adviser to the United Nations.', TRUE, FALSE),
('930fbe7e-5805-4954-bbde-cc8d75c295e2', 'Quek Leng Chan', 'Quek', 'Quek', 'Malaysia', 'Banking, property', 'Diversified', 'Quek Leng Chan is the executive chairman of privately held Hong Leong Co. (Malaysia), which has interests in finance, food and property. He inherited part of his fortune from his father, one of three brothers who started a banking group in the 1920s. His cousin, Kwek Leng Beng, is also a billionaire and serves as chairman of Hong Leong Group in Singapore.', TRUE, FALSE),
('ba612740-7e3d-453f-8173-9d947f25c19a', 'Zeng Fangqin', 'Zeng', 'Zeng', 'Hong Kong', 'Smartphone components', 'Technology', 'Zeng Fangqin is the chairman and general manager of Lingyi iTech, a maker of electronic components and a known Apple supplier. The company, already listed in Shenzhen, raised in 2026 $1.1 billion through a separate share sale in Hong Kong. Zeng worked for a state-owned enterprise in Shenzhen before heading to the U.S. in the 1980s. Prior to returning to China, She worked in Silicon Valley. Lingyi also supplies sectors including autos, AI hardware, servers and humanoid robots.', TRUE, FALSE),
('0d625b44-16f9-4509-a96c-1a36582e6481', 'Thai Lee', 'Thai', 'Lee', 'United States', 'IT provider', 'Technology', 'Thai Lee is CEO of $16 billion (gross sales) IT provider SHI International, which has 17,000 customers, including Boeing and AT&amp;T. Born in Bangkok, Lee grew up in South Korea and moved to the U.S. for high school before heading to Amherst for college. Her father, a prominent economist who traveled the world promoting his country''s postwar development plan, was the first Korean to graduate from Amherst. Lee, also an alum of Harvard Business School, did stints at Procter &amp; Gamble and American Express. Lee and her now ex-husband Leo KoGuan paid less than $1 million for a software reseller in 1989, the predecessor to SHI. Today she owns 60% while he owns 40%.', TRUE, FALSE),
('0a2d57b5-50d8-45db-b088-b61270aa7398', 'Yitzhak Tshuva', 'Yitzhak', 'Tshuva', 'Israel', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Yitzhak Tshuva made his billions in energy and real estate. His private El Ad Group, a real estate firm, has developments in Manhattan, Florida, Louisiana, Montreal and Israel. His is also the controlling shareholder of Delek Group, a publicly-traded conglomerate with interests in automotives, oil and gas. His family immigrated from Libya to Israel when he was six months old. He later served in the Israeli army and worked in Israel''s Ministry of Defense.', TRUE, FALSE),
('bcf9777e-d119-4b79-becf-daae5357bf7a', 'Timur Turlov', 'Timur', 'Turlov', 'Kazakhstan', 'Stock brokerage', 'Finance & Investments', 'Timur Turlov is the CEO and founder of Freedom Holding, a Kazakhstan-based retail brokerage; it operates in Central Asia, Europe and the U.S. Freedom Holding gives post-Soviet citizens access to American and European stock exchanges and specializes in IPOs. The company entered the U.S. in 2015 through a shell of a Kazakh oil and gas exploration entity located in Nevada. 
 Freedom Holding began trading on the Nasdaq in 2019, an event that Turlov calls his proudest accomplishment to date. Turlov says he started the company in 2008 (before he finished college) with $100,000 pooled with his cofounders.', TRUE, FALSE),
('0c68cf95-a2cf-4196-b58c-f7a6d88a6d12', 'Cao Renxian', 'Cao', 'Cao', 'China', 'Photovoltaic equipment', 'Energy', 'Cao Renxian is the chairman and president of Sungrow Power Supply, which makes renewable energy products such as solar PV inverters, wind power converters and energy storage products.  Coming from an impoverished rural family in Hangzhou, Cao got his bachelor''s and master''s degrees in industrial automation from the Hefei University of Technology. After spotting opportunities in the renewable energy market, he founded in 1997 Sungrow while teaching at his alma mater.  Today, the Shenzhen-listed company also sells its products in global markets including the Middle East, Southeast Asia and the U.S.', TRUE, FALSE),
('68fd638f-cb6e-4f24-b722-d447bf0a8c93', 'You Xiaoping & family', 'You', 'You', 'China', 'Polyurethanes', 'Manufacturing', 'You Xiaoping is the chairman of Huafon Group, a maker of polyurethane products. Huafon Group is also involved in metals, finance, logistics and trade. One of its units, Shenzhen-listed Huafon Chemical, is among the world''s largest spandex fiber makers by production volume.', TRUE, FALSE),
('4e2fc633-e818-464b-b11c-716846a75f4b', 'Elizabeth Uihlein', 'Elizabeth', 'Uihlein', 'United States', 'Packaging materials', 'Manufacturing', 'Elizabeth Uihlein is president of Uline, one of North America''s biggest distributors of shipping, packaging and industrial supplies. Headquartered in Pleasant Prairie, Wisconsin, $8.1 billion (est. revenue) Uline sells more than 43,000 products via its 900+ page catalog to businesses nationwide. Elizabeth (Liz) and her husband, Richard (Dick), started Uline in their basement in 1980; it now has 9,000 employees. Together, the couple has given over $450 million over the years backing conservative candidates in federal races, according to FEC filings, making them one of the top donors in the United States. The duo shelled out more than $140 million in the 2023-2024 election cycle. Originally Ron DeSantis supporters, they shifted to Trump after the Republican primary.', TRUE, FALSE),
('fd0f4fab-0813-47cf-bad1-d08795638d86', 'Richard Uihlein', 'Richard', 'Uihlein', 'United States', 'Packaging materials', 'Manufacturing', 'Richard Uihlein is the CEO of Uline, one of North America''s biggest distributors of shipping, packaging, and industrial supplies. Headquartered in Pleasant Prairie, Wisconsin, $8.1 billion (est. revenue) Uline sells more than 43,000 products via its 900+ page catalog to businesses nationwide. Richard (Dick) and his wife Elizabeth (Liz) started Uline in their basement in 1980; it now has 9,000 employees. Together, the couple has given over $450 million over the years backing conservative candidates in federal races, according to FEC filings, making them one of the top donors in the United States. The duo shelled out more than $140 million in the 2023-2024 election cycle. Originally Ron DeSantis supporters, they shifted to Trump after the Republican primary.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d47c59ce-c567-4580-b080-092295150cd0', 'Mark Walter', 'Mark', 'Walter', 'United States', 'Finance, asset management', 'Finance & Investments', 'Mark Walter is CEO of investment firm Guggenheim Partners, which has more than $300 billion in assets under management. Walter helped found the firm in the late 1990s after he folded his Chicago-based company, Liberty Hampshire, into the Guggenheim family office. Walter''s personal investments include stakes in plant-based food maker Beyond Meat and online car vendor Carvana. Walter has been an owner of the LA Dodgers since 2012, and bought a majority stake in the Lakers in 2025 before selling the team a year later for a record $12.5 billion. Federal prosecutors and the SEC are investigating whether Walter and his executives concealed financial connections while moving billions of dollars between companies.', TRUE, FALSE),
('5c9a3d75-86e5-412d-948d-5e2eadba20da', 'Lynsi Snyder', 'Lynsi', 'Snyder', 'United States', 'In-N-Out Burger', 'Food & Beverage', 'Lynsi Snyder is the heir to beloved West Coast chain In-N-Out Burger, which her grandparents founded in 1948. She became a billionaire in 2017 on her 35th birthday, when she received the final portion of her inheritance, an additional stake in the chain. Snyder''s uncle and father, both previous In-N-Out presidents, died young; age 17 in 1999, Snyder was the last family heir. She steadily received stakes in the business for a decade as part of a complex trust created by her grandparents. Snyder took on the top job of president in 2010 and has since expanded the number of In-N-Out restaurants by more than 150 locations.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d430ed96-120f-4d73-b585-975cc79bbe5a', 'Horst Julius Pudwill', 'Horst', 'Pudwill', 'Germany', 'Manufacturing', 'Manufacturing', 'Horst Julius Pudwill is cofounder and chairman of Techtronic Industries, a Hong Kong-based manufacturer of power tools and floor-care products. The company produces the iconic vacuum cleaner Hoover, which many people use as a verb (such as in the phrase "hoover the carpet"). Pudwill was an engineer at Volkswagen in Germany before transferring to Hong Kong in the mid-1970s to become a general manager. Pudwill cofounded Techtronic in 1985 with Roy Chi Ping Chung. He continues to oversee Techtronic''s operations with his son, Stephan, the firm''s vice chairman.', TRUE, FALSE),
('fe57d80f-6d5d-4cfb-b040-cac666409b33', 'Frederik Paulsen', 'Frederik', 'Paulsen', 'Sweden', 'Health care', 'Healthcare', 'Frederick Paulsen inherited small drugmaker Ferring Pharmaceuticals, founded by his father in 1950. When he took over running the business in 1983, it generated $15 million in annual revenue. Today the biotech outfit, which makes infertility, obstetrics, urology, gastroenterology and endocrinology drugs, has estimated sales of $2.2 billion. Ferring employs more than 6,500 people and has subsidiaries in nearly 60 countries. Board members include H?l?ne Ploix, former director of the IMF, and Alexandra, the Countess of Frederiksborg, a former Danish princess.', TRUE, FALSE),
('8dcdfd83-80d0-4550-8cd0-4bf372b2d060', 'Juergen Blickle', 'Juergen', 'Blickle', 'Germany', 'Auto parts', 'Manufacturing', 'Juergen Blickle and his brother Rainer own SEW-Eurodrive, a manufacturer specializing in drive-automation and power-transmission solutions. The company, acquired by his father, Ernst, in 1945, now employs more than 19,000 people and generates around $3.7 billion in annual revenue. Its motor, gear and electronic components power conveyors, lifts and other applications in contexts ranging from auto assembly to commercial baking. In the U.S., it operates a manufacturing plant in Lyman, South Carolina, and has five regional assembly centers and dozens of technical sales offices.', TRUE, FALSE),
('914f9c33-e642-4ad6-a403-a743b04ef75d', 'Edward Roski Jr', 'Edward', 'Roski', 'United States', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Through his Majestic Realty, Los Angeles-based developer Edward Roski Jr. owns more than 92 million square feet of industrial real estate across the country. Majestic Realty is developing a 441-acre business park on the site of Pennsylvania''s former Bethlehem Steel plant, with tenants including Crayola and Walmart. Roski''s father founded Majestic Realty in 1948. Roski Jr. helped lead development of the Staples Center in downtown L.A., and is a minority owner of the L.A. Kings. In 2016, Roski and his wife, Gayle, announced a $25 million gift to endow an eye institute at the University of Southern California, where they met as undergraduates.', TRUE, FALSE),
('f6ee5be9-db73-4731-b416-04078dc25a8f', 'Zhou Chaonan', 'Zhou', 'Zhou', 'China', 'Manufacturing', 'Manufacturing', 'Zhou Chaonan is the chairman of Range Intelligent Computing Technology Group, a provider of data center services. Zhou worked as a teacher briefly before finding a job at a state-owned logistics hub in her home town of Hengyang in Hunan Province. She then worked for various state-owned firms for almost two decades, and didn''t launch her own business until 2000 -- when Zhou was already in her 40s. Zhou officially set up Range in 2009. The company went public on the Shenzhen Stock Exchange in a backdoor listing in 2022. Zhou''s son, Li Li, is CEO and vice chairman of Range, while his wife, Zhang Xian, serves as deputy general manager.', TRUE, FALSE),
('575ec68b-a0d6-453f-a871-c12517e2a35c', 'Howard Lutnick & family', 'Howard', 'Lutnick', 'United States', 'Finance', 'Finance & Investments', 'Donald Trump tapped Howard Lutnick to co-chair his transition team, then named him America''s 41st secretary of commerce. Lutnick lost both parents as a teenager, leaving him and his two siblings to take care of each other. After graduating from Haverford College, he got a job at the Wall Street firm of Cantor Fitzgerald, where he became a favorite of founder Bernie Cantor and eventually took control of the firm. The September 11, 2001 attack on the World Trade Center killed 658 of Cantor Fitzgerald''s 960 New York employees, including Lutnick''s younger brother, Gary.  Thanks to an electronic trading business and savvy dealmaking, Lutnick rebuilt his empire, which employed more than 14,000 people by the time he joined the Trump administration in 2025.', TRUE, FALSE),
('e5ed8c32-81b6-4d1b-897f-e02ec01dbf2f', 'Li Ping', 'Li', 'Li', 'Hong Kong', 'Batteries', 'Energy', 'Li Ping is the vice chairman of Contemporary Amperex Technology (CATL), a supplier of batteries for electric vehicles founded in 2011. CATL, dual-listed in Hong Kong and Shenzhen, supplies batteries to automakers including BMW, Geely and Tesla. Despite repeated pushbacks amid geopolitical concerns, a Ford battery factory in Michigan that licenses technologies from CATL has been completed in June 2026.', TRUE, FALSE),
('47df5187-e8c5-458c-b7d2-e219e5afef86', 'Blair Parry-Okeden', 'Blair', 'Parry-Okeden', 'United States', 'Media, automotive', 'Media & Entertainment', 'Blair Parry-Okeden inherited a 25% stake in Cox Enterprises in 2007 when her mother, Barbara Cox Anthony, passed away. Cox Enterprises is a billion dollar (sales) communications, automotive and media company based in Atlanta; it owns cable TV firm Cox Communications. Blair''s brother, Jim Kennedy, is chairman emeritus of the company. Her grandfather, James M. Cox, founded the company in 1898 with the purchase of the Dayton Evening News newspaper.', TRUE, FALSE),
('7295f4c6-0e6f-464e-a902-4a94743c3915', 'Jim Kennedy', 'Jim', 'Kennedy', 'United States', 'Media, automotive', 'Media & Entertainment', 'The Cox family owns media and automotive company Cox Enterprises, which had $23.1 billion in 2025 revenues.  Based in Atlanta, Georgia the privately held company is family owned and operated. James M. Cox founded the company in 1898.  Kennedy''s grandfather, James M. Cox, founded Cox Enterprises in 1898 when he purchased the Dayton Evening News.  Kennedy''s first job at the company was as a production assistant in the newspaper division in 1972.  He inherited his 25% stake in Cox Enterprises from his mother, Barbara Cox Anthony, who died in 2007.', TRUE, FALSE),
('b38fad84-405b-4770-9674-d3dab875eca1', 'Wang Xin', 'Wang', 'Wang', 'China', 'PCB drill bit', 'Manufacturing', 'Wang Xin is the chairman and general manager of Guangdong Dtech Technology, the world''s largest PCB drill bit manufacturer by sales volume.  Wang worked as an accountant for a local PCB manufacturer in Guandong before starting her entrepreneurial business. 											 The company went public in Shenzhen in 2022 and became dual-listed in Hong Kong in July 2026. Wang''s husband, Lin Xia, and her brothers, Wang Xuefeng and Wang Junfeng, are active in the business.', TRUE, FALSE),
('0deea00a-750a-43c4-91d1-683a67f13b53', 'Paul Singer', 'Paul', 'Singer', 'United States', 'Hedge funds', 'Finance & Investments', 'Hedge fund magnate Paul Singer is known for his high-profile, and often combative, dealmaking. He founded his hedge fund firm, Elliott Management, in 1977 with $1.3 million. The firm now has more than $80 billion in assets under management.  He famously spent 15 years warring with the government of Argentina over bond payments, which resulted in a $2.4 billion payout to his firm in 2016. Elliott took over beleaguered soccer club AC Milan in 2018 and sold it for $1.2 billion to RedBird Capital Partners in 2022. Singer frequently donates to Jewish and pro-Israel causes, including BBYO and Hillel. He''s given roughly $300 million to his foundation since 2010.', TRUE, FALSE),
('b9863dce-9b0f-4f3b-b178-9772bcc180aa', 'Mike Hollingshead & family', 'Mike', 'Hollingshead', 'United States', 'Concrete', 'Construction & Engineering', 'Mike Hollingshead is founder and chairman of $3.5 billion (2025 revenue) concrete maker Smyrna Ready Mix (SRM).  He started the company with his wife in 1999, when he built his first concrete plant in his Smyrna, Tennessee backyard.  SRM is now the largest producer of ready mix concrete in the U.S., with 18.7 million cubic yards produced in 2025.  Hollingshead''s son Jeff has served as CEO since 2014. Jeff''s younger brother Ryan runs the company''s small but growing aggregates (otherwise known as rock, sand and gravel) division.   Hollingshead and his immediate family own 100% of SRM.', TRUE, FALSE),
('930a7b6a-b73f-47d3-a38c-13df9bd364be', 'Jim Davis & family', 'Jim', 'Davis', 'United States', 'New Balance', 'Manufacturing', 'Jim Davis bought a small Boston shoemaker in 1972 and turned it into $9.2 billion (2025 sales) New Balance.  Davis is the chairman of New Balance, and his wife Anne, who joined the company in 1977, is the vice chairman. Davis and his family own an estimated 95% of the privately held company. New Balance is known for its running shoes but also makes footwear, clothing and equipment for baseball, lacrosse, and soccer, as well as lifestyle fashion. He got his start working for his father''s restaurants as a "lumper" carrying trays.', TRUE, FALSE),
('c2badc11-123b-4b49-8841-b0f23a27544e', 'Neal Blue & family', 'Neal', 'Blue', 'United States', 'Defense', 'Manufacturing', 'Neal Blue is chairman and CEO of General Atomics, a defense company based in San Diego. The company is best known as the manufacturer of the Predator drone, one of the first drones to fly over Afghanistan after 9/11. The largest private government contractor in the U.S., GA''s clients include foreign nations such as Italy, Spain, and the UAE. With his brother Linden, he bought the then nuclear energy company from Chevron for a reported $60 million in 1986. After graduating from Yale, Blue served in the U.S. Air Force as a nuclear weapons custodian.', TRUE, FALSE),
('5ad90748-a60c-4e02-b5ed-d6bef677106d', 'Albert Avdolyan', 'Albert', 'Avdolyan', 'Russia', 'Oil, mining', 'Energy', 'Albert Avdolyan owns Far East and Siberian coal mining and gas companies.
 Avdolyan got the investment capital from selling stakes in the Russian telecommunications companies Megafon and Yota. Two billion tons of coking are proven reserves of the largest in Russia basin Elga. Avdolyan is the major shareholder of the company that keeps the license on extracting coal there. In 2022 he started construction of a private railroad from coal deposits in Yakutia to the future port on the Sea of Okhotsk, the Pacific railway. Its length is about 500 kilometers.', TRUE, FALSE),
('24f28255-c396-43d4-9dd0-fc848d177d6e', 'Kerry Stokes', 'Kerry', 'Stokes', 'Australia', 'Construction equipment, media', 'Diversified', 'Kerry Stokes took a winding path en route to earning a fortune with his SGH (formerly Seven Group Holdings), which has media, construction and mining assets. He started his career selling Caterpillar tractors and trucks in Australia and eventually China, before moving into media with Seven Group. In 2021 he retired as chairman of Seven Group Holdings. In 2024, SGH acquired ASX-listed concrete and asphalt maker Boral for A$4.4 billion.   His son Ryan Stokes is the CEO and managing director of SGH.', TRUE, FALSE),
('a913d15f-4236-4e18-bfac-2b7b50dfc41a', 'Teddy Sagi', 'Teddy', 'Sagi', 'Israel', 'Gambling software', 'Gambling & Casinos', 'Teddy Sagi founded gambling software developer Playtech in 1999. It has revenue of more than $1 billion and is traded on London''s stock exchange. Sagi sold a 12% slice of Playtech for almost $400 million in 2016; he sold the rest for $88 million in November 2018. He has taken 4 companies public on London''s AIM: Playtech, Market Tech, online payments processor SafeCharge and cybersecurity company Kape. Sagi took Market Tech (now Labtech London) private in July 2017; it owns a portfolio of London property including tourist hot spot Camden Market. In 2019, he sold SafeCharge to Canadian company, Nuvei for $889 million. His other investments include co-working spaces and technology startups.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d2d03d4b-420c-4d46-ade4-70f984361131', 'Rick Caruso', 'Rick', 'Caruso', 'United States', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Rick Caruso is a Los Angeles real estate developer who has built some of the country''s most successful shopping centers. Caruso ran for mayor of Los Angeles in 2022 and advanced to the run-off, where he lost to former Democratic Rep. Karen Bass. Three of Caruso''s retail centers--The Grove, The Americana and Palisades Village--rank among the 15 largest in the country in sales per square foot. The grandson of Italian immigrants, Caruso opened a retail center in 1992 and has more recently expanded into residential, office and hospitality. In 2020, Caruso served on both White House and state-level task forces on how to safely reopen the economy after Covid-19.', TRUE, FALSE),
('1a5f0309-85e3-48bd-81ff-6afdcf156a1a', 'Daryl Katz', 'Daryl', 'Katz', 'Canada', 'Pharmacies', 'Diversified', 'Daryl Katz amassed a fortune in the pharmacy business, buying the Canadian rights to U.S. franchise Medicine Shoppe in 1991. 
 A few years later he snatched up struggling Canadian drugstore chain Rexall, then expanded to the U.S. market. Katz, the son of a drug store owner,  has since sold off all of his pharmacy operations, pivoting his Katz Group to real estate and entertainment. He has been co-developing a $2 billion, 25-acre complex in Edmonton''s downtown that will include offices, condos and retail, among others. Katz also owns his native city''s NHL team, the Edmonton Oilers.', TRUE, FALSE),
('99683edb-7b5e-46dc-b1da-c89cfbde249a', 'Alexandra Schoerghuber & family', 'Alexandra', 'Schoerghuber', 'Germany', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Alexandra Schoerghuber oversees private family investment company Schoerghuber Unternehmensgruppe, as chairwoman of the group''s supervisory board. It has stakes in a brewery co-owned with Heineken and in Arabella Hospitality, a hotel joint venture with Marriott. The group also owns one of Germany''s largest real estate companies, Bayerische Bau und Immobilien GmbH, which builds, owns and manages properties. Its Productos del Mar Ventisqueros S.A., based in Puerto Montt, Chile, specializes in the cultivation and processing of salmon. Alexandra is the widow of Stefan Schoerghuber. He inherited a fortune built by his father, Joseph, and died unexpectedly in 2008, at age 47.', TRUE, FALSE),
('67cdddd6-d2a5-4dd5-a69d-1a41fdf5367b', 'Robert Bass', 'Robert', 'Bass', 'United States', 'Oil, investments', 'Energy', 'Robert Bass and his brothers inherited $2.8 million each from their oil tycoon uncle Sid Richardson in 1959. Robert has helped launch a half dozen investment shops including his Oak Hill Advisors. Bass'' private jet start-up Aerion collapsed in 2021 amid reported financial difficulties. With his wife Anne, Bass has given at least $70 million to Duke and $55 million to Stanford.', TRUE, FALSE),
('27dc0ea7-2ac4-48e3-b205-15a3f52c7d25', 'Kjeld Kirk Kristiansen', 'Kjeld', 'Kristiansen', 'Denmark', 'Lego', 'Manufacturing', 'Third-generation owner of Lego, Kjeld Kirk Kristiansen led the toy company known for its interlocking plastic bricks from 1979 to 2004. He and his three grown children together evenly split ownership of a 75% stake in the $7.2 billion (sales) business. He stepped down from Lego''s board in 2019. His son Thomas, Lego''s deputy chairman, will replace him as chair of family holding company Kirkbi in 2023. His grandfather Ole, a carpenter, started making wooden toys in his workshop in 1932 before moving into plastic in the 1940s. The family also owns about half of theme park operator Merlin Entertainments, which it took private with a consortium in 2019.', TRUE, FALSE),
('4e4b64ba-bdb7-4b53-9f5c-7acfef6453c2', 'Ronda Stryker', 'Ronda', 'Stryker', 'United States', 'Medical equipment', 'Healthcare', 'Ronda Stryker is a director of Stryker Corp., the medical equipment company founded by her grandfather, Homer Stryker (d. 1980). She owns about 4% of Stryker Corp. which she inherited from her parents; she is the only one of her siblings to serve on the board. In 2011, she and her husband gave $100 million to create the Homer Stryker medical school at Western Michigan University.<br> In 2016 the couple pledged $20 million to the Harvard Medical School Department of Global Health and Social Medicine to support equitable health care. Stryker and her husband donated $30 million to Spelman College in 2018, the largest gift from living donors in the institution''s history.', TRUE, FALSE),
('7a516145-ae55-4815-a51b-d6a9b4e67aba', 'Ion Stoica', 'Ion', 'Stoica', 'United States', 'Data analytics', 'Technology', 'Ion Stoica is cofounder and executive chairman of software startup Databricks, which private investors valued at $190 billion in August. He served as the original CEO from its inception in 2013 until early 2016, when he ceded the position to cofounder Ali Ghodsi. Prior to Databricks, Stoica cofounded video streaming startup Conviva. He is also a UC Berkeley computer science professor. Stoica cofounded Databricks alongside six UC Berkeley academics who had built the popular data analytics engine Apache Spark. Databricks is built on top of the Apache Spark framework and uses AI to help companies store and utilize their data.', TRUE, FALSE),
('c5bc1ed2-adbe-402d-bce7-de8ee00dbb84', 'Matei Zaharia', 'Matei', 'Zaharia', 'United States', 'Data analytics', 'Technology', 'Matei Zaharia is cofounder and chief technology officer of software startup Databricks, which private investors valued at $190 billion in August. He is the mastermind behind popular analytics engine Apache Spark, which was conceived when he was a 24-year-old Ph.D. student at UC Berkeley. Spark set a world record for speed of data sorting in 2014 and won Zaharia an award for the year''s best computer science dissertation. In 2013, Zaharia and six UC Berkeley collaborators cofounded Databricks, whose software is built on top of Spark. He has led development on multiple new, AI-powered features beyond Spark.', TRUE, FALSE),
('c51ef05b-669b-4240-909c-5c65541b0f7d', 'Edythe Broad & family', 'Edythe', 'Broad', 'United States', 'Homebuilding, insurance', 'Diversified', 'Edythe Broad is an American art collector and philanthropist. She was married to billionaire businessman Eli Broad from 1954 until his death in 2021. Known for their philanthropy, Edythe and Eli established two foundations that support medical research, public education and the visual and performing arts. The foundations, which have been awarding grants for over 50 years, have pledged or given away more than $4 billion to date.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d82e96fe-12b5-4546-ad3b-48372683f80d', 'Joe Lewis', 'Joe', 'Lewis', 'United Kingdom', 'Investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Lewis is a British businessman who owns the Tavistock Group, a company with more than 200 assets across 13 countries.  Through Tavistock, Lewis owns Premier League soccer team Tottenham Hotspurs and has a stake in U.K. pub operator Mitchells & Butlers.  He pleaded guilty to insider trading charges in 2024 for sharing information with his pilots and ex-girlfriend but was later pardoned by Trump in 2025, paying a $5 million fine.  Born above a pub in London''s East End, Lewis helped his family build a catering business. He sold it and became a currency trader.  He is now living on his yacht, Aviva, in the Bahamas.', TRUE, FALSE),
('b81e4fdc-121f-4ea0-9369-7b52a1f343ee', 'Robert Clark', 'Robert', 'Clark', 'United States', 'Construction', 'Construction & Engineering', 'Robert Clark is the founder and executive chairman of Chicago-based construction firm Clayco, which he started in 1984 as a college dropout. The St. Louis native owns most of the company and built it into a $7.6 billion (2024 revenue) U.S. construction giant. Clayco''s projects include the Washington University School of Medicine and several Amazon e-commerce centers. Clark briefly stepped down as Clayco''s executive chairman in September 2021 to become the commissioner general for the U.S. pavilion at Expo 2020 Dubai.', TRUE, FALSE),
('7b2f2f0f-5226-4dd6-b733-1b2e08008854', 'Miguel Krigsner', 'Miguel', 'Krigsner', 'Brazil', 'Cosmetics', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Bolivian-born Miguel Krigsner founded Grupo Boticario, Brazil''s second-largest cosmetics company behind number one, Natura. Grupo Boticario operates in more than 50 countries; Krigsner individually owns approximately 80% of the business. His brother-in-law Artur Grynbaum joined as a financial assistant and worked his way up to president of the group by 2008. He owns about 20% of the group. In 1990 Krigsner created the Boticario Group Foundation dedicated to environmental protection, which receives about 1% of Grupo Boticario''s net income annually. Today, Krigsner and Grynbaum serve as president and vice president, respectively, of the Grupo Boticario advisory board.', TRUE, FALSE),
('274f1907-0024-4a73-8c66-e0693be10252', 'Philip Ng', 'Philip', 'Ng', 'Singapore', 'Real Estate', 'Real Estate', 'Philip Ng and his brother Robert control Far East Organization, Singapore''s largest private landlord and property developer. The group was founded by their father Ng Teng Fong, who moved from China to Singapore in 1934 and came to be known as "The King of Orchard Road." Their Hong Kong arm, Sino Group, is run by older sibling Robert and his son Daryl, while Philip oversees the Singapore interests. Singapore-listed Far East Orchard repurposed the century-old former Westminster Fire Station in London into a luxury development with 17 apartments and put it on sale in 2022.', TRUE, FALSE),
('a38350b7-6cec-47d2-9224-77f5548e0342', 'Jayshree Ullal', 'Jayshree', 'Ullal', 'United States', 'Computer networking', 'Technology', 'Jayshree Ullal has been president and CEO of Arista Networks, a computer networking firm, since 2008. The publicly traded company generates more than $9 billion in annual revenue. Ullal studied electrical engineering at San Francisco State University and engineering management at Santa Clara University. She did stints at Cisco Systems, semiconductor firm Advanced Micro Devices and Fairchild Semiconductor before joining Arista when it had no revenues and fewer than 50 employees. Ullal owns around 2% of Arista''s stock, some of which is earmarked for her two children, niece and nephew, and sits on the board of cloud computing company Snowflake.', TRUE, FALSE),
('273853e3-3204-4ed1-9e61-f9c9ac88fa4d', 'Vincent Bolloré & family', 'Vincent', 'Bolloré', 'France', 'Investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Vincent Bollore runs his family''s conglomerate Bollore Group, which was founded in 1822 as a paper manufacturer of cigarettes wrappers and bibles. After a quick stint at Edmond de Rothschild bank, Bollor? took control of the struggling group in 1981 and turned it into a global giant. The group, which is active in media, advertising, shipping, construction and logistics, owns a majority stake in telecom conglomerate Vivendi. In 2018, French officials reportedly launched an investigation into Vincent Bollore''s dealings for alleged corruption. His group denied involvement. In December 2019, Vivendi agreed to sell a 10% stake in its Universal Music Group to billionaire Ma Huateng''s Tencent Holdings.', TRUE, FALSE),
('82b6c83d-91af-411d-bd0d-265730fab4d5', 'Ding Shizhong', 'Ding', 'Ding', 'China', 'Sports apparel', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Ding Shizhong is the chairman of Hong Kong-listed Anta Sports, one of China''s largest homegrown sportswear companies. It sells under a range of brands such as Anta, Fila, Descente and Kolon Sport, as well as labels like Arc''teryx and Salomon that were acquired through a $5.2 billion deal in 2019. The company has kept expanding its portfolio of western athletic brands through mergers and acquisitions. In 2026, Anta agreed to purchase a 29% stake in German sportswear brand Puma from France''s billionaire Pinault family for $1.8 billion. Its subsidiary Amer Sports went public on the New York Stock Exchange in 2024, raising $1.4 billion. His older brother Ding Shijia, who serves as the company''s deputy chairman, is also a billionaire.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d71c0ee0-4101-40cc-afce-7587d284fc40', 'Venu Srinivasan', 'Venu', 'Srinivasan', 'India', 'Two-wheelers', 'Automotive', 'Venu Srinivasan is chairman emeritus of TVS Motor Company, India''s third-largest maker of two-wheelers. TVS Motor is the flagship of the TVS Group, which was founded in 1911 by T. V. Sundaram Iyengar. Srinivasan belongs to the third generation. The Chennai company has three factories in India and one each in Indonesia and the U.K. His son Sudarshan Venu, who was managing director, took over as chairman of TVS Motor in August 2025.', TRUE, FALSE),
('139d8b5c-515b-430b-836d-119db83447a4', 'Mike Adenuga', 'Mike', 'Adenuga', 'Nigeria', 'Telecom, oil', 'Diversified', 'Mike Adenuga built his fortune in telecommunications and oil production. His mobile phone network, Globacom, is the third-largest operator in Nigeria, with more than 17 million subscribers. His oil exploration outfit, Conoil Producing, operates 6 oil blocks in the Niger Delta. Globacom also built Glo-1, a 6,100-mile-long submarine Internet cable to the U.K. via Ghana and Portugal. Adenuga also owns 74% of publicly traded gasoline firm Conoil and just under 6% of publicly traded Nigerian bank Sterling Financial Holding.', TRUE, FALSE),
('5f9c46c9-f6c1-479b-939e-fb12b494ac52', 'Jeremy Jacobs Sr & family', 'Jeremy', 'Jacobs', 'United States', 'Food service', 'Service', 'Jeremy Jacobs is chairman of concessions juggernaut Delaware North, a private company that serves 500 million people per year across four continents. The business was founded in 1915 by his father, who began by selling popcorn and peanuts The New York-based company is currently considered a global leader in hospitality management & food service management. Jacobs is also the owner of the NHL''s Boston Bruins ice hockey team, and he was inducted into the Hockey Hall of Fame in 2017. In early 2019, Jacobs began handing control of the Boston Bruins team and Delaware North to his six children.', TRUE, FALSE),
('790164f5-e8da-4da3-b25e-a811ba48882e', 'Ronald Wanek', 'Ronald', 'Wanek', 'United States', 'Furniture', 'Manufacturing', 'Ronald Wanek is the founder of America''s largest home furniture manufacturer and retailer, Ashley Furniture. Wanek grew up poor on a dairy farm in Minnesota, where his grandfather and great uncle built furniture as a hobby.
 He started his first furniture manufacturing business, Arcadia Furniture, in 1970 with a loan from his father and money he got from selling his home. Six years later he bought retailer Ashley Furniture, which had been around since the 1940s. He is chairman of Ashley Furniture; his son Todd, also a billionaire, has been CEO since 2002.', TRUE, FALSE),
('aed170ea-b1b5-4b57-ace3-7c1cb130873a', 'Wu Jianshu', 'Wu', 'Wu', 'Hong Kong', 'Auto parts', 'Automotive', 'Wu Jianshu is the chairman of Ningbo Tuopu Group, a supplier of vibration control, acoustic and suspension systems for the auto industry. Founded in 1983, Tuopu today supplies automakers including Audi, BMW and BYD. The company has expanded into humanoid robotics sector, supplying components such as actuators and sensors.  Wu''s son, Wu Haonian, is the company''s vice chairman.', TRUE, FALSE),
('c3f20e09-b7ae-4e92-9471-623d59cbdecc', 'Evangelos Marinakis & family', 'Evangelos', 'Marinakis', 'Greece', 'Shipping, soccer', 'Logistics', 'Evangelos Marinakis owns shipping group Capital Maritime Trading Corp. as well as a media conglomerate and stakes in several soccer teams. Through his Capital Maritime Trading Corp. he owns several private shipping firms, as well as a 59% stake in publicly traded Capital Clean Energy Carriers. He bought 80% for English soccer team Nottingham Forest in 2017. Under his ownership, the firm was promoted to the English Premier League in 2022. He also owns 86% of Olympiacos, Greece''s most successful soccer team, and invested in Portuguese soccer team Rio Ave in November 2023. Marinakis owns Alter Ego Media, a Greek media group that owns two of the country''s largest newspapers plus the second-largest TV channel; he took it public in 2025.', TRUE, FALSE),
('be00a504-2e98-4c25-99e0-fa1d3738869f', 'Clive Calder', 'Clive', 'Calder', 'United Kingdom', 'Record label', 'Media & Entertainment', 'Clive Calder became a billionaire in 2002, when he sold his music company Zomba Group to German mass media corporation Bertlesmann for $2.7 billion. The crown jewel of his empire was Jive Records, the record label behind many of the first commercially successful hip hop artists. The South Africa native founded Zomba in London in 1975, then opened an office in New York City in 1978. Known for shunning the spotlight, Calder now lives in the Cayman Islands with his wife. He frequently travels to parts of Africa for charity, and his ELMA Philanthropies works on improving childhood education and health on the continent.', TRUE, FALSE),
('ef16bbdf-087b-4650-9360-2533a74d668d', 'Robert Ng', 'Robert', 'Ng', 'Singapore', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Robert Ng and his brother Philip control Far East Organization, Singapore''s largest private landlord and property developer. The group was founded by their father Ng Teng Fong, who moved from China to Singapore in 1934 and came to be known as "The King of Orchard Road." Their Hong Kong arm, Sino Group, is run by older sibling Robert''s son Daryl, while Philip oversees the Singapore interests. Singapore-listed Far East Orchard repurposed the century-old former Westminster Fire Station in London into a luxury development with 17 apartments and put it on sale in 2022.', TRUE, FALSE),
('e40909bd-77d8-4849-aa9c-d2be8c9d92d7', 'Mark Cuban', 'Mark', 'Cuban', 'United States', 'Online media, Dallas Mavericks', 'Media & Entertainment', 'Mark Cuban founded video portal Broadcast.com with fellow Indiana University alum Todd Wagner in 1995 and sold it to Yahoo for $5.7 billion in 1999. Today he owns a minority stake in the NBA''s Dallas Mavericks and is cofounder of Cost Plus Drugs, which he launched in January 2022 with the aim of lowering prescription drug prices.  Cuban sold 58% of the Dallas Mavericks in December 2023 for an estimated $2 billion (pre-tax).  He sold stamps door-to-door as a kid and gave disco lessons to help pay his way through Indiana University.
 Cuban was inspired to strike out on his own when he was fired from a software shop for closing a $15,000 sale instead of cleaning up the store.', TRUE, FALSE),
('ebc96e65-2a83-4694-b8bb-b57c9cbc04c7', 'Radovan Vitek', 'Radovan', 'Vitek', 'Czech Republic', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Real estate mogul Radovan Vitek got his start during Slovakia''s voucher privatization in the 1990s. He moved to the Czech Republic in 1997, where he took over a cooperative and turned the headquarters into a luxury hotel. His CPI Property Group owns 1 million square meters of lucrative real estate in Berlin, Germany. CPI also has property in Budapest, Croatia, the Cote d''Azure and Poland including  shopping centers.', TRUE, FALSE),
('08181010-1751-4b33-a8cb-065dbe31ed5b', 'Andrei Skoch & family', 'Andrei', 'Skoch & family', 'Russia', 'Metals and mining', 'Metals & Mining', 'Andrei Skoch is a partner in Russian investment group, USM, and has been a member of the State Duma, Russia''s legislative body, since 1999. He and his former partner, Lev Kvetnoi, were born in a settlement near Moscow and studied at the same athletics school, Institute of Physical Culture. The partners merged their business with that of billionaire Alisher Usmanov. Kvetnoi later sold out. As a member of the Duma, he isn''t allowed to own stakes in businesses so his shares in USM are held by his father Vladimir and his daughter Varvara. Skoch was sanctioned by the U.S. in 2018 for "longstanding ties to Russian organized criminal groups," which he has denied. The EU and U.K. sanctioned him in 2022.', TRUE, FALSE),
('183ed7c2-c590-476e-b60f-bed3865e3050', 'Carlos Alberto Sicupira & family', 'Carlos', 'Sicupira', 'Brazil', 'Beer', 'Food & Beverage', 'Carlos "Beto" Sicupira is a co-founder and partner in private equity firm 3G Capital, best known for its investments in Anheuser-Busch InBev and Restaurant Brands International, parent of Burger King and Canadian coffee chain Tim Hortons. Sicupira''s billionaire partners in 3G include fellow Brazilians Jorge Paulo Lemann, Marcel Herrmann Telles and Alex Behring. Most of Carlos "Beto" Sicupira''s wealth comes from his shares of Anheuser-Busch InBev, the world''s largest brewer, in which he owns about a 3% stake. 3G sold its stake in U.S. condiment maker Kraft-Heinz in 2024 after 11 years.  In 2021, 3G acquired 75% of Dutch window shade company Hunter Douglas in a $7 billion transaction, and in 2025 paid almost $10 billion for U.S sneaker brand Skechers.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6bb27b22-6779-4c84-a782-e17667cd77bc', 'Ricardo Faria', 'Ricardo', 'Faria', 'Brazil', 'Eggs', 'Food & Beverage', 'Ricardo Faria founded Global Eggs (known in Brazil as Granja Faria) in 2018 when he started buying up farms across Brazil.  The company reached an $8 billion valuation in 2026 when it secured a $1 billion investment from New York-based private equity firm Warburg Pincus. In 2025, Global Eggs acquired Pennsylvania-based Hillandale Farms for $1.1 billion.	 Faria, who majored in agronomic engineering, got his entrepreneurial start when he founded a laundry company for hotel linens and uniforms in 1997. He sold it to French group Elis nearly 20 years later for almost $400 million. Faria is the CEO and owns 82% of the Luxembourg-based company.', TRUE, FALSE),
('c6f08ac7-7aa8-4b39-89dc-01a129c8c551', 'Stephen Smith', 'Stephen', 'Smith', 'Canada', 'Finance and investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Stephen Smith is a Canadian financial services magnate. Smith cofounded mortgage lender First National Financial in 1988, just four years after being personally bankrupt. He also owns about half of Canada Guaranty Mortgage Insurance Company and a stake in publicly traded Canadian bank EQB. He acquired lender Home Trust for more than $1.2 billion in 2023 and merged it with Fairstone Bank of Canada in early 2025. Smith has donated more than $100 million to Queen''s University, where the business school is named after him.', TRUE, FALSE),
('c2c04d8c-b389-415e-9bd0-44ed2f4931f7', 'John Brown', 'John', 'Brown', 'United States', 'Medical equipment', 'Healthcare', 'John Brown ran Stryker Corp., a medical device and software company, for 32 years before retiring as chairman in 2009. Stryker''s revenues climbed from $17 million to $6.7 billion under Brown''s leadership. He led the IPO of Stryker in 1979. Brown is chairman emeritus of Stryker''s board and owns slightly more than 5% of the company. Stryker Corp. was founded by orthopedic surgeon Dr. Homer Stryker from Kalamazoo, Michigan in 1941, who made devices to help with procedures. Brown sat on the board of St. Jude Medical until it was acquired by Abbott Labs in January 2017.', TRUE, FALSE),
('8ffff10b-6fb8-4fbc-ac7b-8f9157ae9d8e', 'Baiju Bhatt', 'Baiju', 'Bhatt', 'United States', 'Stock trading app', 'Finance & Investments', 'Baiju Bhatt cofounded no-fee stock trading app Robinhood in 2013 with his friend Vlad Tenev. Bhatt was co-CEO of Robinhood until late 2020, then chief creative officer before stepping down in 2024. He remains a board member.  Since its launch, Robinhood''s no-commission trading model has revolutionized the brokerage industry. Robinhood went public on the Nasdaq exchange in 2021 at a $32 billion valuation.  Bhatt owns around 6% of the company.', TRUE, FALSE),
('7be5e4c0-5f1c-4d2f-ac16-dedb538c6c64', 'Liu Debing', 'Liu', 'Liu', 'China', 'AI', 'Technology', 'Liu Debing is the chairman of Chinese AI firm Z.AI. Also known as Zhipu, the company went public in Hong Kong in January 2026, raising $560 million. The AI model developer, which sells its services in China and Southeast Asia, previously raised funding from investors including Ant Group, Tencent and Qiming Venture Partners. The firm was added to the U.S. government''s entity list in 2025, barring it from acquiring advanced American technology.', TRUE, FALSE),
('f85e1434-4060-4035-bfbd-5b87c61b7f8d', 'Dmitry Rybolovlev & family', 'Dmitry', 'Rybolovlev', 'Russia', 'Fertilizer', 'Manufacturing', 'Rybolovlev'' built his fortune in Uralkali, Russia''s largest producer of potassium fertilizers, during the 1990s privatization era. He sold his stake in Uralkali for $6.5 billion in 2010 and doesn''t appear to have any business in Russia these days. He has spent roughly $1 billion on property in Europe, including Greek island Skorpios and $400 million Monaco penthouse La Belle Epoque. After a nasty years-long divorce battle, Rybolovlev was ordered to pay his ex-wife $605 million. In Oct. 2015 they reached an undisclosed settlement. Rybolovlev sued art dealer Yves Bouvier, who had helped him buy 38 works for $2 billion. In December 2023 they reached a settlement, ending a nine-year feud.', TRUE, FALSE),
('8b660446-e478-4755-84d2-20e121b42c2c', 'Mitchell Morgan & family', 'Mitchell', 'Morgan', 'United States', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Mitchell Morgan is the founder, chairman and owner of Conshohocken, Pennsylvania-based Morgan Properties, the second-largest owner of apartments in the U.S. Morgan Properties owns more than 350 properties with over 97,000 units in 20 states. Morgan founded the company in the Philadelphia suburb of King of Prussia in 1985 with a partner and took sole ownership in 1996. Morgan Properties'' first major deal was the 2007 acquisition of a 17,000-unit portfolio from the Kushner Companies for $1.9 billion alongside AIG. Before entering the real estate business, Morgan worked as an accountant while taking night classes to earn a law degree at Temple University.', TRUE, FALSE),
('571792e7-7339-4b7c-ab85-0a07bb4ccbdc', 'Ding Shijia', 'Ding', 'Ding', 'China', 'Sports apparel', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Ding Shijia is the deputy chairman of Hong Kong-listed Anta Sports, one of China''s largest homegrown sportswear companies. It sells under a range of brands such as Anta, Fila, Descente and Kolon Sport, as well as labels like Arc''teryx and Salomon that were acquired through a $5.2 billion deal in 2019. The company has kept expanding its portfolio of western athletic brands through mergers and acquisitions. In 2026, Anta agreed to purchase a 29% stake in German sportswear brand Puma from France''s billionaire Pinault family for $1.8 billion. Its subsidiary Amer Sports went public on the New York Stock Exchange in February 2024, raising $1.4 billion. Ding''s younger brother Ding Shizhong, Anta''s chairman, is also a billionaire.', TRUE, FALSE),
('bf24c6a9-f3f7-448d-b02f-38e87942581d', 'Pavel Durov', 'Pavel', 'Durov', 'United Arab Emirates', 'Messaging app', 'Technology', 'Pavel Durov is the founder and owner of messaging app Telegram, which has more than 1 billion monthly active users worldwide. Telegram, which is free to use, competes with messaging apps like Facebook''s WhatsApp. Durov left Russia after refusing to cooperate with the secret service and provide encrypted data of his first social network''s users. Telegram was banned in Russia from 2018 to 2021. In 2026, Russia charged Durov with aiding in terrorism and put him on an international wanted list. He was accused of failing to remove certain channels on Telegram, which were allegedly being used as a conduit for Ukrainian forces to recruit Russians and promote acts of terrorism.  Durov became a French citizen in 2021 but lives in Dubai.', TRUE, FALSE),
('f7feee8e-6680-482e-adb5-dab62bece3b5', 'Christiane Schoeller', 'Christiane', 'Schoeller', 'Germany', 'Publishing', 'Media & Entertainment', 'Christiane Schoeller is the only child of Holtzbrinck Publishing Group heir Monika Schoeller, who passed away in 2019. She holds a 50% stake. Monika and her brothers, Stefan and Dieter von Holtzbrinck, inherited the business, which includes Macmillan Publishers, from their father, Georg. In 2006, Dieter sold his shares to his siblings, leaving them each with 50% of the company, originally founded as a book club in 1948. Holtzbrinck''s venture investments have included many internet and e-commerce startups, such as Zalando, Groupon, HelloFresh and Rocket Internet. Christiane and her partner, a former publisher and designer from Stuttgart, keep a low profile.', TRUE, FALSE),
('b80d82a2-e3f5-42a6-8f05-8ceb0b2059c9', 'Stefan von Holtzbrinck', 'Stefan', 'von Holtzbrinck', 'Germany', 'Publishing', 'Media & Entertainment', 'Stefan von Holtzbrinck, his brother Dieter and sister Monika Schoeller inherited Holtzbrinck Publishing Group from their father, Georg. Originally founded as a book club in 1948, Holtzbrinck''s businesses include Macmillan Publishers, S. Fischer Verlag and Holtzbrinck Digital. In 2006, Dieter sold his shares to his siblings, leaving each of them with 50% of the company. Monika died in 2019. Holtzbrinck Ventures (now HV Capital) was founded in 2000 as an investment arm of the publishing business and became independent in 2010. HV has invested in many internet and e-commerce startups including Zalando, Groupon, HelloFresh and Rocket Internet.', TRUE, FALSE),
('954e0f0a-160a-40e9-bb50-86d59d5426e5', 'Donald Trump', 'Donald', 'Trump', 'United States', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Donald Trump has presided over the most lucrative presidency in American history, adding billions to his net worth, largely by cashing in on crypto.  Much of Trump''s fortune remains in real estate, which has struggled in recent years as interest rates increased, shoppers moved online and office workers headed home.  He also owns golf courses, mansions, a winery and a 1991 Boeing 757 nicknamed Trump Force One.  A New York judge ordered Trump to pay $454 million after the attorney general accused him of lying about his net worth for years to make himself look more creditworthy. An appeals court overturned the penalty in 2025. Trump got his start working for his father, Fred, who developed low-cost housing in Brooklyn and Queens.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d1011172-e543-4e65-a03b-659cc49ba15d', 'Rahul Bhatia', 'Rahul', 'Bhatia', 'India', 'Aviation', 'Service', 'Rahul Bhatia''s biggest asset is a stake in InterGlobe Aviation, whose IndiGo is India''s biggest airline by market share. IndiGo, which he cofounded with billionaire airline veteran Rakesh Gangwal in 2006, has a 64% domestic market share (as of November 2025). It has a fleet of more than 400 aircraft and flies to 140 destinations, including 44 overseas. Its CEO, Pieter Elbers, was the former CEO of KLM. In 2019,  Bhatia and Gangwal had a public falling out over how IndiGo is run. In 2022, Gangwal stepped down from the board and has been gradually selling his stake since. His privately held InterGlobe Enterprises has a joint venture with logistics giant UPS called Movin.', TRUE, FALSE),
('3957b738-9dba-41cc-9ee3-dbfc29299719', 'Charles B. Johnson', 'Charles', 'Johnson', 'United States', 'Franklin Templeton', 'Finance & Investments', 'Charles Johnson is the second largest shareholder in Franklin Resources, a global investment management firm also known as Franklin Templeton Investments. Johnson became CEO at age 24 in 1957, a decade after his father, Rupert Johnson Sr., founded the company. Johnson spent 56 years at the company before handing over the chairman''s post to his son, Gregory, in 2013. His daughter Jennifer, a champion of the company''s data science capabilities and fintech initiatives, became CEO in 2020. Under his leadership, the firm''s assets under management rose from $2.5 million in 1957 to more than $800 billion when he retired.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d09c2e39-531b-41e6-b864-d66f17e867c9', 'Michael Otto', 'Michael', 'Otto', 'Germany', 'Retail, real estate', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Michael Otto inherited shares in the retail empire his late father, Werner Otto, founded as a mail-order business in Hamburg in 1949. As chief executive, he ran his family''s Otto Group for 26 years until 2007. He is now chairman of its supervisory board. With revenues exceeding $15 billion, Otto Group has more than 40 companies in retail (including Crate and Barrel), real estate and financial services. Michael''s stepmother Maren and her children Alexander and Katharina -- all billionaires -- also own stakes in Otto Group. Separate from Michael, they own ECE Group, a real estate company focused on shopping centers, and a stake in office property firm Paramount Group.', TRUE, FALSE),
('63271b93-130b-4a5e-955b-9e9a43d1f415', 'Chen Tao & family', 'Chen', 'Chen', 'China', 'Hardware', 'Technology', 'Chen Tao is the chairman of Victory Giant Technology, which specializes in printed circuit boards.  The company''s products are widely used in artificial intelligence, data centers, automobiles, aerospace, medical devices and industrial industries. Prior to his entrepreneurial journey, Chen served as an officer in the People''s Armed Police. His brother Chen Yong is a director and vice president at the company.', TRUE, FALSE),
('44df9fae-2f98-4155-92f2-891b595cbbb7', 'Mark Scheinberg', 'Mark', 'Scheinberg', 'Canada', 'Online gambling', 'Gambling & Casinos', 'Mark Scheinberg cofounded PokerStars with his father, Isai, and built it into the world''s biggest online poker company before cashing out in 2014. Scheinberg, who owned 75% of parent business Rational Group at the time, pocketed more than $3 billion from the sale. He helped launch PokerStars in 2001, at age 28, and benefited tremendously from the poker boom that soon swept the U.S. and the rest of world. Scheinberg has invested some of his proceeds from the sale in luxury hospitality assets through his real estate investment vehicle, Mohari. His real estate investments include a stake in the Ritz-Carlton Yacht Collection, a historic Madrid hotel and a luxury resort in Costa Rica.', TRUE, FALSE),
('5b2a52ea-ee14-4ce1-a0e4-a76c019cdc80', 'Wang Xing', 'Wang', 'Wang', 'China', 'Food delivery', 'Technology', 'Wang Xing is the chairman and CEO of Hong Kong-listed Meituan, which was created through a 2015 merger of Groupon-like group buying site Meituan and Yelp-like Dianping.com. Wang cofounded China''s first college social network xiaonei.com, which was sold to Oak Pacific  Interactive in 2006. After growing Meituan into a food-delivery heavyweight in mainland China, Wang is also expanding in regions including Hong Kong, the Middle East and Latin America. Wang in 2021 transferred shares at the time worth more than $2 billion to his foundation amid a China antitrust investigation.', TRUE, FALSE),
('473d048f-8025-4aeb-bb4c-363350c3637b', 'Rudolf Maag', 'Rudolf', 'Maag', 'Switzerland', 'Medical devices', 'Healthcare', 'Rudolf Maag''s fortune stems from medical devices. Maag got an M.B.A. from Insead in 1973 and began working his way up the corporate ladder at pharmaceutical company Sandoz AG of Switzerland. He later moved to dental giant Straumann, where in 1990 he bought out the medical device division and later took it public as Stratec Medical. In 1999 he merged Stratec with Swiss medical device powerhouse Synthes and built up a 15% stake, which was later sold to Johnson & Johnson.', TRUE, FALSE),
('4f2d06a8-e67f-46ba-9f6c-874a4f78acbd', 'Yip Sum Yin', 'Yip', 'Yip', 'Hong Kong', 'Printed circuit boards', 'Technology', 'Yip Sum Yin is the chairman and general manager of Jiangxi Redboard Technology, a producer of printed circuit boards (PCB). Its products are used in tech heavyweights such as Huawei, Amazon, Google and Microsoft. He set up Redboard in 2005 and took it public on the Shanghai Stock Exchange in April 2026. He is also cofounder of Hong Kong-listed PCB maker Same Time Holdings, which was acquired by Chinese solar module manufacturer GCL Technology Holdings in 2014.', TRUE, FALSE),
('c690a7dc-7e40-4425-8529-917391409222', 'Eric Lefkofsky', 'Eric', 'Lefkofsky', 'United States', 'Groupon, investments', 'Technology', 'Eric Lefkofsky made his fortune from the daily deals site Groupon, which he founded in 2008 with  Andrew Mason and Brad Keywell. Lefkofsky founded and now runs healthcare company Tempus AI, which uses data to improve cancer treatment.  Tempus went public at a $6 billion valuation in 2024. Lefkofsky also cofounded VC firm Lightbank, which has made investments in over 100 companies, including social media firm Sprout Social. He grew up outside of Detroit and went to the University of Michigan for his undergraduate and law degrees.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d3ee23c0-25c8-4798-8f46-07ea0d62dde0', 'Jon Yarbrough', 'Jon', 'Yarbrough', 'United States', 'Gambling machines', 'Gambling & Casinos', 'Jon Yarbrough started Video Gaming Technologies, which produced casino games, in 1991. The business grew due to the proliferation of tribal casinos; Yarbrough says he''s worked with around 35 tribes in 100-plus locations over the years. Yarbrough sold his company to Australian firm Aristocrat Leisure in 2014 for about $1.3 billion. These days he manages his investments, which include real estate and tech stocks, through his family office Yarbrough Capital.', TRUE, FALSE),
('eb3abf23-0ef8-4f06-a5e6-fef7f04fe999', 'Robert Hale Jr', 'Robert', 'Hale', 'United States', 'Telecom', 'Telecom', 'Robert Hale is the founder and CEO of wholesale telecommunications provider Granite Telecommunications. Hale founded Granite in 2002, less than six months after his previous company, Network Plus, filed for bankruptcy. The company provides voice, data and other communications services to businesses and governmental agencies in the U.S. and Canada. Granite generated over $1.7 billion in sales in 2025, servicing over 1.8 million voice and data lines.  Hale has personally donated over $470 million toward cancer research, educational institutions and other charitable causes.', TRUE, FALSE),
('93192c1e-9129-4f95-ad39-cdb86b890fcb', 'Zhang Congyuan', 'Zhang', 'Zhang', 'Taiwan', 'Shoes', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Zhang Congyuan is the chairman of Huali Industrial Group, a shoe manufacturer he founded in 2004. The company now has factories in China, Indonesia, Vietnam, Dominica and Myanmar. Huali supplies to dozens of brands including Nike, Puma, UGG and Vans. Zhang also cofounded Hong Kong-listed shoemaker Symphony Holdings, but sold his stake and is no longer with the company. He shares the fortune with his wife and children.', TRUE, FALSE),
('c8e0c134-334c-4ab5-a14d-4cd9c2604127', 'Alain Merieux & family', 'Alain', 'Merieux', 'France', 'Pharmaceuticals', 'Healthcare', 'Alain Merieux is chairman of Institut Merieux, a medicine and public health conglomerate specializing in diagnostics, immunotherapy and nutrition. Alain''s grandfather, Marcel Merieux, founded the institute in 1897. Alain founded BioMerieux, one of the firm''s publicly traded arms, which specializes in diagnostic tests for infectious diseases such as tuberculosis. The firm''s other publicly-traded subsidiary, Transgene, develops vaccines to combat infectious diseases and cancers. Alain''s third son Alexandre, who shares the fortune, was named CEO of BioMerieux in 2014.', TRUE, FALSE),
('0a909e04-d6cc-4ac4-a2ee-e8f5a01e2f71', 'Arnon Milchan', 'Arnon', 'Milchan', 'Israel', 'Movie making', 'Media & Entertainment', 'Arnon Milchan owns film and TV production company New Regency Enterprises. New Regency has produced hits like Pretty Woman, Mr. and Mrs. Smith, The Revenant, Birdman and Bohemian Rhapsody. Milchan transformed his family''s bankrupt fertilizer company, which he took over in 1962 at the age of 21, into a $125 million business. He was a business student, professional soccer player and consultant for weapons systems between Israeli Defense Forces and U.S. defense contractors. Milchan has been ensnared in the corruption probe into Israeli prime minister Benjamin Netanyanhu, but will reportedly not be charged with wrongdoing.', TRUE, FALSE)
