 He expanded into home linen, focusing on the export market, with customers such as Walmart and Macy''s. His Welspun Corp is one of the largest pipe companies in the world. His wife Dipali runs listed home textiles maker Welspun Living.', TRUE, FALSE),
('dfe48823-659e-4312-85ca-89b58ce0f1fa', 'Angelo Koo', 'Angelo', 'Koo', 'Taiwan', 'Finance', 'Finance & Investments', 'Angelo Koo owns a significant stake in KGI Financial Holding, formerly known as China Development Financial Holding, a major financial services firm in Taiwan with subsidiaries such as KGI Securities and CDIB Capital Group. Angelo is the chairman and CEO of CDIB Capital Group. He left the position as president of KGI Financial in 2009 amid an insider trading probe.  KGI Financial took Taiwan''s China Life Insurance private in 2021 and rebranded it as KGI Life. Angelo is the seventh-generation of the Koo Family that trace their roots to Koh Lay Huan, the first Kapitan Cina of Penang. The family first made their fortune in camphor, salt, sugar and land and founded the Koos Group. Angelo''s brothers, Andre and Jeffrey Jr., are also billionaires and own stakes in Taiwan''s financial giants Chailease Holding and CTBC Financial Holding, respectively.', TRUE, FALSE),
('eb37d0e9-1fe5-457a-bc1d-bf688edec234', 'Cen Junda', 'Cen', 'Cen', 'China', 'Pharmaceuticals', 'Healthcare', 'Cen Junda''s fortune stems from his stakes in Jiangsu Hengrui Pharmaceuticals and Hansoh Pharmaceutical Group. China-based Hansoh operates a research center in the U.S. state of Maryland. He holds degrees from Zhejiang University and the China State Institute of Pharmaceutical Industry.', TRUE, FALSE),
('e9dfe387-4bed-4a45-9fc5-09ba55541f73', 'Jiang Bin', 'Jiang', 'Jiang', 'China', 'Acoustic components', 'Technology', 'Jiang Bin is the chairman of Goertek, a leading supplier of acoustic components in China. The company is a key supplier of AirPods to Apple. Goertek plans to spin off its semiconductor subsidiary Goertek Microelectronics for a Hong Kong IPO and filed its prospectus in July 2025. His younger brother Jiang Long, also a billionaire, serves as Goertek''s vice chairman.', TRUE, FALSE),
('349a4b26-f3d1-4169-8b07-5d8d449e4b6c', 'Claudio Del Vecchio', 'Claudio', 'Del Vecchio', 'Italy', 'Eyeglasses', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Claudio Del Vecchio is one of six children of Leonardo Del Vecchio, the late chairman (d. 2022) of EssilorLuxottica, the world''s largest eyeglasses firm. He inherited a 12.5% stake in his father''s Luxembourg-based holding company Delfin after his death, along with his stepmother and six siblings. Besides EssilorLuxottica, Delfin also owns shares in insurer Generali; banks Monte dei Paschi di Siena and UniCredit; and real estate developer Covivio. Claudio served as Luxottica''s co-CEO in the 1990s and took the company public on the New York Stock Exchange in 1990. He acquired Brooks Brothers, America''s oldest clothing retailer, in 2001; the firm filed for bankruptcy in September 2020.', TRUE, FALSE),
('58c1b496-ce84-4e07-b8b7-5a7bd386f19e', 'Shapoor Mistry', 'Shapoor', 'Mistry', 'Ireland', 'Diversified', 'Diversified', 'Shapoor Mistry controls the 160-year-old engineering and construction giant Shapoorji Pallonji Group. His late brother Cyrus was chairman of Tata Sons for four years until October 2016, when he was ousted. The family''s biggest asset is an 18.4% stake in Tata Sons, holding outfit of the $180 billion (revenue) Tata Group. Mistry suffered a double loss in 2022: his father and group patriarch Pallonji Mistry died in June. Three months later his younger brother Cyrus Mistry died in a car crash at age 54. Shapoor and Cyrus were jointly working to restructure the debt-laden family business by selling key assets.', TRUE, FALSE),
('39cd6855-e8f9-4a78-8c12-4348861e06ff', 'Matthias Reinhart', 'Matthias', 'Reinhart', 'Switzerland', 'Financial services', 'Finance & Investments', 'Matthias Reinhart is chairman and majority shareholder of VZ Holding Ltd., a Swiss financial services company he took public in 2007. After getting his MBA at University of St. Gallen, he worked at McKinsey & Co. in Zurich and Chicago before co-founding VZ in 1993. VZ''s key proposition: bringing transparency to a market that made it hard for customers to compare the prices and benefits of financial products. The firm does not broker financial products; instead, customers pay a fee for advisory and portfolio-management services.', TRUE, FALSE),
('0564f1a5-0757-44ef-ba22-fad67eba4719', 'Michel Leclercq & family', 'Michel', 'Leclercq', 'France', 'Sporting goods', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Michel Leclercq set up a small sporting goods store called Decathlon in 1976. It''s now one of the world''s largest athletic retailers with more than $16.5 billion in sales from more than 1,700 stores in 60 countries. Leclercq is cousin of Gerard Mulliez, the patriarch of the famed French retail dynasty behind Auchan department stores. Leclerq and his immediate family own approximately 40% of the company; the extended Mulliez family own about 40% as well.', TRUE, FALSE),
('3cb58124-ed69-4a28-9264-334df4581d73', 'Chen Bang', 'Chen', 'Chen', 'China', 'Hospitals', 'Healthcare', 'Chen Bang is the chairman of Aier Eye Hospital Group, China''s largest ophthalmology chain by the number of outlets.  The Changsha-based company operates more than 800 eye hospitals and centers in China, Europe, Southeast Asia and the U.S. Already traded on the Shenzhen Stock Exchange, Aier in May 2026 filed for a dual listing in Hong Kong.  Chen dabbled in property and beverage distribution until meeting a retired ophthalmologist, who inspired him to open his own hospitals.', TRUE, FALSE),
('464c196f-7c7f-4a02-8ba1-73152256f383', 'Steven Klinsky', 'Steven', 'Klinsky', 'United States', 'Investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Steve Klinsky founded the $55 billion (assets) investment firm New Mountain Capital in 1999.  Klinsky rose to become one of the top partners at Forstmann Little, an early private equity titan, before striking out on his own. One of the buyout industry''s top performers, New Mountain Capital specializes in private equity, private credit and real estate. Its private equity business, known for buying and growing small and midsized companies through acquisitions, has never had an investment default. Klinsky''s wife, Maureen Sherry, is a former Bear Stearns banker who, in 2016, published "Opening Belle," a fictionalized account of a woman navigating crisis-era Wall Street.', TRUE, FALSE),
('4e1ca36b-919a-4313-bf00-e221f74d704d', 'Paul Foster', 'Paul', 'Foster', 'United States', 'Oil refining', 'Energy', 'Texas-based Paul Foster built a fortune in oil refining.  In 2017, he sold his company Western Refining to San Antonio-based Tesoro for $6.4 billion. The merged entity was later renamed Andeavor and sold to Marathon Petroleum.  Through Franklin Mountain Investments, Foster owns stakes in more than 30 companies spanning real estate, restaurants and sports. In 2025, he sold his energy venture for $2.5 billion. A graduate of Baylor University and a registered CPA, Foster handled the books for small oil refineries across the Southwest. He and his partners took over bankrupt El Paso Refining in 1992. He bought out his partners five years later.', TRUE, FALSE),
('1d94dda3-e7ec-4c9a-be60-6e052920ce6a', 'Marisa Del Vecchio', 'Marisa', 'Del Vecchio', 'Italy', 'Eyeglasses', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Marisa Del Vecchio is one of six children of Leonardo Del Vecchio, the late chairman (d. 2022) of EssilorLuxottica, the world''s largest eyeglasses firm. She inherited a 12.5% stake in her father''s Luxembourg-based holding company Delfin after his death, along with her stepmother and six siblings. Besides EssilorLuxottica, Delfin also owns shares in insurer Generali; banks Monte dei Paschi di Siena and UniCredit; and real estate developer Covivio. She is one of three children Del Vecchio had with his first wife, Luciana Nervo, along with her siblings Claudio and Paola. Marisa leads the Museum of Optics in Agordo, the northern Italian town where her father founded Luxottica in 1961.', TRUE, FALSE),
('63f9d865-b422-4a25-b855-a02c2712fa5f', 'Clemente Del Vecchio', 'Clemente', 'Del Vecchio', 'Italy', 'Eyeglasses', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Clemente Del Vecchio is one of six children of Leonardo Del Vecchio, the late chairman (d. 2022) of EssilorLuxottica, the world''s largest eyeglasses firm. He inherited a 12.5% stake in his father''s Luxembourg-based holding company Delfin after his death, along with his stepmother and six siblings. Besides EssilorLuxottica, Delfin also owns shares in insurer Generali; banks Monte dei Paschi di Siena and UniCredit; and real estate developer Covivio. He is one of two children Del Vecchio had with Sabina Grossi, Luxottica''s former head of investor relations, along with his brother Luca. After inheriting his stake in his father''s fortune in 2022, Clemente became the world''s youngest billionaire at age 18.', TRUE, FALSE),
('de557372-13ef-4afa-b571-1ad93bcf8360', 'Luca Del Vecchio', 'Luca', 'Del Vecchio', 'Italy', 'Eyeglasses', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Luca Del Vecchio is one of six children of Leonardo Del Vecchio, the late chairman (d. 2022) of EssilorLuxottica, the world''s largest eyeglasses firm. He inherited a 12.5% stake in his father''s Luxembourg-based holding company Delfin after his death, along with her stepmother and six siblings. Besides EssilorLuxottica, Delfin also owns shares in insurer Generali; banks Monte dei Paschi di Siena and UniCredit; and real estate developer Covivio. He is one of two children Del Vecchio had with Sabina Grossi, Luxottica''s former head of investor relations, along with his brother Clemente.', TRUE, FALSE),
('603eca7d-8742-4a0e-b564-f22e43494269', 'Nicoletta Zampillo', 'Nicoletta', 'Zampillo', 'Italy', 'Eyeglasses', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Nicoletta Zampillo is the widow of Leonardo Del Vecchio, the late chairman (d. 2022) of EssilorLuxottica, the world''s largest eyeglasses firm. She inherited a 12.5% stake in Del Vecchio''s Luxembourg-based holding company Delfin after his death, along with her two kids and five stepchildren. Besides EssilorLuxottica, Delfin also owns shares in insurer Generali; banks Monte dei Paschi di Siena and UniCredit; and real estate developer Covivio. Zampillo and Del Vecchio first married in 1997 and both already had children from an earlier marriage; they later divorced and then remarried in 2010. Zampillo''s two children, Rocco Basilico, who she had with her ex-husband Paolo Basilico, and Leonardo Maria Del Vecchio, both work at EssilorLuxottica.', TRUE, FALSE),
('2d0404ac-70ce-43b3-99e2-70981d2dbf76', 'Paola Del Vecchio', 'Paola', 'Del Vecchio', 'Italy', 'Eyeglasses', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Paola Del Vecchio is one of six children of Leonardo Del Vecchio, the late chairman (d. 2022) of EssilorLuxottica, the world''s largest eyeglasses firm. She inherited a 12.5% stake in her father''s Luxembourg-based holding company Delfin after his death, along with her stepmother and six siblings. Besides EssilorLuxottica, Delfin also owns shares in insurer Generali; banks Monte dei Paschi di Siena and UniCredit; and real estate developer Covivio. She is one of three children Del Vecchio had with his first wife, Luciana Nervo, along with her siblings Claudio and Marisa.', TRUE, FALSE),
('3080a821-91cf-48c7-bf15-9ad674c0834d', 'Rocco Basilico', 'Rocco', 'Basilico', 'Italy', 'Eyeglasses', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Rocco Basilico is the stepson of Leonardo Del Vecchio, the late chairman (d. 2022) of EssilorLuxottica, the world''s largest eyeglasses firm. He inherited a 12.5% stake in Del Vecchio''s Luxembourg-based holding company Delfin after his death, along with his mother and six siblings. Besides EssilorLuxottica, Delfin also owns shares in insurer Generali; banks Monte dei Paschi di Siena and UniCredit; and real estate developer Covivio. Basilico is one of only two Del Vecchio heirs to work at the company; he is EssilorLuxottica''s chief wearables officer and head of luxury brands.', TRUE, FALSE),
('2d3300b3-3afc-4959-ae08-ec6de335d20c', 'Georg Nemetschek & family', 'Georg', 'Nemetschek', 'Germany', 'Software', 'Technology', 'Georg Nemetschek is the founder and deputy chairman of publicly traded German software company Nemetschek Group. He started using design software in his own engineering office in the late 1960s, long before computers became available for personal use. The company, which serves the architecture, engineering and construction industries, went public in 1999 and has annual revenue of about 1 billion euros. Nemetschek Group expanded into 3D animation and motion design, securing access to the media industry. Its software has around six million users. In 2020, Georg launched the Nemetschek Innovation Foundation to support scientific research and artificial intelligence in the construction industry.', TRUE, FALSE),
('9bdffc3f-a571-48f9-a0c7-d5486fb30404', 'Naguib Sawiris', 'Naguib', 'Sawiris', 'Egypt', 'Telecom', 'Telecom', 'Naguib Sawiris is a scion of Egypt''s wealthiest family. His brothers  Nassef and Samih are also billionaires. He built a fortune in telecom, selling Orascom Telecom in 2011 to Russian telecom firm VimpelCom (now Veon) in a multibillion-dollar transaction. He''s chairman of Orascom TMT Investments, which has stakes in an asset manager in Egypt and Italian internet company Italiaonline, among others. He also developed a luxury resort called Silversands on the Caribbean island of Grenada.', TRUE, FALSE),
('3e9a7062-c37f-4878-a002-5b78e6e61b06', 'Robert Low', 'Robert', 'Low', 'United States', 'Trucking', 'Logistics', 'Robert Low is the founder and CEO of New Prime, Inc., a privately held trucking carrier with over 10,000 drivers. Prime is the leading provider of refrigerated trucks with over 6,500 temperature-controlled trucks hauling everything from meat and yogurt to flowers and pharmaceuticals. Raised on a farm in rural Missouri, Low founded Prime in 1970 when he was 19 after buying his first truck to help fund his college studies.  After surviving Chapter 11 bankruptcy in the early ''80s, Low reinvented Prime by making its drivers into independent contractors.  He and his wife Lawana Low are Prime''s only two shareholders. The company generated an estimated $2.5 billion in revenue in 2025.', TRUE, FALSE),
('26e8d790-f108-4281-8b9c-9ab2a399d0f1', 'Dan Kurzius', 'Dan', 'Kurzius', 'United States', 'Email marketing', 'Technology', 'Dan Kurzius founded what later became Mailchimp with Ben Chestnut in 2001 as a side project to their web design company. Mailchimp''s email marketing software for small businesses garnered enough customers that in 2007 they committed to it full time. Wary of giving up control to outside investors, Kurzius and Chestnut bootstrapped growth from profits and took no outside money. In 2021, Intuit announced it would acquire Mailchimp in a $12 billion cash and stock acquisition. At the time of announcement, Chestnut and Kurzius each owned 50% of the Atlanta-based company, which had $800 million in 2020 revenue.', TRUE, FALSE),
('1cdae3bb-0c04-41c2-a77f-faf31e9b9793', 'Chandru Raheja', 'Chandru', 'Raheja', 'India', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'One of four brothers of a property family, Chandru Raheja ventured out on his own in 1996. Today his privately held K. Raheja Corp. is one of Mumbai''s leading developers and is run by his sons Neel and Ravi. Raheja is known for its IT parks, hotels, malls and department store chain, Shoppers Stop. His Chalet Hotels, which owns a string of hotels such as the J.W. Marriott in Mumbai and the Westin in Hyderabad, was listed in 2019. In 2020, Raheja listed part of his commercial properties, co-owned with private equity firm Blackstone, under the Mindspace Business Parks REIT.', TRUE, FALSE),
('fc051ec4-8aef-4764-9331-e6a7b979b661', 'Thomas Tull', 'Thomas', 'Tull', 'United States', 'Movies, investments', 'Media & Entertainment', 'Former film financier and founder of production company Legendary Entertainment, Thomas Tull''s biggest hits came from backing blockbusters. In 2015, Tull inked a deal with Chinese billionaire Wang Jianlin''s Wanda Group to sell Legendary for up to $3.5 billion in cash, stock and debt. Tull has his hands in a variety of industries, including real estate, financial services, tech, and bio-science. He rolled several of his firms into a new joint venture, TWG Global, and owns shares in publicly traded scrubs maker Figs and high-tech makeup company Oddity.  A sports fan, Tull owns minority stakes in the Pittsburgh Steelers and the New York Yankees along with a collection of baseball memorabilia.', TRUE, FALSE),
('79491e45-333b-41be-b8f2-41bce5bae915', 'Gary Rollins & family', 'Gary', 'Rollins', 'United States', 'Pest control', 'Service', 'Gary Rollins is executive chairman emeritus of $3.8 billion (2025 sales) Rollins Inc., the biggest pest control company by revenues in North America. He ran the company with his brother, Randall Rollins, until Randall''s death in 2020. The company was founded by Rollins'' father Wayne (d. 1991) and uncle John (d. 2000), who made an early fortune with regional radio stations and bought bug-killing giant Orkin for $62 million in 1964.  The family has unloaded $2.6 billion of Rollins Inc. stock since 2023. They still own about 35% of the publicly traded company. In 2010, Gary Rollins'' children sued their father and uncle, alleging the two were blocking access to trusts and denying them their rightful cash allocations. The family settled the matter in 2019.', TRUE, FALSE),
('aeec8cde-7a0c-475c-ad78-e1e23ba49b0a', 'Margarita Louis-Dreyfus & family', 'Margarita', 'Louis-Dreyfus', 'Switzerland', 'Commodities', 'Food & Beverage', 'Margarita Louis-Dreyfus is the majority owner and chairwoman of agricultural commodities giant Louis-Dreyfus. Her husband Robert Louis-Dreyfus died of leukemia in 2009, leaving her a 70% stake in the business, which was founded in 1851. She reportedly pledged her shares to take out a $1 billion loan in 2019 to buy out minority stakes owned by family members. In 2021, she sold a 45% stake in the company to Abu Dhabi-based investment firm ADQ. In 2016, she sold French soccer team Olympique Marseille to former Los Angeles Dodgers owner Frank McCourt, but held onto a 5% stake.', TRUE, FALSE),
('f81d5503-5cda-426c-be55-3ef2ae0c21d4', 'John Sall', 'John', 'Sall', 'United States', 'Software', 'Technology', 'John Sall cofounded statistical software firm SAS with James Goodnight in 1976. The two partners met at North Carolina State, where Sall was studying graduate-level statistics and Goodnight was pursuing his Ph.D. SAS saw more than $3 billion in revenue in 2024 and has more than 83,000 customers, including banks, government agencies and insurance companies. SAS offers employees generous workplace perks, including an on-site health care center, pharmacy and daycare services. Sall and his wife, Ginger, have given nearly $280 million to their Sall Family Foundation, which invests in the environment, public health and science.', TRUE, FALSE),
('388d8960-bd5f-4011-bc1a-2c13f7ed5a7d', 'Bob Gaglardi & family', 'Bob', 'Gaglardi', 'Canada', 'Hotels', 'Real Estate', 'Bob Gaglardi founded Northland Properties, which has interests in hotels, restaurants, sports and construction. Gaglardi launched the business in 1963 with a $5,000 loan, opening his first Sandman Inn hotel four years later in British Columbia. He continued to put up Sandman Inns throughout Canada, plus expanded into real estate and restaurants. In 2011 he and his son, Tom, purchased the then-bankrupt Dallas Stars NHL team in a $240 million deal; Forbes now values the team at $2 billion.', TRUE, FALSE),
('13ac2f03-8aeb-4039-bcdb-9d838043dc2a', 'Mitchell Rales', 'Mitchell', 'Rales', 'United States', 'Manufacturing, investments', 'Manufacturing', 'Mitchell Rales and his brother Steven acquired a real estate investment trust in 1983 and merged it into the firm Danaher. Over the years they acquired more than three dozen companies and turned Danaher into an industrial firm with nearly $25 billion in 2025 revenue.	  Mitchell Rales serves as chairman of Danaher''s executive committee.  Rales is also a minority owner of the NFL''s Washington Commanders.  In 2021, he and his brother each transferred Danaher shares worth more than $1.5 billion to their charitable foundations.', TRUE, FALSE),
('47d0d778-72e3-44ae-94a2-ad7afe9c1911', 'Li Hua', 'Li', 'Li', 'China', 'Financial services', 'Finance & Investments', 'Li Hua, who also goes by Leaf, is the chairman and CEO of Futu Holdings, an online financial services business in China. The company initially operated a platform for mainland Chinese investors to trade offshore securities such as Hong Kong and U.S.-listed stocks. Its immense popularity later led to government crackdowns amid worries of capital outflow and data security. Following a 2022 ban that forbade it from signing up new users in mainland China, the company was fined in 2026 $271 million for offering cross-border investments without proper licenses. Li received a personal penalty of $180,000. The company has been seeking growth in international markets including Malaysia, Singapore and the U.S. It was also ordered to wind down its mainland China business, where investors will only be allowed to sell their holdings for the next two years starting from 2026. Li founded Futu in 2007, after a seven-year stint at Chinese internet giant Tencent, where he held senior management positions.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6784be6b-894f-4ef1-ab6a-03eb3910f230', 'Yang Chang-Chih', 'Yang', 'Yang', 'Taiwan', 'Printed circuit board', 'Manufacturing', 'Yang Chang-Chih is the founder of Gold Circuit Electronics, a maker of printed circuit boards for servers and networking equipment. He handed over the chairman position to his son Chen-Tse in 2017. The older Yang still serves as a director. Gold Circuit Electronics listed on the Taiwan Stock Exchange in 1998. The company opened its first Thai plant in 2025 with $40 million investment and is pumping another $40 million into its expansion project. His daughter Chen-Jung also sits on the board.', TRUE, FALSE),
('4bc826bd-38af-4db1-98b4-490d566d080b', 'Lu Weiding', 'Lu', 'Lu', 'China', 'Diversified', 'Diversified', 'Lu Weiding is the chairman of Wanxiang Group, a maker of auto parts with growing interests in clean energy and agriculture. His late father Lu Guanqiu (d. 2017) founded the predecessor of Wanxiang Group in 1969.  Starting from a small blacksmith shop, Guanqiu eventually grew the company to become the first Chinese auto parts supplier that entered the U.S. market.  Lu Weiding is also the chairman of China Wanxiang, a subsidiary in the insurance and fintech sectors.', TRUE, FALSE),
('19aa518c-3b50-474c-897f-845ea57f379f', 'Florentino Perez', 'Florentino', 'Perez', 'Spain', 'Construction', 'Construction & Engineering', 'Florentino Perez runs ACS Group, Spain''s largest construction company.  Perez, who has been CEO since 1997, owns about 15% of the publicly-traded builder. He is currently serving his eighth term as president of fan-owned Spanish soccer team Real Madrid, which has won seven European Cups under his leadership.  Forbes values the Real Madrid soccer team at $9.5 billion, making it the most valuable soccer team in the world. In 2026, Perez boosted his ownership of ACS with a $170 million investment to back the company''s shift into buildings data centers.', TRUE, FALSE),
('2b828e98-97b2-4608-b951-e0e6d671ced1', 'Alejandro Bulgheroni', 'Alejandro', 'Bulgheroni', 'Argentina', 'Oil & gas', 'Energy', 'Alejandro Bulgheroni and his late brother Carlos (d. Sept. 2016) took over Argentine energy company Bridas Corp., founded by their father, in 1985. The Bulgheroni brothers sold a 50% stake in Bridas to China''s state-owned offshore oil company, CNOOC, for $3.1 billion in 2011. In September 2017 BC Energy entered into a cash-free agreement with BP to form Pan American Energy Group, the largest privately-owned integrated energy company in Argentina.  Bulgheroni owns more than 10 vineyards across the world, including Bodegas Garzon in Uruguay, one of the country''s main exporting wineries.  His agro-industrial complex Estancias del Lago has over 13,000 dairy cows producing an average of 550,000 liters of milk a day.', TRUE, FALSE),
('080eb4cd-c9db-4712-ac5e-4c6814f506b6', 'Benu Gopal Bangur', 'Benu', 'Bangur', 'India', 'Cement', 'Manufacturing', 'Cement czar Benu Gopal Bangur gets his wealth from a majority stake in Shree Cement, one of India''s most cost-efficient cement producers. Shree, which was started in 1979 in Jaipur, sells branded cement under the names of Shree Ultra Jung Rodhak, Bangur Cement and Rockstrong. Bangur hails from a storied business clan in Kolkata and got control of Shree Cement in the 1990s after a family split. Today the company is run by his son Hari Mohan, who was appointed chairman in 2022 after Bangur stepped down. His grandson Prashant is vice chairman. In October 2024, Shree Cement signed an agreement with the Indian government''s internal trade department to help manufacturing startups with financial support.', TRUE, FALSE),
('3d7bd6b4-30c5-4fac-bad5-feb41e8ff0fb', 'Andre Koo', 'Andre', 'Koo', 'Taiwan', 'Financial services', 'Finance & Investments', 'Andre Koo is the honorary chairman of Chailease Holding, an equipment-leasing outfit operating in Taiwan, mainland China and Southeast Asia. Chailease comprises over 70 companies with 10,000 employees. It operates in Taiwan, mainland China and 12 other countries and regions. He is the seventh-generation of the Koo Family that trace their roots to Koh Lay Huan, the first Kapitan Cina of Penang. The family first made their fortune in camphor, salt, sugar and land and founded the Koos Group. Andre''s brothers, Jeffrey Koo Jr. and Angelo Koo, are also billionaires and own stakes in Taiwan''s financial giants CTBC Financial Holding and China Development Financial Holding, respectively. Andre Jr. is founder and general partner of K8 Capital, a New York-based private credit and venture capital firm.', TRUE, FALSE),
('abf03cd6-fcf3-4743-b7d4-6864f2ab51a2', 'Helen Johnson-Leipold', 'Helen', 'Johnson-Leipold', 'United States', 'Cleaning products', 'Manufacturing', 'Helen Johnson-Leipold is an heir to family-owned SC Johnson, a privately-held cleaning products company since 1999. Helen is the chairman and CEO of Johnson Outdoors, a publicly-traded company that sells outdoor gear. She is also chairman of the Johnson Financial Group, which includes family-owned Johnson Bank. SC Johnson products include Pledge, Off! and Windex; the company has $11.4 billion in revenues (estimate). Helen and her siblings pledged $150 million to Cornell in 2017 to fund the SC Johnson College of Business.', TRUE, FALSE),
('49f029f6-eb87-4c64-b5b8-c275c6c8fa7d', 'Richard Liu', 'Richard', 'Liu', 'China', 'E-commerce', 'Technology', 'Richard Liu, who also goes by his Chinese name Liu Qiangdong, is the founder and chairman of e-commerce site JD.com. He stepped down as JD.com chief executive in 2022, joining other tycoons in relinquishing top management roles as Beijing seeks to rein in the market influence of large tech firms.  Liu started his career by opening a retail shop to sell electronic gadgets in 1998. He closed it six years later and moved the business online. He also chairs two of JD.com''s Hong Kong-listed units, JD Health and JD Logistics. In 2024, Walmart sold its entire 9.4% stake in JD.com for $3.6 billion, ending an eight-year partnership as the U.S. retail giant shifts to focus on its own operation in China.', TRUE, FALSE),
('7aecf5c6-d297-4c4a-abf5-2e7ffd41638e', 'Joy Alukkas', 'Joy', 'Alukkas', 'India', 'Jewelry', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Son of a jewelry store owner and school dropout, Joy Alukkas went to the Middle East to open the family''s first overseas store in 1987 in Abu Dhabi. He broke off to launch his own jewellery chain, which now has 100 outlets spread across India and 60 overseas. His other interests include a money exchange outfit, malls and real estate. Alukkas'' son John Paul is managing director of the international jewelry business. Alukkas decided to postpone the public listing of the jewelry business in 2023 citing a tepid IPO market.', TRUE, FALSE),
('91ad8738-a4c1-49d6-af53-73af453942eb', 'Heinrich Otto Deichmann', 'Heinrich', 'Deichmann', 'Germany', 'Shoes, retail', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Heinrich Otto Deichmann is chairman of Deichmann SE, one of Europe''s largest shoe retailers with 2024 sales revenue of about $9 billion.  Headquartered in Essen, Germany, the company operates 4,700 locations across 34 countries and employs nearly 50,000 people.  His grandfather Heinrich Deichmann started the business as a shoemaker store in 1913 and ran it with his wife Julie.  Deichmann joined the company in 1989 and became its chairman ten years later; he now owns 80% of the company.  His son Samuel joined the management board in 2020', TRUE, FALSE),
('09a0d03f-ca3c-4e20-809e-bfe8cef9c22c', 'Eric Douglas', 'Eric', 'Douglas', 'Sweden', 'Investments', 'Diversified', 'The son of billionaire Gustaf Douglas, Eric has sat on the board of the family''s investment company Wasatornet for more than a decade. The Douglas family is the largest shareholder of Latour AB, which holds stakes in Securitas AB and Assa Abloy, the world''s largest lock producer. Latour is also the main shareholder in AB Fagerhult, one of the leading European manufacturer of light fixtures and several other public companies. Eric is a board member of Latour AB, chairman of the boards of Pod Investment AB and Sparb''ssan Fastigheter AB, and vice chairman of AB Fagerhult. The Douglas family is one of the largest land owners in Sweden.', TRUE, FALSE),
('5e068b44-4ce3-4217-8bab-1fa2b63dbbe7', 'Pablo Legorreta', 'Pablo', 'Legorreta', 'United States', 'Investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Pablo Legorreta is the founder of Royalty Pharma, the world''s biggest acquirer of pharmaceutical royalty streams. Royalty Pharma, which went public in 2020, has collected revenue slices of blockbuster drugs like Humira, Imbruvica, Lyrica, and Xtandi. A former investment banker at Lazard Frères, Legorreta started Royalty Pharma in New York as a private equity vehicle in 1996. In 2025, Royalty Pharma acquired its external investment manager RP Management in a $1.1 billion deal. Legorreta owned 100% of RPM until 2024, when he gave just under half his stake to employees', TRUE, FALSE),
('c8290ddf-ac51-4910-a858-e12169a28761', 'Dinara Kulibayeva', 'Dinara', 'Kulibayeva', 'Kazakhstan', 'Banking', 'Finance & Investments', 'Dinara Kulibaeva is the daughter of Kazakhstan''s former president, Nursultan Nazarbayev, and  shares a majority of Halyk Bank with her husband, Timur Kulibayev. Their portfolio also includes investments focused on the construction, operation and servicing of oil and gas wells. She benefited from the 2014 sale of Altynalmas Gold to Polymetal, part-owned by Russian billionaire Alexander Nesis, for cash and company shares. Forbes assumes all of Kulibaeva''s assets are owned 50/50 with Timur, giving them an equal net worth. Halyk Bank, based in Almaty, Kazakhstan, is their most valuable holding.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6e40ff14-d1b9-49ce-8df6-cc08cb507138', 'Timur Kulibayev', 'Timur', 'Kulibayev', 'Kazakhstan', 'Banking', 'Finance & Investments', 'Timur Kulibayev is the founder of Altyn Alma, an investment company created in 1992 that later morphed into Almex LLP. An investment in mobile service paid off in 2004, when a company he controlled sold Kar-Tel, operating in Kazakhstan, to VimpleCom for $350 million. In 2014, he sold Altynalmas Gold to Polymetal, part-owned by Russian billionaire Alexander Nesis, for cash and company shares. Kulibayev and his wife, Dinara, own a majority stake in Halyk Bank of Kazakhstan. Kulibayev''s father-in-law is Nursultan Nazarbayev, Kazakhstan''s first president, from 2010 to 2019.', TRUE, FALSE),
('a02b78cc-c6f7-4e8c-8a7f-415399f01677', 'Michal Solowow', 'Michal', 'Solowow', 'Poland', 'Investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Michal Solowow is a Polish investor who got his start in the late 1980s with construction company Mitex, which he sold in 2002 to French investor Eiffage. Solowow then plowed the proceeds into the nascent Polish stock market. Over the past several years he has been taking his companies private, including building materials producers Barlinek and Cersanit. He took his last main listed asset, chemical group Synthos, private in 2018. Solowow has invested in technology startups such as OncoaArendi, a biotech firm that went public in 2018.', TRUE, FALSE),
('e774cba9-7a90-4164-a786-533f010a4dce', 'Ronald Lauder', 'Ronald', 'Lauder', 'United States', 'Estee Lauder', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Ronald Lauder is the youngest son of makeup maven Estée Lauder, who founded her eponymous beauty company in 1946. He became the chairman of Clinique Laboratories in 1994 and still occupies that position today. Lauder spent nearly 50 years as a board member. He stepped off in 2009, but was reelected to the board in 2016 and retired in 2025.  The president of the World Jewish Congress and a Trump donor, Lauder has informally advised the White House on Israel. Lauder served as deputy assistant secretary of defense for NATO affairs from 1983 to 1986 and was ambassador to Austria for one year.', TRUE, FALSE),
('3267fcd5-4320-45f4-9721-04300bf03c42', 'Mario Verrocchi', 'Mario', 'Verrocchi', 'Australia', 'Pharmacies', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Mario Verrocchi opened the first Chemist Warehouse pharmacy store with brothers Jack Gance and Sam Gance in 2000. Today it has over 600 outlets across Australia, New Zealand, China, Dubai and Ireland. Chemist Warehouse dropped its IPO plan in favour of a merger with ASX-listed Sigma Healthcare, which was completed in February 2025. Verrocchi bought a A$40 million historic seaside mansion in 2020.', TRUE, FALSE),
('557c9669-0a89-44ef-8e12-bf23b075bbf6', 'George Lucas', 'George', 'Lucas', 'United States', 'Star Wars', 'Media & Entertainment', '''Star Wars'' creator George Lucas has largely retired from filmmaking since he sold his Lucasfilm to Disney in 2012 for $4.1 billion in stock and cash. Lucas is now focused on philanthropy: his charitable family foundation has more than $1 billion in assets. Lucas attended junior college in his hometown of Modesto, California where his parents ran a stationary store, before attending USC. He founded Lucasfilm, his production company, in 1971 and built his fortune through his movies and their merchandise. The Lucas Museum of Narrative Art will open in Los Angeles in 2026 and is entirely funded by Lucas and his wife, Mellody Hobson.', TRUE, FALSE),
('80ff382b-af7c-48be-a482-a74b99648b70', 'Peter Gassner', 'Peter', 'Gassner', 'United States', 'Software', 'Technology', 'Peter Gassner is the CEO and founder of Veeva Systems, a cloud software provider for pharmaceutical and biotech companies. Before Veeva, Gassner worked at IBM, PeopleSoft and Salesforce. After 4 years at Salesforce, he saw an opportunity to offer software focused on life sciences built on Salesforce''s platform. Gassner started Veeva in 2007 with Matt Wallach, who had a background in tech sales to big pharma. Today Veeva helps companies manage their drug development and commercialization processes. Customers include Abbvie and Pfizer.', TRUE, FALSE),
('40459312-d98a-430a-b6f7-a01a09260b65', 'N. Murray Edwards', 'N.', 'Edwards', 'Canada', 'Oil & gas', 'Energy', 'N. Murray Edwards derives much of his fortune from stakes in Canadian oil and mining companies. His largest investments include oil sands miner Canadian Natural Resources, aerospace firm Magellan and a minority stake in the NHL''s Calgary Flames. A lawyer by training, Edwards made the jump to business at age 28 after promising a dying friend that he would always pursue his passions. He started a merchant bank with partners in the late 1980''s, but they spent half their initial capital on digging a natural gas well that came up dry. Edwards then switched gears and diversified from exploration to investing in existing oil and gas assets.', TRUE, FALSE),
('ec490494-f97f-4904-bd8b-cd7eeeddf41d', 'Zhu Yan & family', 'Zhu', 'Zhu', 'China', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Zhu Yan inherited the fortune held by her late husband Zuo Hui, the KE Holdings founder, after his death in 2021. KE Holdings, which trades in both New York and Hong Kong, is one of the world''s largest real estate brokerage chains. Zuo Hui, a pioneering real estate tycoon, died at age 50 of an undisclosed illness. Zuo formed KE Holdings in 2018 to encompass several companies: Lianjia, Beike and a property financial services firm he''d launched in 2010.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6c8dc947-c413-4068-b831-bcb672f0f958', 'Sofia Högberg Schörling', 'Sofia', 'Högberg Schörling', 'Sweden', 'Investments', 'Diversified', 'Sofia Schorling Hogberg is the daughter of Melker Schorling, the billionaire Swedish investor who died in 2023. Schorling had built up a portfolio of stakes in publicly-traded companies he controlled through the family holding vehicle, Melker Schorling AB. Her sister, Marta Schorling Andreen, is also a billionaire. The two sisters are the majority owners of Melker Schorling AB. Today, the family holding company controls large stakes in stock traded companies Hexagon, AAK, Assa Abloy, Hexpol and Securitas.', TRUE, FALSE),
('aa5ccb6e-5613-4f55-a898-aead7b5e87bb', 'Cai Haoyu', 'Cai', 'Cai', 'China', 'Mobile games', 'Technology', 'Cai Haoyu is a cofounder of Shanghai-based online games developer miHoYo, which he established in 2012 with college friends, Liu Wei and Luo Yuhao. He stepped down as miHoYo chairman in 2023 for unexplained reasons and handed the reins over to Liu, but continued to retain a large stake. Best known for its Genshin Impact adventure game, the company develops products that often feature anime-style characters and rich storylines. Also in 2023, Cai cofounded Anuttacon, which focuses on developing AI-powered games. It released in 2025 Whispers from the Star, an interactive game featuring an AI companion named Stella.  Liu and Luo are both billionaires.', TRUE, FALSE),
('3431758a-49fd-4ec2-977b-3990d3f7f348', 'Andy Mills', 'Andy', 'Mills', 'United States', 'Medical supplies', 'Healthcare', 'Andy Mills is a director and former president of Illinois-based medical supplies giant Medline, which his father and uncle founded in 1966. Mills and his extended family, which includes four other billionaires, own roughly 18% of the company, which IPO''d on the Nasdaq in December 2025 and ended its first trading day with a market cap of more than $55 billion. The Mills family previously sold 79% of Medline to a group of private equity firms in a leveraged buyout that valued the company at more than $30 billion in 2021. Andy Mills served as Medline''s president for 26 years until 2023, while his cousin Charlie Mills served as CEO during that same period. Charlie Mills still serves as the company''s chairman. Andy Mills'' brother-in-law Jim Abrams served as chief operating officer of Medline from 1997 to 2023. The company is now run by non-family executives.', TRUE, FALSE),
('08d5dd00-40ae-4af7-937b-1828e43020f9', 'Bulat Utemuratov', 'Bulat', 'Utemuratov', 'Kazakhstan', 'Mining, banking, hotels', 'Metals & Mining', 'Bulat Utemuratov is a Kazakhstani investor whose investment portfolio includes holdings in the hotel sector and mobile phone companies Kar-tel and Kyrgyzstan''s Sky Mobile. In 2012, he led the sale of mineral company Kazzinc to commodities firm Glencore for $1.4 billion in cash and shares, which he sold in 2021. Utemuratov purchased 88% of Kazakhstan''s Forte Bank for $400 million in 2014. In 2025, the businessman sold The Ritz-Carlton Vienna hotel, the gold mining company RG Gold in Kazakhstan, the Burger King franchise in Kazakhstan, and Sky Mobile LLP in Kyrgyzstan (a mobile operator).
 One of his biggest transactions was the 2007 sale of Kazakhstan''s ATF Bank to Italian bank UniCredit for a reported $2.2 billion', TRUE, FALSE),
('f9f960c6-5658-41a8-b122-03144c6223d6', 'Lynda Resnick', 'Lynda', 'Resnick', 'United States', 'Agriculture', 'Food & Beverage', 'From almonds &amp; oranges in California''s Central Valley to seedless lemons in South Texas, Lynda Resnick and her husband Stewart are worth billions from farming as the world''s leading grower of tree nuts and America''s largest citrus grower. They cofounded and co-own the Wonderful Company, among the largest farming operations in America. As a couple, they share a fortune worth an estimated $11.6 billion.  Lynda dropped out of college at 19 to start her own ad agency. Stewart came to her looking for marketing help.
 Both previously divorced, they met in the 1970s when she provided marketing help for a burgeoning janitorial business. Lynda focuses on philanthropy; the Resnicks have pledged more than $2 billion to charitable causes, including climate change research.', TRUE, FALSE),
('70f59bac-ab6b-483c-ab01-3041d885d927', 'Stewart Resnick', 'Stewart', 'Resnick', 'United States', 'Agriculture', 'Food & Beverage', 'From almonds & oranges in California''s Central Valley to grapefruits in South Texas, Stewart Resnick and his wife Lynda owe their billions to nature''s bounties.
 They cofounded and continue to co-own the Wonderful Company, among the largest farming operations in America. As a couple, they share a fortune worth an estimated $11.6 billion. Nearly half of all Americans purchase one of their products, including pistachios, almonds, Halos oranges, POM Wonderful and Fiji Water. Stewart bought his first piece of California farmland in 1978 as a hedge against inflation.
 They own a majority stake in the Kern Water Bank, one of the country''s largest underground water storage facilities.', TRUE, FALSE),
('07d84826-800c-4407-89c9-0ba0bcfd4158', 'Ratmir Timashev', 'Ratmir', 'Timashev', 'United States', 'Software', 'Technology', 'Ratmir Timashev is the cofounder and former CEO of Columbus, Ohio-based data management firm Veeam. He and his college friend Andrei Baronov cofounded Veeam in 2006 and sold it to VC firm Insight Partners for $5 billion in 2020. Before Veeam, Timashev and Baronov cofounded systems management tools outfit Aelita Software in 1996; they sold it to Quest Software for $115 million in 2004. In 2026, Timashev launched Oh.io, a VC firm that''s aiming to invest $100 million to bring 100 early-stage startups to Columbus, Ohio over five years. Timashev is a major donor to his alma mater, Ohio State, pledging around $150 million, including a $110 million gift in 2020 to establish the Center for Software Innovation.', TRUE, FALSE),
('81c89511-11ff-43d2-96b8-603479544c40', 'Winifred J. Marquart', 'Winifred', 'Marquart', 'United States', 'Cleaning products', 'Manufacturing', 'Winifred J. Marquart is the president of the Johnson Family Foundation, the main purpose of which is to facilitate meetings and build community.  She is the great-great-granddaughter of SC Johnson (d. 1991), the company''s founder. She is an heir to family-owned SC Johnson, the privately-held cleaning products company whose products include Pledge and Windex. Winifred and her siblings pledged $150 million to Cornell in 2017 to fund the SC Johnson College of Business.', TRUE, FALSE),
('0e0e76a5-4e43-46bb-81ec-a8cbc69fe6f3', 'Joe Mansueto', 'Joe', 'Mansueto', 'United States', 'Investment research', 'Finance & Investments', 'Joe Mansueto started independent investment research firm Morningstar in 1984 with $80,000 in savings. Mansueto stepped down as CEO in 2017 after more than 30 years at the helm. He owns about 36% of the publicly traded firm, which manages or advises on more than $290 billion in assets. In 2018, the Chicagoan paid $255 million for the iconic Wrigley Building and $106 million to buy the Belden-Stratford apartment building. Mansueto bought a 49% stake in the Chicago Fire soccer team in 2018; he bought the rest a year later.', TRUE, FALSE),
('af5387c8-5b7a-4185-aced-20a644bcf61c', 'Märta Schörling Andreen', 'Märta', 'Schörling Andreen', 'Sweden', 'Investments', 'Diversified', 'Marta Schorling Andreen is the daughter of Melker Schorling, the billionaire Swedish investor who died in 2023. Schorling had built up a portfolio of stakes in publicly-traded companies he controlled through the family holding vehicle, Melker Schorling AB. Her sister, Sofia Schorling Hogberg, is also a billionaire. The two sisters are the majority owners of Melker Schorling AB. Today, the family holding company controls large stakes in stock traded companies Hexagon, AAK, Assa Abloy, Hexpol and Securitas.', TRUE, FALSE),
('e30e8197-4af1-4b1b-b038-ab7305767400', 'Tomas Olivo Lopez', 'Tomas', 'Olivo Lopez', 'Spain', 'Shopping centers', 'Real Estate', 'Tomas Olivo Lopez owns nearly all General de Galerias Comerciales, a chain of shopping centers in Spain.  His company has developed six shopping malls in the Andalucia and Catalonia regions of the country. He began buying land outside of Marbella in the 1990s and built his first shopping mall, Parque Comercial La Canada, on that land.', TRUE, FALSE),
('54618482-13f3-4ab9-91af-04f188248096', 'H. Fisk Johnson', 'H.', 'Johnson', 'United States', 'Cleaning products', 'Manufacturing', 'H. Fisk Johnson III is the chairman and CEO of SC Johnson, a privately-held cleaning products company. He is the fifth generation of the Johnson family to lead the company. The company, which has $11.4 billion in estimated revenues, is best known for brands like Windex, Off! and Pledge. Fisk and his three siblings are all shareholders of SC Johnson. Together they own a majority of the company.  Fisk''s late father, Sam Johnson Jr. (d. 2004), ran SC Johnson from 1966 to 2000.', TRUE, FALSE),
('8dd7c419-9ee6-45d1-a0a5-c0cbefd779ca', 'Joao Moreira Salles', 'Joao', 'Moreira Salles', 'Brazil', 'Banking, minerals', 'Diversified', 'Joao Moreira Salles is a Brazilian documentary filmmaker and member of one of Brazil''s oldest banking families. His late father, Walther Moreira Salles, was the founder of Unibanco and a former ambassador to the United States. In 2008 Unibanco merged with Itau, then Brazil''s second-largest commercial bank, creating Itau-Unibanco, the largest bank in Latin America. Moreira Salles and his three brothers, all billionaires, also own stakes in CBMM, the world''s leading supplier of the mineral niobium.', TRUE, FALSE),
('87d2e4f9-68c7-41a0-8585-033db0d29ce8', 'Walther Moreira Salles Junior', 'Walther', 'Moreira Salles Junior', 'Brazil', 'Banking, minerals', 'Finance & Investments', 'Walther Moreira Salles Junior (also known as Walter Salles) is a Brazilian filmmaker and member of one of Brazil''s oldest banking families. His late father, Walther Moreira Salles, was the founder of Unibanco and a former ambassador to the United States.
 In 2008 Unibanco merged with Itau, then Brazil''s second-largest commercial bank, creating Itau-Unibanco, the largest bank in Latin America. Moreira Salles and his three brothers, all billionaires, also own stakes in CBMM, the world''s leading supplier of the mineral niobium.
 Moreira Salles directed more than 20 films, including ''The Motorcycle Diaries'' and 1998 Academy Award nominee ''Central Station.''', TRUE, FALSE),
('a9222a84-c932-4a24-a606-71235f89ef8f', 'Ivan Tavrin', 'Ivan', 'Tavrin', 'Russia', 'Private equity', 'Finance & Investments', 'Ivan Tavrin is the founder of Kismet Capital Group, which has interests in technology and consumer companies in Russia. From 2012 to 2016 Tavrin was CEO of Megafon, a large Russian telecommunication operator owned by fellow billionaire Alisher Usmanov and his partners. He bought one of Russia''s largest internet companies, Avito, from South African conglomerate Naspers for $2.4 billion in 2022, selling 50% to state-owned Rosselkhozbank (or Russian Agricultural Bank) in 2025.  During his university years, Tavrin started an advertising agency selling TV ads and eventually invested in regional TV and radio stations which were later acquired by The Walt Disney Company. He was shareholder in Disney Channel Russia until 2023.', TRUE, FALSE),
('48eb6928-7009-456e-82a0-893c84c8ef3c', 'Euisun Chung', 'Euisun', 'Chung', 'South Korea', 'Hyundai', 'Automotive', 'Euisun Chung was appointed chairman of Hyundai Motor Group in 2020, succeeding his father, Mong-Koo Chung, who retired from the board. Its unit Hyundai Motor India went public in India in 2024, raising $3.3 billion, which was the country''s largest IPO in history. As president of Kia from 2005 to 2009, Chung grew the subsidiary auto brand faster than Hyundai Motor. A bulk of his fortune is derived from auto parts maker Hyundai Glovis. He is the only son of Mong-Koo Chung, who is also a billionaire.', TRUE, FALSE),
('aba52b96-aac6-4c61-ac18-ab3ca49661b5', 'Torbjorn Tornqvist', 'Torbjorn', 'Tornqvist', 'Sweden', 'Oil trading', 'Energy', 'Torbjörn Törnqvist is the Swedish cofounder of Gunvor, a global energy and commodities group. Gunvor has a diverse portfolio that includes refineries, pipelines, terminals, LNG carriers, and biofuel and hydrogen plants. Törnqvist got his start at British Petroleum in 1977, and launched Gunvor in 2000. He bought out his cofounder Gennady Timchenko in 2014, following the Russian invasion of Crimea. Törnqvist owned more than 80% of Gunvor until December 2025, when he sold his stake to a group of employees and stepped back from the company.', TRUE, FALSE),
('e9661182-2db9-422e-8f7e-349e0f46b71c', 'S. Curtis Johnson', 'S.', 'Johnson', 'United States', 'Cleaning products', 'Manufacturing', 'S. Curtis Johnson is a great-great-grandson of Samuel Curtis Johnson, who founded SC Johnson, the family''s cleaning products company, in 1886. In 2014, he was sentenced to four months in jail and fined $6,000 after pleading guilty to misdemeanor sexual assault of his stepdaughter. S. Curtis had been the chairman of family-owned industrial cleaning company Diversey, but stepped down before his arrest in 2011. SC Johnson is known for products including Pledge, Windex and Drano. S. Curtis and his siblings pledged $150 million to Cornell in 2017 to fund the SC Johnson College of Business.', TRUE, FALSE),
('0fba9bee-bb83-480d-9821-5ae73c888b1b', 'Gwendolyn Sontheim Meyer', 'Gwendolyn', 'Meyer', 'United States', 'Cargill', 'Food & Beverage', 'Gwendolyn Sontheim Meyer inherited an estimated 8% stake in food giant Cargill. The heiress spends most of her time on a farm in Rancho Santa Fe, Calif., training horses that compete in show jumping. Her great-grandfather, W.W. Cargill, the son of a Scottish sea captain, founded Cargill in Conover, Iowa in 1865. The family still owns roughly 90% of Cargill, which did $154 billion in 2025 sales across food, agriculture, financial and industrial divisions.', TRUE, FALSE),
('b476b229-1eef-4f04-8328-a54d8a76b0b0', 'Dan Snyder', 'Dan', 'Snyder', 'United States', 'Washington Commanders', 'Sports', 'Dan Snyder initially made his fortune with a marketing business, Snyder Communications, that he started as a college dropout. After taking the company public in 1996, Snyder sold it to French firm Havas for $2.1 billion in stock in 2000. In 1999, he bought the NFL''s Washington Commanders for $750 million, borrowing $350 million to do so. He sold the franchise for $6.05 billion in 2023. After years of controversy over the Native American origins of the team''s former name, the Redskins, Snyder renamed the team the Commanders in 2022. He dropped out of college to start a business chartering planes to fly college kids to sporting events. By 20 he was a millionaire.', TRUE, FALSE),
('1dc02c54-a1db-4479-933d-1652820fd50f', 'Lutz Mario Helmig & family', 'Lutz', 'Helmig', 'Germany', 'Hospitals', 'Healthcare', 'Lutz Mario Helmig, a doctor by training, is well known in Germany for having founded the company that became Helios Hospital Group. In 2005, Helmig sold Helios to competitor Fresenius for $2 billion. His family investment firm, Aton GmbH, is active in four segments: engineering, mining, medical and aviation. Helmig owns 60% of Aton, which is based in Munich. The remaining 40% is held by his wife and two daughters. Aton owns about 75% of EDAG Engineering Group, spun off from Aton in a 2015 IPO.', TRUE, FALSE),
('23f2ece0-09fc-4cf2-a0f9-580200cc0ded', 'George Economou', 'George', 'Economou', 'Greece', 'Shipping', 'Logistics', 'George Economou is a Greek shipping tycoon who owns several privately-held firms under his TMS Group. He took one of those firms, Dryships, public on the Nasdaq in 2005 before ultimately taking it private again in 2019 at a $456 million valuation. In 2018, he sold offshore drilling firm Ocean Rig to publicly traded TransOcean at a $2.7 billion valuation, just 18 months after the firm filed for bankruptcy. Between August and December 2023, Economou bought large positions in several publicly-traded shipping firms in the U.S. Outside of shipping, he owns an estimated $250 million art collection including works by Pablo Picasso. Part of it is on display in his private museum in Athens.', TRUE, FALSE),
('f8b69f80-555f-48af-8082-fa37cacb9ac1', 'Kailashchandra Nuwal', 'Kailashchandra', 'Nuwal', 'India', 'Industrial explosives', 'Manufacturing', 'Kailashchandra Nuwal draws his wealth from shares in Solar Industries, a maker of industrial explosives, founded by his brother Satyanarayana Nuwal.  Solar Industries gets the biggest chunk of its annual revenue from exports, followed by the defense sector, the housing and infrastructure segments, non-coal companies and state-owned coal company. Until 2019 he was vice chairman and a director in the company but had to step down for failing to disclose his stake in a private company. Kailashchandra approached the National Company Law Tribunal for reinstatement. The Supreme Court in 2025 disposed off the appeal.  The fight between the brothers came to a head in 2023 when Kailashchandra Nuwal voted against four resolutions including altering the articles of association at the company''s annual general meeting.', TRUE, FALSE),
('3eb82708-9e15-46d5-81f3-744cf37fe542', 'Fan Hongwei', 'Fan', 'Fan', 'China', 'Petrochemicals', 'Energy', 'Fan Hongwei is the chairman of Hengli Petrochemical, a listed unit of Hengli Group. Her husband Chen Jianhua, also a billionaire, is the chairman of the parent company.  Fan worked as an accountant before establishing a textile and silk trading business with Chen. The couple later acquired a state-owned chemical fiber factory and expanded into petrochemicals. The couple''s son, Chen Hanlun, is the CEO of Shanghai-listed Guangdong Songfa Ceramics, which merged with the group''s shipbuilding unit in 2025. Their daughter, Chen Yiting, once led its tourism arm.', TRUE, FALSE),
('486db199-82f1-4b72-979d-d42fa4c04df4', 'Tsai Eng-meng', 'Tsai', 'Tsai', 'Taiwan', 'Food, beverages', 'Food & Beverage', 'Tsai Eng-meng is the chairman of Want Want China, one of the world''s largest suppliers of Chinese-style snacks and drinks. He also invests in hotels, financial services and media, including China Times newspaper and China Television Co. At age 19, Tsai joined his father''s food business and later came up with an idea for a new product: crackers made from rice flour. He took over the company as president in 1987. Sons Kevin and Matthew, along with nephew Cheng Wen-Hsien, are members of Want Want''s board of directors.', TRUE, FALSE),
('0ca8b65a-1f31-4e25-a846-cf4462ebdab6', 'Marc Stad', 'Marc', 'Stad', 'United States', 'Venture capital', 'Finance & Investments', 'Marc Stad founded Dragoneer Investment Group, a $37 billion (assets under management) venture capital firm focused on technology investments.  Stad began his career in public service as president and commissioner of the City and County of San Francisco Finance Corporation, helping oversee financial assistance to the city and county. He then moved into finance with stints at McKinsey, TPG and the Investment Group of Santa Barbara. He launched Dragoneer in 2012. It has invested in giants in the technology industry, including OpenAI, Anthropic, Spotify and Uber.  Stad and his wife pledged $3 million to the University of California, San Francisco''s UCSF Benioff Children''s Hospitals in 2022 to launch the Stad Center for Pediatric Pain to treat children with acute pain.', TRUE, FALSE),
('41e83c94-017b-49d7-b77e-2e139fa35911', 'Rajiv Bajaj', 'Rajiv', 'Bajaj', 'India', 'Diversified', 'Diversified', 'Rajiv Bajaj is the son of the late Rahul Bajaj, who was chairman emeritus of the storied Bajaj Group until his death in February 2022.
 The group was founded by his great-grandfather Jamnalal Bajaj, who set it up in 1926 and was a follower of Mahatma Gandhi. Today, the Bajaj Group is a conglomerate of 40 companies in sectors such as two-wheelers, financial services and electrical appliances. Rajiv runs two-wheeler flagship Bajaj Auto. In 2025, the family agreed to buy out Germant giant Allianz''s stake In their two insurance joint ventures for $2.8 billion.', TRUE, FALSE),
('09b63513-be9c-4a36-b25f-97c4439d3248', 'Sanjiv Bajaj', 'Sanjiv', 'Bajaj', 'India', 'Diversified', 'Diversified', 'Sanjiv Bajaj is the son of the late Rahul Bajaj, who was chairman emeritus of the storied Bajaj Group until his death in February 2022. The group was founded by their great-grandfather Jamnalal Bajaj, who set it up in 1926 and was a follower of Mahatma Gandhi. Today, the Bajaj Group is a conglomerate of 40 companies in sectors such as two-wheelers, financial services and electrical appliances. Sanjiv oversees the group''s financial services business, which includes insurance. In 2025, the family agreed to buy out Germant giant Allianz''s stake In their two Indian Insurance joint ventures for $2.8 billion.', TRUE, FALSE),
('c934e76f-4f46-4b43-9f70-404eb0766576', 'Marina Budiman', 'Marina', 'Budiman', 'Indonesia', 'Data centers', 'Technology', 'Marina Budiman is cofounder and president commissioner of data center company DCI Indonesia. She set up DCI in 2011 with Otto Toto Sugiri and Han Arming Hanafia. She worked with Sugiri at Bank Bali in 1985 and joined IT company Sigma Cipta Caraka in 1989. She cofounded Indonet, the first internet service provider in Indonesia, in 1994. She and other cofounders sold their stakes in 2023.', TRUE, FALSE),
('39d1b9e9-3d8e-4686-8037-6ceb952cc279', 'Scott Cook', 'Scott', 'Cook', 'United States', 'Software', 'Technology', 'Scott Cook is the cofounder of financial software giant Intuit, known for products like QuickBooks, TurboTax and Mint. The Harvard Business School grad worked for Procter & Gamble and Bain before launching Intuit in 1983. He stepped down as CEO in 1994 and chairman in 1998 but remains a director and has a 2% stake.  Cook and his wife are big supporters of education and have donated millions to universities and are impact investors in several ed-tech funds. Cook was planning to get a Ph.D. in economics but decided to pursue business after successfully turning his defunct college ski club into the biggest in the state.', TRUE, FALSE),
('7be2488b-23b7-41e3-8b44-4e450741682c', 'Willy Michel', 'Willy', 'Michel', 'Switzerland', 'Medical devices', 'Healthcare', 'Willy Michel is the cofounder of Ypsomed Selfcare Solutions, a Swiss pharma company that develops self-injection and diagnostic systems. Ypsomed was started in 2003 out of Disetronic Holding, which Michel founded in 1984 with his brother and sold to Roche for $1.2 billion. As part of the sale agreement, Michel got the injection business back from Roche for $310 million, forming what is known as Ypsomed today. Michel and his three children together own a 71% stake in the company. In 2025, Michel bought Ypsomed''s diabetes business for over $500 million; it''s now a part of TecMed, another medical company he founded.', TRUE, FALSE),
('02c6ac9b-1922-42cf-b7bf-76608fbc60d4', 'Arkady Rotenberg', 'Arkady', 'Rotenberg', 'Russia', 'Construction, pipes, banking', 'Construction & Engineering', 'A friend of President Vladimir Putin, Arkady Rotenberg was once his judo sparring partner.
 In the late 2000s Rotenberg became an owner of SGM Group and Mostotrest, now two of Russia''s biggest construction contractors. Both companies were targeted by EU sanctions in 2018 due to their participation in the construction of the Crimean bridge. Rotenberg was also the target of U.S. and European sanctions in 2014. In 2019 he sold SGM Group to a Gazprom subsidiary and agreed to transfer his shares of Mostotrest to a joint venture with state-owned Vnesheconombank.', TRUE, FALSE),
('b0fcc592-1f55-4523-9025-333c23794465', 'Ian Livingstone', 'Ian', 'Livingstone', 'United Kingdom', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Ian Livingstone, with his billionaire brother Richard, own properties throughout London including high-end shops, swanky hotels and tony apartments. Among their signature projects is Panama Pacifico, a master planned city they''re developing in Panama with Colombian billionaire Jaime Gilinski Bacal. When finished, Panama Pacifico will include 20,000 residential properties, industrial parks and retail and commercial space. Their real estate firm London & Regional operates hotels in L.A., Las Vegas and Miami. The firm is also tapped to revitalize Albert Island, a 25-acre site between London''s Royal Docks and the Thames River, into a mixed-use development.', TRUE, FALSE),
('53539bd6-430d-406c-a0c8-555c8b8ef3de', 'Richard Livingstone', 'Richard', 'Livingstone', 'United Kingdom', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Richard Livingstone, with his billionaire brother Ian, own properties throughout London including high-end shops, swanky hotels and tony apartments. Among their signature projects is Panama Pacifico, a master planned city they''re developing in Panama with Colombian billionaire Jaime Gilinski Bacal. When finished, Panama Pacifico will include 20,000 residential properties, industrial parks and retail and commercial space. Their real estate firm London & Regional operates hotels in L.A., Las Vegas and Miami. The firm is also tapped to revitalize Albert Island, a 25-acre site between London''s Royal Docks and the Thames River, into a mixed-use development.', TRUE, FALSE),
('935f52bb-9c08-433e-a3cf-65fccb094c46', 'Chao Chung-Hsin', 'Chao', 'Chao', 'Taiwan', 'Cooling devices and components', 'Manufacturing', 'Chao Chung-Hsin is the chairman of Jentech Precision Industrial, a supplier of cooling devices and other components for semiconductors. Its products are used in areas such as computers, AI servers and electric vehicles.  A high school dropout, Chung-Hsin acquired industrial molding techniques by working in factories and started his own module business in 1978. He brought in his younger brother Yung-Tsang, now vice chairman, to cofound Jentech in 1987.  In the early stages Chung-Hsin oversaw R&D as well as business operation; Yung-Tsang took charge of finance.', TRUE, FALSE),
('b019dd3b-be80-497a-8ec9-a109456a7ba4', 'Li Min', 'Li', 'Li', 'China', 'Semiconductor', 'Technology', 'Li Min is the chairman of Rockchip Electronics, a supplier of integrated circuits specializing in the intelligent internet of things (IoT) segment. Rockchip''s clients include Intel, Samsung and Google. Li cofounded Rockchip in the southern China city of Fuzhou in 2001. Huang Xu, another cofounder, is also a billionaire.', TRUE, FALSE),
('9e00569c-f8f9-43ae-8df6-01e7f82e516b', 'Liu Yonghao & family', 'Liu', 'Liu', 'China', 'Agribusiness', 'Service', 'Liu Yonghao is the chairman of New Hope Group, which has around 100,000 employees and over 600 subsidiaries around the world. The group has interests in agribusiness, dairy, fast foods, real estate and chemicals. His daughter Liu Chang replaced him as chairman of the group''s animal feed arm New Hope Liuhe, one of China''s largest agribusiness firms, in 2013. In the U.S., New Hope owns stakes in Lansing Trade Group,  a feed and raw materials trading company, and food processing outfit Ruprecht.', TRUE, FALSE),
('5446e9ac-70a6-42e4-b50b-eafcf1547be7', 'Pyotr Aven', 'Pyotr', 'Aven', 'Russia', 'Oil, banking, telecom', 'Finance & Investments', 'Pyotr Aven is a co-owner of Alfa Bank and LetterOne along with Mikhail Fridman, Khan and fellow billionaires Alexei Kuzmichev and Andrei Kosogov. Aven and his partners were all sanctioned by the EU and U.K. in February and March 2022; Aven stepped down from LetterOne''s board in March. He grew up in Moscow, graduated from Moscow State University, and worked at the Institute for Systems Studies at the Soviet Academy of Sciences. In 1989 he went to work at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs; two years later he was tapped to be Putin''s minister of foreign economic relations. Aven was president of Russia''s largest privately held bank, Alfa-Bank, which was hit with sanctions in April 2022, from 1994 to 2011.', TRUE, FALSE),
('7f1edafe-3ae9-4260-b70e-baeb71c2bb32', 'Gail Miller & family', 'Gail', 'Miller', 'United States', 'Car dealerships', 'Automotive', 'Utah-based Gail Miller owns the Larry H. Miller Group, which has interests in real estate, healthcare, finance and entertainment businesses. She and husband Larry (d. 2009) turned a single Toyota dealership into the eighth-largest auto dealer group in America before she sold it to Asbury Automotive in 2021 for $3.2 billion. The Millers purchased the Utah Jazz NBA team in 1986 for $22 million; in 2020 the family agreed to sell it to billionaire Ryan Smith for $1.66 billion. They still own a small stake. In April 2025, Miller''s family spent a reported $600 million to buy a majority stake in Utah''s two professional (and one minor league) soccer teams from billionaire David Blitzer.', TRUE, FALSE),
('bc42e682-79e0-4eba-bc91-36cccf23feff', 'Dagmar Dolby & family', 'Dagmar', 'Dolby', 'United States', 'Dolby Laboratories', 'Technology', 'Dagmar Dolby owns about 36% of publicly-traded audio technology firm Dolby Laboratories, which her husband Ray Dolby (d. 2013) founded in 1965. The company pioneered surround sound technologies used in thousands of films and products, and most recently, in video games and mobile devices. Her two sons share voting power over some assets. David is a board member at Dolby Labs; his brother, Tom, is a novelist and filmmaker. Since 2015, she has committed over $160 million to the University of Cambridge, where Ray Dolby earned a Ph.D. in physics. In September 2018, Dolby donated $20 million to UC San Francisco to establish the Dolby Family Center for Mood Disorders.', TRUE, FALSE),
('91080c1d-9be2-44d0-9e2f-46831dd06004', 'Cho Jyh-jer', 'Cho', 'Cho', 'Taiwan', 'Semiconductors', 'Technology', 'Cho Jyh-jer retired as vice chairman at smartphone chipmaker MediaTek in 2015. He joined the firm as its president in 1997, when it was spun off from his then employer, United Microelectronics. The bulk of his wealth comes from his stake in MediaTek.', TRUE, FALSE),
('5312dd23-cbec-450a-b25f-8fb37686cbd2', 'Jose Joao Abdalla Filho', 'Jose', 'Abdalla Filho', 'Brazil', 'Investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Jose Joao Abdalla Filho is the son of J. J. Abdalla, a Brazilian entrepreneur and politician who built a real estate and textile company.
 In the 1950s, the group his father led became one the largest manufacturers of cement in the country, employing over 40,000 people. Abdalla Filho used the money he inherited to open Banco Classico, which owns stakes in a number of Brazilian companies. 
 His Banco Classico owns 5% of Eletrobras, Brazil''s largest electric utility, and almost 7% of Cemig, an energy giant that owns over 200 companies.', TRUE, FALSE)
