 He is president and founder of the Arcus Foundation, which supports the advancement of LGBTQ human rights and the conservation of great apes. In 2021, Jon and husband Slobodan Randjelovi&#263; gave $15 million to the ACLU Foundation to focus on LGBTQ rights and HIV issues. Stryker has given away more than $850 million in his lifetime. In June 2021 he gave $5.3 million to University of California, Berkeley''s College of Environmental Design.', TRUE, FALSE),
('8e7e21c5-d6dd-43ae-85cd-a30ccd93e61b', 'Ruan Xueping', 'Ruan', 'Ruan', 'Hong Kong', 'Power strip', 'Manufacturing', 'Ruan Xueping is the vice chairman of Shanghai-listed power strip supplier Goneo Group. It''s formerly known as Gongniu Group, which means bull in Chinese. Ruan cofounded Gongniu with his elder brother Ruan Liping, also a billionaire, in 1995. Both brothers hold Hong Kong citizenship.', TRUE, FALSE),
('3442f516-891f-4e4e-b339-aa96244893ae', 'Phil Ruffin', 'Phil', 'Ruffin', 'United States', 'Casinos, real estate', 'Diversified', 'Phil Ruffin owns the Treasure Island Hotel & Casino plus 50% of the Trump International Las Vegas hotel alongside friend Donald Trump. Son of a grocer, Ruffin dropped out of college to sell hamburgers with his buddies, then used the profits to buy convenience stores. From there he expanded into real estate: strip malls, office parks and hotels, including Marriotts in Alabama, California and the Bahamas.  In 1998 he bought the New Frontier Hotel & Casino for $165 million; he sold it for $1.2 billion in 2007 to Israeli billionaire Yitzhak Tshuva. He bought Treasure Island from MGM in 2009, amid the great recession, for $775 million.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6bfa74a5-7eb7-4d46-acc2-b9ef4456b8e0', 'Richard Schulze', 'Richard', 'Schulze', 'United States', 'Best Buy', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Richard Schulze worked as an electronics components manufacturer representative before opening his stereo equipment shop, Sound of Music, in 1966. He grew it into the chain of superstores he renamed Best Buy. He is chairman emeritus of Best Buy and its largest individual shareholder, with a 5% stake. Schulze served as the company''s CEO from 1983 to 2002 and stepped down as chairman in 2012, when a scandal erupted around his hand-picked CEO. Schulze aims to give away $1 billion of his fortune in his lifetime, through his family foundation.', TRUE, FALSE),
('c286d22f-ec58-4998-b86d-db8582797357', 'Marc Lore', 'Marc', 'Lore', 'United States', 'Jet.com', 'Technology', 'Marc Lore is founder and CEO of Wonder, a food tech startup that bills itself as "a new kind of food hall." He founded Wonder in 2018, and it was valued by private investors at more than $7 billion in May 2025.  The Staten Island native studied business and economics at Bucknell, then spent six years in banking before striking out on his own. Lore cofounded Diapers.com parent Quidsi in 2005 and ecommerce firm Jet.com in 2014. Jet.com sold to Walmart for $3.3 billion in 2016. He co-owns the NBA''s Minnesota Timberwolves and WNBA''s Lynx as part of a partnership with retired Yankees star Alex Rodriguez.', TRUE, FALSE),
('b504c3b8-d6f0-409d-aee1-f82923ef185e', 'Scott Kapnick', 'Scott', 'Kapnick', 'United States', 'Private equity', 'Finance & Investments', 'Scott Kapnick is founder and CEO of HPS Investment Partners, one of the world''s biggest alternative credit managers with $149 billion in assets.  He spent 21 years at Goldman Sachs, rising to become co-head of investment banking and co-CEO of Goldman Sachs International.  He left Goldman in 2007 to join hedge fund Highbridge Capital after its sale to JPMorgan, eventually building up its credit arm HPS.  Kapnick was CEO of Highbridge from 2013 until 2016, when he and the principals bought HPS from JPMorgan in a carveout. Assets have since swelled.  He sold HPS to BlackRock in July 2025 for around $12 billion in BlackRock stock.', TRUE, FALSE),
('a9e55cb8-75cd-485d-b990-4144e76cccd7', 'God Nisanov', 'God', 'Nisanov', 'Russia', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'God Nisanov and his partner Zarakh Iliev, who came to Moscow from Azerbaijan, own roughly 14 million of square feet of real estate in Moscow. The partners developed a 225-acre wholesale distribution center, Food City, in Moscow and also several shopping centers on Moscow''s outskirts.
 In 2022 a real estate mogul Nisanov was hit with U.S. and U.K. sanctions in the wake of Russia''s invasion of Ukraine.', TRUE, FALSE),
('84bf14cd-a3b3-472f-a505-f32a6bab93d9', 'Zarakh Iliev', 'Zarakh', 'Iliev', 'Russia', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Zarakh Iliev and his longtime partner God Nisanov are building trade centers, hotels and residential property in Moscow. The pair, who moved to Moscow from Azerbaijan, own roughly 14 million of square feet of real estate in Moscow. The partners developed a 225-acre wholesale distribution center, Food City, in Moscow and also several shopping centers on Moscow''s outskirts. Ililev is co-owner of 5- star Moscow Royal Radisson hotel, which served as FIFA''s headquarters during the World Cup 2018 in Russia. <br> In September 2022 a real estate mogul Iliev was hit with U.K. sanctions in the wake of Russia''s invasion of Ukraine.', TRUE, FALSE),
('fce5404c-2e97-45c1-80fc-3f7c32ed2ea4', 'Steven Udvar-Hazy', 'Steven', 'Udvar-Hazy', 'United States', 'Aircraft leasing', 'Service', 'Steven Udvar-Hazy, who immigrated to New York from Hungary as a child, is credited with creating the airplane leasing industry. He started his own airline in his 20s, but realized there was easier money to be made in buying planes and leasing them to airlines. Udvar-Hazy''s first airplane leasing firm, International Lease Finance Corp., was sold to AIG in 1990 for $1.3 billion. Thirty six years later, he sold his second airplane leasing company, publicly traded Air Lease Corp., in a $7.4 billion deal. The Smithsonian''s National Air and Space Museum named its sister location in Virginia for him after a $60 million donation in 2000.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d25f19d3-dcfe-4131-962f-6b95141f07c0', 'Larry Gies', 'Larry', 'Gies', 'United States', 'private equity', 'Finance & Investments', 'Larry Gies is the founder and CEO of Chicago-based Madison Industries, a private equity firm he has built through dozens of acquisitions and rollups across the industrial sector. Gies was born in Mendota, Illinois, to a father who worked at a manufacturing company and a Dutch mother who was orphaned during World War II.  Gies started his career as an accountant at Touche Ross (now Deloitte) before working under investor Michael Heisley, where he learned how to acquire and run underperforming companies. He started PE firm Madison Capital Partners in 1994 by maxing out ten credit cards and taking a $50,000 loan from a high school friend while his wife worked three jobs. He has invested in everything from air filtration systems to medical simulation companies, and is chairman of HVAC company Madison Air, which went public in 2026 in the largest industrial IPO in decades.', TRUE, FALSE),
('655d6200-a34c-41f6-930f-bf5e9175bbe4', 'John A. Sobrato & family', 'John', 'Sobrato', 'United States', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Real estate mogul John A. Sobrato began selling homes in Palo Alto while he was still a student at Santa Clara University. He later worked with his mother to develop industrial properties, and founded his own real estate company in 1979. The Sobrato Organization owns over 7.5 million square feet of office space with tenants like Netflix, plus 30 apartments buildings. Sobrato is chairman emeritus of his Cupertino-based firm, while his son, John M. Sobrato, serves as chairman of the board. In 2017, he pledged $100 million to Santa Clara University, his alma mater, for a new STEM education center.', TRUE, FALSE),
('f2a86a21-5aa1-4303-9c60-5bc1d50c1a38', 'Thomas Hagen & family', 'Thomas', 'Hagen', 'United States', 'Insurance', 'Finance & Investments', 'Thomas Hagen is chairman emeritus of Erie Indemnity and has been a part of the company for more than 50 years, including three years as CEO from 1990 to 1993. The publicly-traded insurance company was cofounded by his late wife Susan''s father, H. O. Hirt, and his friend, O. G. Crawford. Susan Hagen, who was Erie''s longest serving director, died in 2015 at age 79. Now one of the nation''s largest property and casualty insurance companies, the firm began with a business plan scribbled in a 10-cent notebook in 1925.  In 2017, Hagen gifted $1.5 million to Mercyhurst University''s history department, which subsequently took his name.', TRUE, FALSE),
('a735a861-b41d-4a3d-86fe-e533689735d3', 'Danielle Bellon & family', 'Danielle', 'Bellon', 'France', 'Food services', 'Service', 'Danielle Bellon is the widow of Pierre Bellon, who founded food service and catering company Sodexo in 1966. 
 Pierre Bellon, who expanded Sodexo to 56 countries, died in 2022 at age 92. Danielle and Pierre''s daughter Sophie served as CEO of the Paris-listed business for four years until late 2025.	 Their son, François-Xavier Bellon, is chairman of family holding company Bellon S.A. Their daughter, Nathalie Bellon-Szabo, heads events hospitality arm Sodexo Live!', TRUE, FALSE),
('da12f460-9c3d-4b16-b093-f37a670cceb8', 'Nikolai Buinov', 'Nikolai', 'Buinov', 'Russia', 'Oil, gas', 'Energy', 'Nikolay Buinov is the main shareholder of Irkutsk oil company, the largest independent private oil company in Russia. Buinov got his start with a timber company in the early 1990s. In 1995, Buinov and his father founded Bodaibo energy company, which supplied fuel and lubricants to gold miners in the north of Irkutsk in Siberia. Buinov purchased the license for an oil field in 1997, which was the start of what would become Irkutsk Oil Company. Buinov sold a stake in IOC to the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD) in 2008; EBRD later sold part of its stake to Goldman Sachs.', TRUE, FALSE),
('9c532bcb-00c5-484a-9067-634774fe1a5e', 'Jamshyd Godrej', 'Jamshyd', 'Godrej', 'India', 'Consumer goods, real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Jamshyd Godrej is chairman of the Godrej Enterprises Group, a conglomerate in Mumbai, which he controls with his sister, Smita Crishna-Godrej, also a billionaire. The flagship of the Godrej Enterprises Group is privately held consumer goods giant Godrej & Boyce, which makes everything from locks to refrigerators. His niece Nyrika Holkar is an executive director.at Godrej &amp; Boyce and tipped to succeed him. His son Navroze and niece Freyan Crishna Bieri have board seats at Godrej & Boyce.', TRUE, FALSE),
('1c38d84f-0777-498c-b129-52fdf74fd350', 'Smita Crishna Godrej', 'Smita', 'Crishna Godrej', 'India', 'Consumer goods', 'Diversified', 'Smita Crishna-Godrej hails from the storied Godrej clan and controls the Godrej Enterprises Group, along with her brother Jamshyd Godrej. In 2024, the siblings and their cousins Adi and Nadir Godrej divided the family''s business empire into two separate business groups.  The flagship of the Godrej Enterprises Group is privately held consumer goods giant Godrej &amp; Boyce, which makes everything from locks to refrigerators. Their biggest asset is a 3,400-acre land parcel in suburban Mumbai. While Jamshyd Godrej is chairperson of the newly carved group, her daughter Nyrika Holkar is tipped to succeed him.', TRUE, FALSE),
('98a4fa1a-6b6a-4afa-b8d2-aad259878655', 'David MacNeil', 'David', 'MacNeil', 'United States', 'Automobile accessories', 'Manufacturing', 'David MacNeil founded the automotive accessories company WeatherTech in 1989. WeatherTech, which manufactures all of its products in the United States, generated $800 million in revenues in 2025. Known for its car floor mats, WeatherTech has expanded into home goods in recent years. In January 2026, President Trump nominated MacNeil to the Federal Trade Commission. His confirmation is pending. MacNeil owns a vintage car collection worth over $400 million. It includes one of the most expensive cars in the world: a 1963 Ferrari 250 GTO, which he bought in 2018 for an estimated $75 million.', TRUE, FALSE),
('0a932513-4682-4336-bc89-77b77db9b016', 'Todd Christopher', 'Todd', 'Christopher', 'United States', 'Hair care products', 'Fashion & Retail', 'A high school dropout, Todd Christopher founded hair care products company Vogue International in 1987. Christopher sold a stake to the Carlyle Group in 2014. Two years later, they sold the company to Johnson & Johnson for $3.3 billion. Before the sale, Vogue International borrowed several hundred million dollars and made a $400 million distribution to Christopher. Vogue International owns hair care brands like OGX and Maui Moisture. Christopher has trademarked phrases including Vitamin &amp; Herbal Indulgence, Hair Prescriptions, Beach Bum Gear, Ego Trip and Shampurity.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6ed76f2d-ec63-4a31-a537-53635696b835', 'Shen Guojun', 'Shen', 'Shen', 'China', 'Retail', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Shen Guojun is the founder and chairman of Yintai Group, whose interests cover retail, real estate and investment. Yintai''s department store chain Intime was taken private from the Hong Kong Stock Exchange by Shen and Alibaba in 2017, in a deal that valued it at $2.6 billion. Shen worked in a state-run bank before he started his own business. The tycoon has divested sizable stakes in gold, property and other businesses amid China''s slower growth. In 2024, Alibaba sold its 99% stake in Intime to a consortium led by China''s textile heavyweight Youngor Group for $1 billion, registering $1.3 billion loss.', TRUE, FALSE),
('a7f9a9d6-c025-4bb3-94a3-231e80b38ce2', 'Cho Tak Wong', 'Cho', 'Cho', 'Hong Kong', 'Auto parts', 'Manufacturing', 'Cho Tak Wong is the founder of Fuyao Glass Industry Group, one of Asia''s largest manufacturers of auto glass that counts Audi, Fiat and Ford among its customers. He stepped down as chairman in 2025, citing reasons including the need to sustainably develop the company''s governance structure.  His son, Tso Fai, is the new chairman. Cho is also known for his philanthropic causes. His Heren Charitable Foundation pledged in 2021 $1.6 billion to build the Fuyao University of Science and Technology in China. The university welcomed its first batch of students in late 2025.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6282c5ec-f5f5-4f6e-b791-5acddc9ed756', 'Tomasz Biernacki', 'Tomasz', 'Biernacki', 'Poland', 'Supermarkets', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Tomasz Biernacki is the founder and chairman of Poland''s largest grocery chain, Dino Polska. Biernacki opened his first shop in 1999; today the company has nearly 1,000 stores that also produce their own meat products. Biernacki took Dino Polska public in 2017.', TRUE, FALSE),
('a6e9aaf7-a609-4a16-8bbf-39970496adae', 'Thomas Straumann', 'Thomas', 'Straumann', 'Switzerland', 'Dental implants', 'Healthcare', 'Thomas Straumann owns a 17% stake in the world''s largest manufacturer of dental implants, publicly held Straumann Holding. Straumann''s grandfather Reinhard founded the company in 1954 as an alloy research company that developed implants to treat bone fractures. Straumann''s father Fritz met real success during the 1970s with the introduction of titanium dental implants. Straumann joined the company''s board of directors in 1990 and shifted the firm''s focus to dental products only. Straumann chairs Medartis, a publicly traded medical device outfit that he founded in 1997.', TRUE, FALSE),
('19267740-3560-470a-80e4-68b7aa0ce594', 'Ruan Liping', 'Ruan', 'Ruan', 'Hong Kong', 'Power strips', 'Manufacturing', 'Ruan Liping is the chairman of power strip supplier Goneo Group, which went public on the Shanghai Stock Exchange in 2020. Previously known as Gongniu Group, the company changed its English name to Goneo in 2023.  Ruan, a basketball fan, named the firm in honor of NBA Chicago Bulls former star Michael Jordan - with Gongniu translating to "bulls." He cofounded Gongniu in 1995 with his younger brother Ruan Xueping, who is the company''s vice chairman and also a billionaire. Ruan started his career as an engineer in a local mechanical factory. He quit his job about a decade later to launch Gongniu.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6a003946-e3c0-4468-8faf-0f89bd350c11', 'Remon Vos', 'Remon', 'Vos', 'Netherlands', 'Logistics real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Remon Vos is the cofounder and CEO of Prague-based CTP, a publicly traded logistics and industrial real estate firm in central and eastern Europe. CTP is the second-largest developer and owner of industrial real estate in Europe, with properties in 10 countries. Vos cofounded the firm in 1998 with Johan Brakema and Eddy Maas (d. 2017). They built their first industrial park in Humpolec, Czech Republic in 2002. Brakema sold his stake in 2002 and Vos bought Maas'' family''s shares in 2019. He took CTP public on the Amsterdam stock exchange in 2021 and owns 73%. Vos first moved to the Czech Republic from his native Netherlands in 1994 in his early 20s, selling Dutch products to the local market.', TRUE, FALSE),
('57fd33f8-e478-48d7-a9c4-36f9b9a48546', 'Weili Dai', 'Weili', 'Dai', 'United States', 'Semiconductors', 'Technology', 'Weili Dai cofounded semiconductor company Marvell Technology with her husband, Sehat Sutardja, in 1995.  Dai was president of the company until she and Sutardja were forced out in 2016 amid an internal accounting investigation.  No evidence of fraud was found in the Marvell accounting investigation.  The couple moved to Las Vegas in 2017 and have been investing in real estate and technology; Sutarjda died in 2024.  Dai cofounded five other companies including AI startup MeetKai in 2018, and semiconductor packaging company Silicon Box in 2021.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6bba9b01-1f5f-4f4b-a9f0-19eb34883829', 'Ben Chestnut', 'Ben', 'Chestnut', 'United States', 'Email marketing', 'Technology', 'Ben Chestnut founded what later became Mailchimp with Dan Kurzius in 2001 as a side project to their web design company. Mailchimp''s email marketing software for small businesses garnered enough customers that in 2007 they committed to it full time. Wary of giving up control to outside investors, Chestnut and Kurzius bootstrapped growth from profits and took no outside money. In 2021, Intuit announced it would acquire Mailchimp in a $12 billion cash and stock acquisition. At the time of announcement, Chestnut and Kurzius each owned 50% of the Atlanta-based company, which had $800 million in 2020 revenue.', TRUE, FALSE),
('57b0e2f8-9950-4c86-9d58-3747d4a2adc6', 'Ling Tang', 'Ling', 'Tang', 'Canada', 'advertising technology', 'Technology', 'Ling Tang is a pre-IPO investor in AI-powered advertising technology company AppLovin, which went public on the Nasdaq in 2021. Tang owns 5% of AppLovin through an entity called Angel Pride Holdings Ltd.
 Tang is one of eight billionaires from AppLovin, including the company''s cofounder and CEO Adam Foroughi. Little is known about Ling Tang, though securities filings list a business address for her on the same street in Hong Kong as another mysterious billionaire AppLovin investor, Hao Tang.', TRUE, FALSE),
('c617fc5e-a45a-445b-845e-502d928ee4ef', 'B. Partha Saradhi Reddy', 'B.', 'Reddy', 'India', 'Pharmaceuticals', 'Healthcare', 'B.Partha Saradhi Reddy is chairman of  Hetero Group, which he founded in 1993. Hetero produces a range of anti-retroviral drugs for a host of diseases including AIDS. It has a portfolio of more than 200 products across therapies ranging from cancer to immunology to diabetes. Hetero makes branded and non-branded generic medicines. He is a member of the Rajya Sabha, upper house of the Indian Parliament.', TRUE, FALSE),
('f421716e-55a6-4299-852d-eade8dc6997e', 'Byron Trott', 'Byron', 'Trott', 'United States', 'Investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Byron D. Trott is chairman and co-CEO of merchant bank BDT & MSD Partners.  Trott merged his company BDT & Co. with Michael Dell''s family investment firm MSD Partners in 2023.  He started BDT in 2009 after nearly 30 years at Goldman Sachs, where he began as stockbroker and eventually rose to become vice chairman of investment banking.  Trott''s closely held BDT has provided advice and capital to family and founder-led companies including ones owned by such billionaires as Dennis Washington and Shahid Khan.  Trott serves on the board of trustees at his alma mater, the University of Chicago.', TRUE, FALSE),
('86474d1d-b5e3-4e71-8188-453401a08197', 'Chao Yung-Tsang', 'Chao', 'Chao', 'Taiwan', 'Cooling devices and components', 'Manufacturing', 'Chao Yung-Tsang is vice chairman of Jentech Precision Industrial, a supplier of cooling devices and components. Its products are used in areas such as computers, AI servers, electric vehicles and semiconductors. He cofounded Jentech in 1987 with older brother Chung-Hsin, now chairman of the company.  In the early stages Chung-Hsin oversaw R&D as well as business operation; Yung-Tsang took charge of finance.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d30f04a9-4269-42e6-8f17-43bf144e7f69', 'Nicolas D''Ieteren', 'Nicolas', 'D''Ieteren', 'Belgium', 'Auto parts, distribution', 'Automotive', 'Nicolas D''Ieteren chairs the Belgium-based D''Ieteren Group.  The Group''s portfolio includes five businesses ranging from automobile distribution to real estate and glass repair.  The Group owns D''Ieteren Auto, which exclusively distributes Volkswagen, Audi, Lamborghini, Bugatti and Porsche in Belgium. The business has been in the family for six generations; it was founded in 1805 by Jean-Joseph D''Ieteren.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6f859887-0d6f-424a-9fee-a63fa36a3700', 'Anthony Pritzker', 'Anthony', 'Pritzker', 'United States', 'Hotels, investments', 'Service', 'Anthony Pritzker runs The Pritzker Group, a private family investment firm; his brother J.B. was involved until he became governor of Illinois in January 2019. The Pritzker Group owns and runs industrial firms, particularly in the packaging sector.  Tony is one of 13 billionaire heirs to the Chicago-based Pritzker family fortune, which includes Hyatt Hotels. He spent 20 years running middle-market manufacturing and distribution companies, including firms within the Pritzker family''s Marmon conglomerate. He also runs Pritzker Private Capital, which has raised $7.9 billion from family and outside investors since spinning out from Pritzker Group in 2017.', TRUE, FALSE),
('5f1d3012-d493-4086-b9e8-d76dec844863', 'Anthony von Mandl', 'Anthony', 'von Mandl', 'Canada', 'Alcoholic beverages', 'Food & Beverage', 'Anthony von Mandl created the ready-to-drink alcoholic beverages White Claw Hard Seltzer and Mike''s Hard Lemonade through his Mark Anthony Brands. Forbes estimates von Mandl''s U.S. business generated around $3.6 billion in revenue in 2025, based on analyst estimates.  He began his career in the Canadian wine business as an importer in the 1970s at age 22. He currently owns six wineries in Canada, including Mission Hill Winery in British Columbia''s Okanagan Valley.', TRUE, FALSE),
('b8e7656d-2609-4309-9f0e-afab78e6ea84', 'Zhu Baoguo & family', 'Zhu', 'Zhu', 'China', 'Pharmaceuticals', 'Healthcare', 'Zhu Baoguo was the chairman of Shenzhen-based Joincare Pharmaceutical Group Industry. He stepped down in September 2026, citing the reach of retirement age. 

 The mogul handed over the reins to the company''s CEO Lin Nanqi, who now assumes both roles.  Zhu has built a pharma empire with businesses in prescription drugs and traditional Chinese medicine, after his first product - an herbal tonic for women - became a nationwide bestseller after its launch in the 1990s.  Prior to his pharmaceutical venture, Zhu was a chemical engineer with a bachelor''s degree in chemistry from the Henan Normal University.  Zhu also owns a stake in WeBank, a Chinese digital bank backed by Tencent.', TRUE, FALSE),
('3a489319-3729-4e43-a7f5-6f4b2e6b307c', 'Arturo Moreno', 'Arturo', 'Moreno', 'United States', 'Billboards, Los Angeles Angels', 'Sports', 'Arturo Moreno agreed to sell the Los Angeles Angels, which he bought in 2003 for $184 million, to Stan Kroenke in September 2026 for $4 billion. Moreno''s initial fortune came from billboard advertising company Outdoor Systems, which he sold to Infinity Broadcasting in 1999 for $8.3 billion. He has stakes in other billboard advertising companies, as well as commercial real estate holdings throughout Phoenix. Moreno''s $325 million plan to develop a new Angels baseball stadium was scuttled in 2022, by Anaheim''s City Council.', TRUE, FALSE),
('4ced1530-b3ef-4f74-ae23-3763572e63ee', 'Gopikishan Damani', 'Gopikishan', 'Damani', 'India', 'Retail, investments', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Gopikishan Damani is the younger brother of billionaire Radhakishan Damani, now considered India''s retailing king. They control listed retailing giant Avenue Supermart, which owns D-Mart, a supermarket chain selling everything from grocery to apparel to footwear. Damani, together with his billionaire brother Radhakishan, reportedly bought a house in south Mumbai in 2021 for more than $100 million. In early 2023, he and his brother reportedly paid $155 million for 28 apartments in a luxury tower in mid-town Mumbai developed by fellow billionaire Vikas Oberoi. In June 2024, he and his older brother sold their holding in India Cements to billionaire Kumar Birla.', TRUE, FALSE),
('50c643aa-f1e2-43ca-aadf-7e7ef08ff130', 'Daniel D''Aniello', 'Daniel', 'D''Aniello', 'United States', 'Private equity', 'Finance & Investments', 'Daniel D''Aniello is one of three billionaire founders of private equity firm Carlyle Group. He stepped down as chairman in 2018 and now serves as chairman emeritus of Carlyle, which has $453 billion in assets under management.   D''Aniello worked at Trans World Airlines, Pepsi and Marriott before joining William Conway Jr. and David Rubenstein to start Carlyle in 1987. He attended Syracuse University on a scholarship, studying transportation economics, and later got his MBA at Harvard. A Vietnam War veteran, D''Aniello contributed $20 million to Syracuse University''s National Veterans Resource Center in 2018.', TRUE, FALSE),
('208edf10-4366-49bd-b99d-d02f4cd630d6', 'Lai Meisong', 'Lai', 'Lai', 'China', 'Package delivery', 'Logistics', 'Lai Meisong is the founder, chairman and CEO of ZTO Express, one of China''s largest express delivery firms by parcel volume. Lai worked in the timber business before setting up ZTO in 2002. The company went public on the New York Stock Exchange in 2016 and became dually listed in Hong Kong in 2020. Chinese tech giant Alibaba and its logistics arm Cainiao hold minority stakes in ZTO.', TRUE, FALSE),
('7cb7c6af-3a80-419f-b7ac-0a4c551ff349', 'Don Vultaggio & family', 'Don', 'Vultaggio', 'United States', 'Beverages', 'Food & Beverage', 'Arizona Beverages cofounder Don Vultaggio has built his fortune one 99-cent tallboy can of iced tea at a time. He got his start in the 1970s selling beer and soda from the back of an old van in Brooklyn''s toughest neighborhoods, where others refused to go. In 1992 he went into iced tea, launching Arizona from a Brooklyn warehouse and quickly toppling the competition with taller cans and flashier labels. Arizona sells some $4 billion worth of tea, juice, water and alcoholic drinks annually, including its popular green tea and Arnold Palmer lines. In 2015 he was ordered to buy out his former friend and partner, John Ferolito, for about $1 billion to settle a lengthy, bitter shareholder dispute.', TRUE, FALSE),
('e5548f64-8b0d-41b4-be40-d56c5401e5fe', 'Igor Altushkin', 'Igor', 'Altushkin', 'Russia', 'Metals', 'Metals & Mining', 'Igor Altushkin is the founder and largest shareholder of the Russian Copper Company (RCC), Russia''s third-largest copper producer. He started his career as a scrap metal trader in the early 1990s. Altushkin, who has six children, is a key supporter of the Russian Orthodox Church. In May 2017, Altushkin was awarded the Order of Friendship by Vladimir Putin. In 2020 RCC built its new headquarters in Ekaterinburg, designed by the British architect Norman Foster.', TRUE, FALSE),
('18adfc71-c1ec-41e0-ae62-ac734459114d', 'Wu Yajun', 'Wu', 'Wu', 'China', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Wu Yajun draws the bulk of her wealth from a stake in Hong Kong-listed real estate developer Longfor Group Holdings. She stepped down as chairman in 2022. She and her ex-husband Cai Kui, who cofounded Longfor with her in 1993, divorced in 2012. He no longer has a role in the company. Wu, who holds a degree in engineering, worked as a journalist before entering the real estate business.', TRUE, FALSE),
('547b4ff1-90a8-4bd1-b57e-adc2035881f4', 'John Middleton', 'John', 'Middleton', 'United States', 'Tobacco', 'Food & Beverage', 'John Middleton made his fortune selling his family''s storied tobacco business to Philip Morris'' parent, Altria, in 2007 for $2.9 billion in cash. The original business, John Middleton Inc., was founded as a small retail tobacco shop in Philadelphia in 1856 by his great-great-grandfather. The company began manufacturing cigarettes in the 1950s and launched the Black & Mild cigar brand in 1980. Middleton bought out his relatives'' stakes in the company in 2003 for about $200 million amid tobacco lawsuits that threatened to harm the business. Middleton has a nearly 50% stake in the Philadelphia Phillies baseball team.', TRUE, FALSE),
('cb0a6f75-3b3d-4f17-afad-9c2ab76ab9ca', 'Fernand Huts', 'Fernand', 'Huts', 'Belgium', 'Logistics, transportation', 'Logistics', 'Fernand Huts controls Katoen Natie, an Antwerp-based logistics business with more than 350 companies worldwide that employs 20,000 People. Huts, who collects archeological textiles, is also involved in politics and was elected to the Belgian parliament in 1995. Over time, Huts bought out 19 partners to assume control of the company.  In 2005, Huts grouped all its activities under Luxembourg-based KN Holding.', TRUE, FALSE),
('a83cef43-f456-4bdd-b758-353f159357a1', 'Li Chunan', 'Li', 'Li', 'China', 'Solar wafers and modules', 'Manufacturing', 'Li Chunan is a cofounder of Longi Green Energy Technology, one of China''s largest manufacturers of solar wafers and modules. The company''s two other cofounders, Li Zhenguo and Zhong Baoshen, are college friends with Chunan from undergraduate days at Lanzhou University.  Li is also the chairman of Linton Technologies, a maker of semiconductor and solar equipment based in the northeastern city of Dalian.', TRUE, FALSE),
('b4b4b5e7-a7e4-41f3-aec8-edbe4388222c', 'Abhay Firodia', 'Abhay', 'Firodia', 'India', 'Automobiles', 'Automotive', 'Abhay Firodia is chairman of Force Motors, maker of vans, pickup trucks, SUVs and tractors and privately held auto parts firm Jaya Hind Industries, which accounted for bulk of his wealth. Force Motors, previously known as Bajaj Tempo when it was a joint venture with the Bajaj clan, is run by his son Prasan since 2009. It was founded by his late father, Navalmal Firodia, in 1958, who fell out with the Bajaj family in 1968 after a bitter feud. Jaya Hind Industries, which has a joint venture with French auto parts firm Montupet, makes aluminium castings for the auto sector.', TRUE, FALSE),
('4f4df80d-e966-4654-897f-7b646bb1a79d', 'Beatriz Davila de Santo Domingo', 'Beatriz', 'Davila de Santo Domingo', 'Colombia', 'Beer', 'Food & Beverage', 'Beatriz Davila de Santo Domingo is the widow of Colombian beer baron Julio Mario Santo Domingo, who died in 2011. She controls more than a third of the Santo Domingo family''s Luxembourg-based holding company, through which she owns shares in Anheuser-Busch InBev. Her two sons Alejandro and Andres Santo Domingo own the next-largest stakes; Alejandro took over the family business after Julio Mario''s death. The family also owns a stake in Château Pétrus, a French wine estate near Bordeaux that produces some of the world''s most expensive wines. The family''s public holdings also include stakes in Keurig Dr. Pepper and Kraft Heinz, as well as closely-held companies in Colombia, including movie theaters, supermarkets and gas distribution.', TRUE, FALSE),
('83cf3d70-2012-4969-944b-b3318ebf2a26', 'Robert Johnson & family', 'Robert', 'Johnson', 'United States', 'Johnson & Johnson, New York Jets', 'Sports', 'Robert "Woody" Johnson''s great-grandfather, Robert Wood Johnson, founded health products giant Johnson & Johnson with two of his brothers in 1886, providing the world with dental floss and first-aid kits. His grandfather, Robert Wood Johnson II (nicknamed The General), left the bulk of the family wealth to the Robert Wood Johnson Foundation. The rest went to Woody, his siblings and other family members. Woody spent four years as Donald Trump''s ambassador to the UK, returning in 2021 to help manage the family assets, which include stock in their namesake company and the New York Jets. He and his family purchased the Jets in 2000 for $635 million, then the third-highest price ever paid for a professional sports team. Now the Jets are estimated to be worth nearly $10 billion. A 2017 government ethics disclosure indicated that Johnson has assets of at least $1.7 billion outside of the Jets.', TRUE, FALSE),
('8fc4f3f9-6dbd-4521-a22b-b52d1cbcee5d', 'Andrei Bokarev', 'Andrei', 'Bokarev', 'Russia', 'Metals, mining', 'Manufacturing', 'Until 2022 Andrei Bokarev runs Transmashholding (TMH), Russia''s biggest producer of rolling stock for railways and subway systems. Bokarev previously headed Krutrade AG, which ran the export operations of the Kuzbassrazrezugol coal company. Bokarev is a partner in most of his senior partner Iskander Makhmudov''s projects including TMH, Kuzbassrazrezugol and Ural Mining Metallurgical Company (UMMC).

 He owns half of Ust-Luga Oil company, largest oil terminal in Europe with capacity of 30 million tons per year.', TRUE, FALSE),
('7f87595b-ac5f-4a44-890f-03067e394541', 'Martin Ebner', 'Martin', 'Ebner', 'Switzerland', 'Investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Martin Ebner founded Swiss bank BZ Bank in 1985, then started his own investment firm, BZ Group, in 1988. He has quietly rebuilt a huge fortune after his indebted BZ Group lost most of its value in 2002. Today he owns multimillion-dollar stakes in various companies through his investment vehicle, Patinex. His biggest holdings include healthcare company Vifor Pharma, software firm Temenos and real estate investor Intershop. A lawyer by training, Ebner has a PhD in business from the University of Florida.', TRUE, FALSE),
('43ec0fc9-059e-45d5-9586-3f6b6624083c', 'Robin Li', 'Robin', 'Li', 'China', 'Internet search', 'Technology', 'Robin Li is the cofounder, chairman and CEO of search engine operator Baidu, which is dual-listed on the Nasdaq and in Hong Kong. The company counts online advertising as its bread-and-butter business. It is also expanding aggressively in AI.  Baidu in 2023 rolled out a chatbot rival to ChatGPT called Ernie. It also operates driverless robotaxi services in mainland China, and secured trial permits for such services in places including Dubai, Hong Kong and London. The company''s semiconductor design unit, Kunlunxin, counts customers that include Chinese telecom giant China Mobile.', TRUE, FALSE),
('82ce1f50-3108-4b3f-a945-dc2fe019bacd', 'Igor Kesaev', 'Igor', 'Kesaev', 'Russia', 'Tobacco distribution, retail', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Megapolis, the company established by retail magnate Igor Kesaev and his partner Sergei Katsiev, controls 70% of Russia''s cigarette market. Philip Morris and Japan Tobacco International bought 40% of Megapolis for $1.5 billion in 2013 in one of the biggest deals in the Russian consumer market. In 2019, he merged his Dixy supermarket chain with a chain of alcohol stores Krasnoe &amp; Beloe to create one of the largest retailers in Russia. He founded Mercury, which began as a food and alcohol importer, in 1991. Kesaev was sanctioned by EU and U.K. in April 2022', TRUE, FALSE),
('83a02a5a-ec11-47c8-9349-e3c4fc51a319', 'Sanjit Biswas', 'Sanjit', 'Biswas', 'United States', 'Sensor systems', 'Technology', 'In 2015, Sanjit Biswas and John Bicket cofounded Samsara, a platform that uses AI-powered tools to help companies, such as transportation and construction businesses, increase efficiency and improve safety.  Biswas serves as CEO of Samsara, which is based in San Francisco; the company listed its shares on the New York Stock Exchange in 2021. Samsara operates in North America, Europe and the Asia-Pacific region; it has more than 20,000 customers. Biswas and Bicket met at MIT as graduate students. Before Samsara, the pair cofounded the cloud networking company Meraki, which they sold to Cisco in 2012 for $1.2 billion.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d7d8456d-60fb-4b55-a7f4-575f37f1a2fa', 'Chip Wilson', 'Chip', 'Wilson', 'Canada', 'Lululemon', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Dennis "Chip" Wilson is the founder and former CEO of Lululemon, which he started with a single store in Vancouver in 2000. He took the athleisure company public in 2007 but resigned as chairman in 2013 and removed himself from the business completely in 2015. Although Wilson has no management role at Lululemon, he remains its biggest individual shareholder with a 7% stake. Wilson, his wife and five sons now operate a holding company called Hold It All, which invests in apparel, real estate and private equity. He has stakes in Chinese activewear company Anta Sports and Amer Sports, which owns brands like Salomon, Arc''teryx and Wilson.', TRUE, FALSE),
('1f184bb0-90ce-4808-bb72-b8da2a22a6f2', 'Rodger Riney & family', 'Rodger', 'Riney', 'United States', 'Discount brokerage', 'Finance & Investments', 'Rodger Riney is the cofounder of discount brokerage firm Scottrade, which is now part of Charles Schwab. After college, Riney turned down a job at a top engineering firm and joined a Missouri investment company for less pay. A decade later, he quit his job, drove 1,500 miles from St. Louis to Scottsdale, Ariz. and cofounded Scottrade in 1980. Riney, who bought out his partner in 1985, expanded the firm to 3 million client accounts with a total of $170 billion in assets under management. He sold out to Joe Ricketts'' TD Ameritrade for $4 billion in 2017, 2 years after he was diagnosed with blood cancer multiple myeloma.', TRUE, FALSE),
('dfefd7e3-e465-4124-9c76-ed1604ce2757', 'Miao Hangen', 'Miao', 'Miao', 'China', 'Textiles, petrochemicals', 'Diversified', 'Miao Hangen is the chairman of Eastern Shenghong, a Shenzhen-listed petrochemical and new material firm. Its parent Shenghong Group, which also has interests in textile and new energy, was founded in 1992. After failing China''s notoriously difficult college entrance examination, the mogul went to work for a state-owned textile factory in the southeastern city of Suzhou.  Miao was soon promoted to the head of that factory, and he grew it bigger through a series of mergers and acquisitions. The billionaire later ventured on his own, before expanding into petrochemicals.  Shenghong broke ground on a $4.2 billion plant for energy storage systems in Zhangjiagang, Jiangsu in 2023, slated to be completed in 2026.', TRUE, FALSE),
('836a1281-225a-4ba5-a9c3-b9554296ddb6', 'August Troendle', 'August', 'Troendle', 'United States', 'Pharmaceutical services', 'Healthcare', 'August Troendle is the CEO of Medpace, a clinical research company he founded in Cincinnati, Ohio in 1992; he owns nearly 19% of the stock.  Medpace conducts clinical trials for pharmaceutical companies seeking to bring drugs, vaccines or medical devices to market. Before starting Medpace, Troendle spent five years as a director at Swiss pharma company Sandoz, now known as Novartis. He also briefly worked as a medical review officer at the FDA''s division of metabolic and endocrine drug products from 1986 to 1987. A doctor with an M.D. from the University of Maryland, Troendle has also served on the boards of several public and private healthcare companies.', TRUE, FALSE),
('2f454f22-1c6a-408b-81fd-5f8c33d2153b', 'Austen Cargill II', 'Austen', 'Cargill', 'United States', 'Cargill', 'Food & Beverage', 'Austen Cargill II is one of 21 billionaire heirs to Cargill, the family business where he served as a vice president until retiring in 2001. His great-grandfather, W.W. Cargill, founded the business as a single grain warehouse on the end of an Iowa railroad line in 1865. The family still owns roughly 90% of Cargill, which did $154 billion in 2025 sales across food, agriculture, financial and industrial divisions. Before becoming a Cargill executive, Austen earned a Ph.D. and worked as a marine biologist for the company.', TRUE, FALSE),
('507c4065-2748-431a-ad5f-8f3c788f0d0c', 'James Cargill II', 'James', 'Cargill', 'United States', 'Cargill', 'Food & Beverage', 'James Cargill is one of 21 billionaire heirs to Cargill, America''s largest private company. His great-grandfather, W.W. Cargill, founded the business as a single grain warehouse on the end of an Iowa railroad line in 1865. The family still owns roughly 90% of Cargill, which did $154 billion in 2025 sales across food, agriculture, financial and industrial divisions. The Cargill-MacMillan family collects an estimated 18% of net profits as dividends every year.', TRUE, FALSE),
('e81fb49c-f8bb-47de-83f2-bf9618ad346c', 'Marianne Liebmann', 'Marianne', 'Liebmann', 'United States', 'Cargill', 'Food & Beverage', 'Marianne Liebmann is one of 21 billionaire heirs to Cargill, America''s largest private company. Her great-grandfather, W.W. Cargill, founded the business as a single grain warehouse on the end of an Iowa railroad line in 1865. The family still owns roughly 90% of Cargill, which did $154 billion in 2025 sales across food, agriculture, financial and industrial divisions. The Cargill-MacMillan family collects an estimated 18% of net profits as dividends every year.', TRUE, FALSE),
('7ff45d7a-2309-4c49-afd0-91219eeff2fc', 'Drayton McLane Jr', 'Drayton', 'McLane', 'United States', 'Walmart, logistics', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Drayton McLane turned his family''s grocery distribution company, McLane Co., into an international firm and sold it to Walmart. McLane became president and CEO of McLane Co. and ran it for almost 30 years, averaging yearly sales growth of 30%. In 1991, he sold McLane Co. to his friend Sam Walton for $50 million and 10.4 million shares of Walmart. In 2003, Walmart sold the company to Warren Buffett''s Berkshire Hathaway for $1.45 billion. Shortly after 1991, he founded McLane Company, a holding company with a wide array of investments, including a stake in the Houston Astros.', TRUE, FALSE),
('1b1d720d-da4d-4055-97bc-3639038ec021', 'Donald Sterling', 'Donald', 'Sterling', 'United States', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Donald Sterling, born Donald Tokowitz to Jewish immigrants, built a fortune largely by buying down-at-the-heels apartment buildings in Los Angeles. Sterling owned the Los Angeles Clippers for 33 years; his wife Shelly sold in 2014 after a tape of his racist remarks to his then-mistress surfaced. The Chicago-born billionaire bought the Clippers in 1981 for $12.5 million when the team was based in San Diego. It was sold for $2 billion. Besides a swath of apartments in L.A.''s Westside and Koreatown, he also owns the Beverly Hills Plaza Hotel. Before he purchased his first West Hollywood property, Sterling was a successful trial lawyer.', TRUE, FALSE),
('e7162f45-e97e-4a31-9be6-03677ecdbca4', 'James Chambers', 'James', 'Chambers', 'United States', 'Media, automotive', 'Media & Entertainment', 'James Cox Chambers inherited an estimated 17% stake in communications, media and automotive conglomerate Cox Enterprises from his mother Anne Cox Chambers. His grandfather, James M. Cox, founded what became Cox Enterprises in 1898. Both his sisters, Katharine Rayner and Margaretta Taylor, also inherited an estimated 17% stake each in Cox Enterprises. Neither James nor his sisters or mother have ever had an active role in the company. His cousin, Jim Kennedy, is chairman emeritus of Cox Enterprises. His nephew, Alex Taylor, is CEO and chairman.', TRUE, FALSE),
('cf11ad4f-e2da-426d-9b72-e4bb95b2ef17', 'Katharine Rayner', 'Katharine', 'Rayner', 'United States', 'Media, automotive', 'Media & Entertainment', 'Katharine Rayner  inherited an estimated 17% stake in media and automotive conglomerate Cox Enterprises from her mother, Anne Cox Chambers. Cox Enterprises, a private communications, media, and automotive conglomerate started by Rayner''s grandfather, has $23.1 billion in revenues.  Her siblings, James Chambers and Margaretta Taylor, also inherited an estimated 17% stake each in Cox Enterprises. Neither Rayner nor her siblings or mother have ever had an active role in the company. Her cousin, Jim Kennedy, is chairman emeritus of Cox Enterprises. Her nephew, Alex Taylor, is CEO and chairman.', TRUE, FALSE),
('c228efe4-7281-4f27-a1e1-7932732cbd68', 'Margaretta Taylor', 'Margaretta', 'Taylor', 'United States', 'Media, automotive', 'Media & Entertainment', 'Margaretta Taylor inherited an estimated 17% stake in communications, media and automotive conglomerate Cox Enterprises from her mother, Anne Cox Chambers. Her grandfather, James M. Cox, founded what has become Cox Enterprises in 1898. Her siblings, James Chambers and Katherine Rayner, also inherited an estimated 17% stake each in Cox Enterprises. Margaretta''s son, Alex Taylor, is CEO and chairman of Cox Enterprises, a $23.1 billion (in revenue) media and automotive company.  Her cousin, Jim Kennedy, is chairman emeritus of Cox Enterprises.', TRUE, FALSE),
('73708a56-3633-4dc1-bfcd-c0d1fae6c232', 'C. Dean Metropoulos', 'C.', 'Metropoulos', 'United States', 'Investments', 'Food & Beverage', 'C. Dean Metropoulos is best known for saving the iconic Twinkies and Hostess Brands. Through his Metropoulos & Co, he''s also turned around and sold Chef Boyardee, Pabst Blue Ribbon, Bumble Bee Tuna and others. Metropoulos and private equity firm Apollo bought Hostess Brands in 2013 and later took it public.  Ten years later, J.M. Smucker Co. acquired Hostess Brands for $5.6 billion.  The Greek-born entrepreneur made his first American acquisition at the age of 32, when he acquired a cheese company in his wife''s native Vermont.', TRUE, FALSE),
('3e7caa04-bb8b-4d0d-af5c-962c9b06d31d', 'Lorinc Meszaros', 'Lorinc', 'Meszaros', 'Hungary', 'Diversified', 'Diversified', 'L&#337;rinc Meszáros is a close friend of Viktor Orbán, Hungary''s former Prime Minister, and also the richest and most famous oligarch in the country. He founded a small gas-fitting company in Felcsút, Orbán''s home village, in 1990. In the 2000s the two men became acquainted through football. Meszaros'' gas-fitting company, Meszaros & Meszaros, is now a big player in the construction market thanks to government contracts. Orbán lost power in 2026.', TRUE, FALSE),
('ba82c63f-372e-40d1-a241-16a32ca562f9', 'Daniel Och', 'Daniel', 'Och', 'United States', 'Hedge funds', 'Finance & Investments', 'Dan Och founded Och-Ziff Capital Management, now a publicly traded hedge fund firm, in 1994. Och stepped down as chairman in 2019 after years of client withdrawals and no longer has a role with the hedge fund. The firm changed its name to Sculptor Capital Management in August 2019, further cutting its ties with its founder. Och now runs his family office, Willoughby Capital, a growth equity investor with a portfolio that includes Robinhood, Coinbase and Instacart. Och has given more than $500 million to his charitable foundation, and has contributed to Undue Medical Debt, a non-profit eliminating medical debt for low-income individuals', TRUE, FALSE),
('d85db4e6-1cc9-4c2d-aafa-f55c4d102f21', 'Catherine Commisso & family', 'Catherine', 'Commisso & family', 'United States', 'Telecom', 'Telecom', 'Catherine Commisso is the owner of Mediacom, a New York-based cable company founded by her husband Rocco Commisso. He died in January 2026 at age 76. Rocco Commisso founded Mediacom to focus on smaller, underserved communities, and grew it into America''s fifth-largest cable TV provider. 
 Catherine is also the owner of  Italian Serie A soccer team Fiorentina.', TRUE, FALSE),
('187d99c1-f7cd-47f4-b9be-558f40666c50', 'Hansjoerg Wyss', 'Hansjoerg', 'Wyss', 'Switzerland', 'Medical devices', 'Healthcare', 'Hansjoerg Wyss'' fortune stems from his 2012 sale of medical device manufacturer Synthes, which he founded, to Johnson & Johnson for $20.2 billion. He now holds stakes in publicly traded biotech company NovoCure and the Chelsea Football Club in the U.K.  One of the most philanthropic people in the world, Wyss also has charitable foundations with assets of over $2 billion. He is a signatory of the Giving Pledge by Bill Gates and Warren Buffett, which asks billionaires to commit to donating at least half of their fortunes to charity. In 2022, he pledged $350 million to the Wyss Institute for Biologically Inspired Engineering at Harvard, where he had already made pledges totaling $381 million since 2009.  In 2018, Wyss'' foundation pledged $1 billion for conservation efforts over a decade. It upped its pledge to $1.5 billion in 2021. The nonprofit has disbursed or committed more than $1 billion of that total to date.', TRUE, FALSE),
('362e1efb-3861-406c-8d74-64888c1a73ab', 'Michael Saylor', 'Michael', 'Saylor', 'United States', 'Cryptocurrency', 'Technology', 'Michael Saylor founded business analytics software firm Strategy (formerly MicroStrategy) and ran it as CEO until 2022, when he moved into the chairman''s role. One of the best-known executives of the Internet bubble, Saylor was a multibillionaire in the late 1990s thanks to his stake in Strategy. He fell from the billionaire ranks after questionable accounting led to a restatement of financial results and the dotcom bust crashed the stock. He''s a billionaire again thanks to timely bitcoin investments. In 2020, he disclosed he personally bought 17,732 bitcoins for $175 million. He has steered Strategy''s corporate coffers into bitcoin, spending billions to accumulate more than 800,000 bitcoins.', TRUE, FALSE),
('57ec7770-eab8-4a6b-81c3-d0a172ce7efc', 'Jiang Rensheng & family', 'Jiang', 'Jiang', 'China', 'Vaccines', 'Healthcare', 'Jiang Rensheng is the chairman of Shenzhen-listed vaccine firm Chongqing Zhifei Biological Products. A longtime distribution partner of Merck, Zhifei won the Chinese sales rights to the U.S. pharma''s HPV drug in 2018. In 2023, Jiang took his antibody drug maker Chongqing Genrix Biopharmaceutical public on the Shanghai Stock Exchange. Prior to striking out on his own, he worked as a primary school teacher and a government health official.  In 2024, Zhifei entered an exclusive partnership with British pharmaceutical giant GSK for the distribution of shingles vaccines and commercialization of Respiratory syncytial virus (RSV) vaccines in China.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d003f27e-29da-4300-b10c-9bf36ab196ee', 'Henning Oldendorff', 'Henning', 'Oldendorff', 'Germany', 'Shipping', 'Logistics', 'Henning Oldendorff is the controlling shareholder and chairman of German shipping company Oldendorff Carriers.  He assumed leadership in 1980 at the age of 23 following the 80th birthday of his father, Egon Oldendorff, who founded the company in 1921. Strategic growth under his direction transformed the company from a traditional shipowner into a global operator managing a fleet of approximately 750 - 800 vessels.  Absolute control is maintained through a 100% shareholding in the family''s holding structures.  Market dominance is driven by a counter-cyclical investment strategy, which involves selling assets during market peaks to fund large-scale fleet renewals during downturns.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6b9243f0-6488-458a-8953-b067bf408441', 'Herbert Wertheim', 'Herbert', 'Wertheim', 'United States', 'Investments', 'Finance & Investments', 'Herbert "Herbie" Wertheim is an optometrist and inventor who built a fortune over five decades of investing in stocks. Wertheim, who is dyslexic and struggled in school, joined the U.S. Navy at age 17 after facing truancy charges. He founded and still runs Brain Power Inc., a manufacturer of optical tints for eyeglasses; it holds more than 100 patents and copyrights.
 Since 1970, he has invested his profits from Brain Power into the stock market and is the largest individual shareholder in aerospace firm Heico.', TRUE, FALSE),
('8af69231-aefa-4ab5-b0e1-1d32f57349d2', 'Nithin Kamath', 'Nithin', 'Kamath', 'India', 'Financial services', 'Finance & Investments', 'Nithin Kamath cofounded discount brokerage Zerodha in 2010 with his brother Nikhil Kamath. It went on to disrupt the brokerage market in India. The Bangalore-based Zerodha, has more than seven million clients, making it one of the largest brokerage firms in the country. Their venture capital fund and incubator, called Rainmatter, invests in fintech companies and ventures that promote financial inclusion. Their investment management firm True Beacon is aimed at ultra-high net worth investors and operates on a zero-fee model. Zerodha''s business took a hit when the stock exchange''s  regulator tightened rules in November 2024 for futures and options traders, who are its main customers.', TRUE, FALSE),
('d7d691b8-495d-4e50-a5c5-cab6fb74e8a1', 'Mark Shoen', 'Mark', 'Shoen', 'United States', 'U-Haul', 'Automotive', 'Mark Shoen owns roughly one-fifth of the publicly traded parent company of U-Haul. Shoen''s parents, L.S. and Anna Mary Shoen, cofounded the truck-and trailer-rental company in 1945. He sided with his brother Joe in a nasty family feud in which Joe wrested control of U-Haul away from their father. Shoen is also majority owner of one of the largest private self-storage operations in the U.S., which does business with U-Haul. He keeps a low profile but apparently remains on good terms with Joe, who still runs U-Haul.', TRUE, FALSE),
('98ec06e5-3204-4646-b151-a8b68729d550', 'Vikas Oberoi', 'Vikas', 'Oberoi', 'India', 'Real estate', 'Real Estate', 'Property magnate Vikas Oberoi controls and runs Mumbai-listed Oberoi Realty, known for its high-end suburban condos. Oberoi owns a Westin hotel in suburban Mumbai and is building the city''s first Ritz-Carlton hotel and residences. Oberoi, who is not related to the family behind the Oberoi hotel chain, is also building a mall, hotel and office tower in midtown Mumbai. The company has leased 1.5 million square feet in its suburban office tower in Mumbai to Morgan Stanley.', TRUE, FALSE),
('218cc69d-983f-48f3-bab5-bcb39613d6de', 'Eleanor Butt Crook & family', 'Eleanor', 'Crook', 'United States', 'Supermarkets', 'Fashion & Retail', 'Eleanor Butt Crook is an heir to the H-E-B grocery fortune. The San Antonio-based chain has 455 stores in Texas and Mexico and generates $50 billion in revenues. Crook''s grandmother, Florence Butt, founded the company in 1905 after her husband was diagnosed with tuberculosis and was unable to work.  Crook has no role in day-to-day operations but serves on the board of directors. Her brother, Charles Butt, who is chairman of H-E-B, is also a billionaire.', TRUE, FALSE),
('e8c296ab-9b2b-4610-a8c6-6af722775cb9', 'Hsieh Wen-Ta', 'Hsieh', 'Hsieh', 'Taiwan', 'Semiconductor testing equipment', 'Manufacturing', 'Hsieh Wen-Ta is the chairman of Hon. Precision, a maker of testing equipment for advanced chips. The company takes up a third of the market for IC test handlers, which sort and move integrated circuits during final testing. It supplies global semiconductor heavyweights such as TSMC and Nvidia. Hsieh set up Hon. Precision''s predecessor in 1999. He took the company public on the Taiwan Stock Exchange in November 2025.', TRUE, FALSE),
('73492501-dba7-402f-83da-9cea34d16f14', 'Hu Baifan', 'Hu', 'Hu', 'China', 'Pharmaceuticals', 'Healthcare', 'Hu Baifan is the chairman of Shenzhen-listed Zhejiang NHU, one of the world''s largest producers of vitamins A and E. After graduation from college in 1982, Hu spent six years teaching chemistry at a remote vocational school in China. With money borrowed from his fellow teachers, Hu in 1988 started a small factory to make industrial ethanol. That factory later expanded into ingredients for vitamins.  His younger brother, Hu Baishan, is the company''s vice chairman and president.', TRUE, FALSE),
('07bd7ce9-cb45-4217-8465-6a4171c3d716', 'Egor Kulkov', 'Egor', 'Kulkov', 'Russia', 'Pharmaceuticals', 'Healthcare', 'Egor Kulkov created Pharmstandard together with Viktor Kharitonin, Roman Abramovich and others by combining five factories bought from ICN Pharmaceuticals in 2003.
 Kulkov and Kharitonin bought out their partners in 2008. Kulkov still has a stake in, and sits on the board of, Pharmstandard, now Russia''s  leading pharmaceutical firm. The partners also have stakes in Russian pharma firms OTCPharm, Biocad and Generium, one of the makers of the Sputnik V covid vaccine. Kulkov is also a shareholder of British medical technology firm CMR Surgical, which makes the surgical robotic system Versius.', TRUE, FALSE),
('6c235e69-166d-4341-93f0-94e5e0b6748d', 'Stewart Rahr', 'Stewart', 'Rahr', 'United States', 'Drug distribution', 'Healthcare', 'Stewart Rahr expanded Kinray, a pharmaceutical distributor his father founded in 1944, and sold it to Cardinal Health in 2010 for $1.3 billion. Rahr is known for his extravagant lifestyle, which he funds through conservative investments in private equity, hedge funds and natural resources. After getting a bachelor''s degree in history at NYU, he briefly attended NYU Law before dropping out to run the family business. He has a sizable art collection that includes works by Picasso, Damien Hirst, Jeff Koons and Alexander Calder. He has donated over $25 million to Make-A-Wish, a nation-wide nonprofit that grants the wishes of critically ill children.', TRUE, FALSE),
('5dd64960-3bb2-4162-bda1-69d8275de6d2', 'Miguel Fluxa Rossello', 'Miguel', 'Fluxa Rossello', 'Spain', 'Hotels', 'Service', 'Miguel Fluxá Rosselló is the executive chairman of Grupo Iberostar, one of Europe''s largest hotel companies. He joined the family business, originally a footwear company founded by his grandfather, in 1962 and launched the Iberostar hotel brand in 1986. The company now has 100 hotels and over 40,000 employees across the world. In 2006 he sold the group''s tour operator and travel agency divisions to the Carlyle Group for $950 million. His eldest daughter Sabina runs the company as CEO while his other daughter Gloria is the chief sustainability officer.', TRUE, FALSE),
('78556831-0a35-4438-9081-5b0a5438a827', 'Martin Haefner', 'Martin', 'Haefner', 'Switzerland', 'Software, investments', 'Technology', 'Martin Haefner''s fortune largely stems from his former stake in IT management software maker CA Technologies, acquired by Broadcom in July 2018. He inherited half of his father Walter''s stake in CA Technologies when he died in June 2012, then the world''s oldest billionaire at 101. He also inherited part of car dealer AMAG, which sells brands including Volkswagen, Audi, Bentley and Porsche. His sister, Eva Maria Bucher-Haefner, inherited equal stakes in CA Technologies and AMAG. He bought her stake in AMAG in 2018. Martin co-owns the Bellerive Hotel in Lausanne, Switzerland, with his sister.', TRUE, FALSE),
('467c661d-8ffe-4cde-9d95-877cdc6b52b4', 'Sid Bass', 'Sid', 'Bass', 'United States', 'Oil, investments', 'Energy', 'Sid Bass inherited several million dollars from his oil tycoon great-uncle Sid Richardson in 1959. He''s been diversifying ever since. Bass has nurtured the careers of famed investors like Richard Rainwater. He personally negotiated the $6 billion sale of Bass oilfields in 2017 with then ExxonMobil CEO Rex Tillerson. He rescued ice cream maker Blue Bell with an investment after a 2015 listeria outbreak.', TRUE, FALSE),
('a6c029fc-fb48-49b3-9f67-a35ec07b13be', 'Garrett Camp', 'Garrett', 'Camp', 'Canada', 'Uber', 'Technology', 'Uber chairman Garrett Camp cofounded the ride-hailing startup with Travis Kalanick in 2009. The Uber mobile phone app lets users request a ride and a driver-contractor is routed to pick them up -- with Uber getting a cut of the fare. Camp owns about 4% of Uber, which listed its shares on the New York Stock Exchange on May 10, 2019. Before Uber, Garrett Camp founded web discovery tool StumbleUpon, which he sold to eBay in 2007 for $75 million. He has backed close to a hundred startups through his incubator Expa Studios.', TRUE, FALSE),
('b57b1126-549d-4184-bf7b-734c66e0db0c', 'Baba Kalyani', 'Baba', 'Kalyani', 'India', 'Engineering', 'Automotive', 'MIT engineer Baba Kalyani''s Bharat Forge, which his son Amit helps him run, was founded by his father in 1966. Bharat Forge, best known for making auto parts, also manufactures components for sectors such as aerospace and oil and gas. Bharat Forge is the flagship of the more-than-$3 billion (revenue) Kalyani Group. Kalyani has a collaboration with Israel Aerospace Industries to make air defense systems. The group has spun off its electric mobility unit into a separate subsidiary, Kalyani Powertrain, to focus on developing that business.', TRUE, FALSE),
('34ffca30-9960-4ab6-92cb-59766fd99764', 'Olivier Pomel', 'Olivier', 'Pomel', 'France', 'Cloud computing', 'Technology', 'Olivier Pomel is the CEO of Datadog, a cloud monitoring company he cofounded with Alexis Le-Quoc, the firm''s chief technology officer, in 2010. Datadog went public on the Nasdaq in 2019 and Pomel and Lê-Quôc became billionaires in 2020, after a blockbuster earnings release sent shares soaring.  Pomel and Lê-Quôc each own more than 2% of Datadog''s common stock.   The French natives met while undergraduates at Ecole Centrale Paris, where both received Master''s degrees in computer science. Before building Datadog, the duo worked together at New York-based firm Wireless Generation, which was acquired by News Corp in 2010.', TRUE, FALSE),
('40d7afc5-1c5b-4989-a6e9-30ea06288816', 'Sergio Stevanato & family', 'Sergio', 'Stevanato', 'Italy', 'Medical packaging', 'Healthcare', 'Sergio Stevanato is chairman emeritus of the Stevanato Group, a medical packaging firm based in Piombino Dese, Italy. Founded by his father Giovanni in 1949, the company is now run by his sons Franco and Marco, who serve as chairman and vice chairman, respectively. Stevanato Group went public on the New York Stock Exchange in 2021. Stevanato Group is the second largest maker of glass vials in the world and a major supplier of vials for several Covid-19 vaccine manufacturers. The company started out making glass bottles for wine and perfume and is now one of the world''s largest producers of insulin pen cartridges.', TRUE, FALSE),
('bb7e7da9-0c1a-4f66-a1cb-07d901c05914', 'Huang Li', 'Huang', 'Huang', 'China', 'Imaging systems', 'Technology', 'Huang Li is the chairman of Guide Infrared, a supplier of infrared imaging systems. Huang founded Guide in 1999 and was the main developer of its proprietary infrared thermal imaging technology. It went public in 2010 on the Shenzhen Stock Exchange. His son Huang Sheng is the company''s director and deputy general manager.', TRUE, FALSE),
('3db5b26c-18f5-458b-b058-b9f8e32dde6c', 'Michael Jordan', 'Michael', 'Jordan', 'United States', 'Charlotte Hornets, endorsements', 'Sports', 'Regarded by many as the NBA''s greatest player of all-time, Michael Jordan won six titles with the Chicago Bulls. His salary during his career totaled $90 million, but he has earned ten figures corporate partnerships with the likes of Nike, Hanes and Gatorade. MJ joined sports-betting firm DraftKings as a special advisor to the board and an investor in September 2020. He also became a NASCAR team co-owner in 2020. Jordan sold his majority ownership of the Charlotte Hornets NBA team in 2023 but reportedly retained a minority stake in the franchise.', TRUE, FALSE)
